07e90a16aa987b0c7f51c2068092c398b224535" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-1208" :question/id #uuid "23e8510c-99c3-539c-9c30-63245db2572b" :question/math-academy-id "q-1208" :question/problem "Which statement is **not** true?" :question/worked-solution "If $A⊆B,$ then $A$ is a subset of $B,$ meaning that every element of $A$ is an element of $B.$\n\nAmong the given choices, only $C⊆Z$ is not true. This statement is not true because not every complex is an integer number. For example, we have $2\\text{i}\\in C$ but $2\\text{i}\\notin Z.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-1208/ma-source-field/82f763aaa0e8334dedf0f46da0f551bc4c351b6a39578c71cf8f37ab01f78ef4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b7f1d12-3335-5dd7-bf36-e07077d0c45d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-1208"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-12498/ma-source-field/3b9490ae87d70da6938a240e4b4e35e7e2929308cca7d0df0193aa405ff12bb6/8851ab7556ff0cfb5d1e16dd5a6129b45e02030c5fa6218acad90fad2a892da1" :answer/id #uuid "c00a40ba-01e3-5ee1-8e78-5ca100de2c2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}\\sqrt{(5x+1)^{3}}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12498/ma-source-field/3b9490ae87d70da6938a240e4b4e35e7e2929308cca7d0df0193aa405ff12bb6/adada5060d3e1080df33d9eb02d8afd45975c004a0160acc07d2e95bc9e69111" :answer/id #uuid "957bc594-a52d-54c5-8fe2-348b94cdf190" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}\\sqrt{5x+1}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12498/ma-source-field/3b9490ae87d70da6938a240e4b4e35e7e2929308cca7d0df0193aa405ff12bb6/d209e698c776e7654a61925fb4e7dbbf34a65043a0a666048b5852cbf3ab6be6" :answer/id #uuid "40a36a09-4403-51a9-8c9b-14cdbfe2aa41" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{15}\\sqrt{(5x+1)^{3}}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12498/ma-source-field/3b9490ae87d70da6938a240e4b4e35e7e2929308cca7d0df0193aa405ff12bb6/f364c5a6b917aad2468a1076e23f116803b4ea51e48b1c12f00d04a43641cdb1" :answer/id #uuid "2458c64b-d709-5fd5-a6bf-7d12e7bb36e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{(5x+1)^{3}}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12498/ma-source-field/3b9490ae87d70da6938a240e4b4e35e7e2929308cca7d0df0193aa405ff12bb6/8ea4a9c87c6ee3ba2eabe7eb1a39cd63223bb25b2a1b696924fc3b941d00d1a7" :answer/id #uuid "b95804dd-01ed-5465-b1ec-454869fcea4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{5x+1}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12498/ma-source-field/3b9490ae87d70da6938a240e4b4e35e7e2929308cca7d0df0193aa405ff12bb6" :answer-field/id #uuid "0bf9bf65-124a-5233-aedc-81c57617266f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-12498/ma-source-field/3b9490ae87d70da6938a240e4b4e35e7e2929308cca7d0df0193aa405ff12bb6/8851ab7556ff0cfb5d1e16dd5a6129b45e02030c5fa6218acad90fad2a892da1" "q-12498/ma-source-field/3b9490ae87d70da6938a240e4b4e35e7e2929308cca7d0df0193aa405ff12bb6/adada5060d3e1080df33d9eb02d8afd45975c004a0160acc07d2e95bc9e69111" "q-12498/ma-source-field/3b9490ae87d70da6938a240e4b4e35e7e2929308cca7d0df0193aa405ff12bb6/d209e698c776e7654a61925fb4e7dbbf34a65043a0a666048b5852cbf3ab6be6" "q-12498/ma-source-field/3b9490ae87d70da6938a240e4b4e35e7e2929308cca7d0df0193aa405ff12bb6/f364c5a6b917aad2468a1076e23f116803b4ea51e48b1c12f00d04a43641cdb1" "q-12498/ma-source-field/3b9490ae87d70da6938a240e4b4e35e7e2929308cca7d0df0193aa405ff12bb6/8ea4a9c87c6ee3ba2eabe7eb1a39cd63223bb25b2a1b696924fc3b941d00d1a7"] :answer-field/correct "q-12498/ma-source-field/3b9490ae87d70da6938a240e4b4e35e7e2929308cca7d0df0193aa405ff12bb6/d209e698c776e7654a61925fb4e7dbbf34a65043a0a666048b5852cbf3ab6be6" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-12498" :question/id #uuid "457b9ae0-36a8-577c-85ad-8057dc66fc9a" :question/math-academy-id "q-12498" :question/problem "$\\int \\sqrt{5x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int (5x+1)^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, we let $u=5x+1.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=5\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $u$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (5x+1)^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {u}^{1/2}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{5})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\int {u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3/2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{15}{u}^{3/2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{15}(5x+1)^{3/2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{15}\\sqrt{(5x+1)^{3}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\frac{2}{15}\\sqrt{(5x+1)^{3}}+C] & =\\frac{2}{15}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\sqrt{(5x+1)^{3}}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{15}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[(5x+1)^{3/2}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{15}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}(5x+1)^{1/2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5x+1)+0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(5x+1)^{1/2}\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =(5x+1)^{1/2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5x+1}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-12498/ma-source-field/3b9490ae87d70da6938a240e4b4e35e7e2929308cca7d0df0193aa405ff12bb6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0ae5760b-9277-596c-8546-dca4fd985bd7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-12498"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-1270/ma-source-field/af446cbcf13db178150e47aaa82382f0275bc885784a2525db6b4a8c24996c71/dc724ecf32f891f3814e0f814161d3351bf7308384acc6d1289eacea9a1e9427" :answer/id #uuid "059cf625-a3dd-5a3d-8a2c-3d1bdcfed336" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{{2,4,6},{8},{10}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-1270/ma-source-field/af446cbcf13db178150e47aaa82382f0275bc885784a2525db6b4a8c24996c71/6246c5522ea416783794c2757592af9b966961d5f4b346b069f407609be26cd1" :answer/id #uuid "e79a6322-44b7-5a94-b196-9b746019ff59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{{2},{2,4},{6,8,10}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-1270/ma-source-field/af446cbcf13db178150e47aaa82382f0275bc885784a2525db6b4a8c24996c71/3d2fc72edeebdb9198c70b8a618c7bf4f47910bccbdcb997a07f2e67b3efbe7e" :answer/id #uuid "0c62bfae-23aa-5f52-b0bc-0424b9578342" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{{2},{4},{6,8}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-1270/ma-source-field/af446cbcf13db178150e47aaa82382f0275bc885784a2525db6b4a8c24996c71/c4b0c92a297d41acfbe05c02b3c7d38deb0794cb9ee0698ec16ce942ec17ef77" :answer/id #uuid "d3365228-8ebc-5740-8fa8-73b9ae0a6b14" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{∅,{2,4},{6,8},{10}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-1270/ma-source-field/af446cbcf13db178150e47aaa82382f0275bc885784a2525db6b4a8c24996c71/da999332997df1cd96f8f412dc7284b57be5fef9fcc0c2c7c012feb1968c2da7" :answer/id #uuid "1db91ae0-8216-5bd3-82ee-556d650a4b32" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{∅,{2,4},{6,8},{8,10}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-1270/ma-source-field/af446cbcf13db178150e47aaa82382f0275bc885784a2525db6b4a8c24996c71" :answer-field/id #uuid "2bbea4c4-defc-5b74-9d20-54587edce7a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-1270/ma-source-field/af446cbcf13db178150e47aaa82382f0275bc885784a2525db6b4a8c24996c71/dc724ecf32f891f3814e0f814161d3351bf7308384acc6d1289eacea9a1e9427" "q-1270/ma-source-field/af446cbcf13db178150e47aaa82382f0275bc885784a2525db6b4a8c24996c71/6246c5522ea416783794c2757592af9b966961d5f4b346b069f407609be26cd1" "q-1270/ma-source-field/af446cbcf13db178150e47aaa82382f0275bc885784a2525db6b4a8c24996c71/3d2fc72edeebdb9198c70b8a618c7bf4f47910bccbdcb997a07f2e67b3efbe7e" "q-1270/ma-source-field/af446cbcf13db178150e47aaa82382f0275bc885784a2525db6b4a8c24996c71/c4b0c92a297d41acfbe05c02b3c7d38deb0794cb9ee0698ec16ce942ec17ef77" "q-1270/ma-source-field/af446cbcf13db178150e47aaa82382f0275bc885784a2525db6b4a8c24996c71/da999332997df1cd96f8f412dc7284b57be5fef9fcc0c2c7c012feb1968c2da7"] :answer-field/correct "q-1270/ma-source-field/af446cbcf13db178150e47aaa82382f0275bc885784a2525db6b4a8c24996c71/dc724ecf32f891f3814e0f814161d3351bf7308384acc6d1289eacea9a1e9427" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-1270" :question/id #uuid "6fe130ed-ce3d-5283-a70b-402fc6b51c7c" :question/math-academy-id "q-1270" :question/problem "If $T={2,4,6,8,10}$, which collection of subsets of $T$ is a partition of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "A partition of a set $T$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $T$ where every element of $T$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nOf the given collections, only ${{2,4,6},{8},{10}}$ is a partition.\n\nThe rest of the collections are not partitions:\n\n- ${∅,{2,4},{6,8},{10}}$ is not a partition because the subset $∅$ is empty.\n\n- ${∅,{2,4},{6,8},{8,10}}$ is not a partition because the subset $∅$ is empty.\n\n- ${{2},{4},{6,8}}$ is not a partition because the element $10\\in T$ does not appear in any subset.\n\n- ${{2},{2,4},{6,8,10}}$ is not a partition because the element $2$ appears in two subsets." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-1270/ma-source-field/af446cbcf13db178150e47aaa82382f0275bc885784a2525db6b4a8c24996c71"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1b082a95-4d6e-512f-a6ed-9100498d17c8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-1270"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186060025 :question/answer-fields 17592186056478] {:db/id "q-1275/ma-source-field/58b7afc3205aba1a2489abc4d47ec381c55cc3fe2bc8cea371454cb745d09934/14e9edcea2876cfe63523f788e75e3f00b2e34a65a3d32f61ada3d949c00a1aa" :answer/id #uuid "9deb231b-1668-5acf-aa27-d4f09e4e18c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{{1,2,3,…,100}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-1275/ma-source-field/58b7afc3205aba1a2489abc4d47ec381c55cc3fe2bc8cea371454cb745d09934/ae7ab1e8040aa41e42fb453ca2d251cc19bdb73a3dcfc3a4d48dc7b75b4fbcbc" :answer/id #uuid "fa457256-1d86-5c77-8f40-ca7a85884c06" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{{2,4,6,…,40},{20,22,24,…,100}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-1275/ma-source-field/58b7afc3205aba1a2489abc4d47ec381c55cc3fe2bc8cea371454cb745d09934/bdd030af3f8009ce71dd33bef067aa751af5d8b6bc85da166c0376bd9c11b037" :answer/id #uuid "cfb1684e-7d04-57bc-aa28-0cefcf575bb7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{{2,4,6,…,40},{42,44,46,…,60},{62,64,66,…,100}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-1275/ma-source-field/58b7afc3205aba1a2489abc4d47ec381c55cc3fe2bc8cea371454cb745d09934/913ffa7ace8e81b130591da0a46bd69a9be382804fe68f986d0189061f9fd7da" :answer/id #uuid "e42f62b9-16b9-540a-b37c-9e34df98915a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{{2,4,6,…,40},{80,82,84,…,100}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-1275/ma-source-field/58b7afc3205aba1a2489abc4d47ec381c55cc3fe2bc8cea371454cb745d09934/a77fd8fd6c2bf1710d65c449b5429ec383fbab169641a9b8d82d5eb420579249" :answer/id #uuid "ee5204f8-4e4a-5bfb-9e6d-e326273014e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{{4,6,8,10},{10,11,12,…,100}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-1275/ma-source-field/58b7afc3205aba1a2489abc4d47ec381c55cc3fe2bc8cea371454cb745d09934" :answer-field/id #uuid "6126d0ad-c8aa-565d-b641-031a1a0379cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-1275/ma-source-field/58b7afc3205aba1a2489abc4d47ec381c55cc3fe2bc8cea371454cb745d09934/14e9edcea2876cfe63523f788e75e3f00b2e34a65a3d32f61ada3d949c00a1aa" "q-1275/ma-source-field/58b7afc3205aba1a2489abc4d47ec381c55cc3fe2bc8cea371454cb745d09934/ae7ab1e8040aa41e42fb453ca2d251cc19bdb73a3dcfc3a4d48dc7b75b4fbcbc" "q-1275/ma-source-field/58b7afc3205aba1a2489abc4d47ec381c55cc3fe2bc8cea371454cb745d09934/bdd030af3f8009ce71dd33bef067aa751af5d8b6bc85da166c0376bd9c11b037" "q-1275/ma-source-field/58b7afc3205aba1a2489abc4d47ec381c55cc3fe2bc8cea371454cb745d09934/913ffa7ace8e81b130591da0a46bd69a9be382804fe68f986d0189061f9fd7da" "q-1275/ma-source-field/58b7afc3205aba1a2489abc4d47ec381c55cc3fe2bc8cea371454cb745d09934/a77fd8fd6c2bf1710d65c449b5429ec383fbab169641a9b8d82d5eb420579249"] :answer-field/correct "q-1275/ma-source-field/58b7afc3205aba1a2489abc4d47ec381c55cc3fe2bc8cea371454cb745d09934/bdd030af3f8009ce71dd33bef067aa751af5d8b6bc85da166c0376bd9c11b037" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "7e7b9d16-36b0-577e-a63c-c84d780d74e5"] :question/problem "If $Y={2,4,6,…,100},$ which collection of subsets of $Y$ is a partition of $Y?$" :question/worked-solution "A partition of a set $Y$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $Y$ where every element of $Y$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nOf the given collections, only ${{2,4,6,…,40},{42,44,46,…,60},{62,64,66,…,100}}$ is a partition.\n\nThe rest of the collections are not partitions:\n\n- ${{2,4,6,…,40},{80,82,84,…,100}}$ is not a partition because many elements of $Y$ (such as $42$) do not appear in any subsets.\n\n- ${{2,4,6,…,40},{20,22,24,…,100}}$ is not a partition because many elements (such as $20$) appear in both subsets.\n\n- ${{1,2,3,…,100}}$ is not a partition because it contains many elements (such as $1$) that do not appear in $Y.$\n\n- ${{4,6,8,10},{10,11,12,…,100}}$ is not a partition because it contains many elements (such as $11$) that do not appear in $Y.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-1275/ma-source-field/58b7afc3205aba1a2489abc4d47ec381c55cc3fe2bc8cea371454cb745d09934"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-13497/ma-source-field/18e512fc1475be2a2b38b955cb26b6a286ec7404e1dde3b1121891bea7fa1cc3/e9bc05c525076ace5de