eld/1444459bd1c216dfe49d32e008dbeb3a5ca034bed3b2d4a34e7c7f12286dab0a/16989581b4dd143fa2853cd83581d7bc569a86c0758c326053a3f45347c4bd08"] :answer-field/correct "q-14191/ma-source-field/1444459bd1c216dfe49d32e008dbeb3a5ca034bed3b2d4a34e7c7f12286dab0a/16989581b4dd143fa2853cd83581d7bc569a86c0758c326053a3f45347c4bd08" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-14191" :question/id #uuid "2a1f70ec-1a84-5f86-99bd-fdd4752087f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-14191" :question/problem "Find the point of intersection of the parabola ${y}^{2}+13x-15y-2=0$ with the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "When the parabola intersects the $x$-axis, we must have $y=0.$ So, we set $y=0$ and solve the resulting equation for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0)^{2}+13x-15(0)-2 & =0 \\\\ 13x-2 & =0 \\\\ x & =\\frac{2}{13}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parabola intersects the $x$-axis at $(\\frac{2}{13},0).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-14191/ma-source-field/1444459bd1c216dfe49d32e008dbeb3a5ca034bed3b2d4a34e7c7f12286dab0a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ddc6c4b1-b4c4-52f8-9f25-feda3130e358"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-14191"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-15589/ma-source-field/7f6471e2e7c78c325461e6c2155d73bb460331165cc546a99096c7720ff874f6/e385ce8df70f14ca2e692d3af7a0b0a16669f00373850da3011cac836bd689df" :answer/id #uuid "96517c6b-bae9-503f-9f98-d3f004b861a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "67\\,\\text{min}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15589/ma-source-field/7f6471e2e7c78c325461e6c2155d73bb460331165cc546a99096c7720ff874f6/2cf3041fe613092a3cb91167de3811d7c800363142e441d7816e6898b8c506a7" :answer/id #uuid "893f4780-2c8b-522b-8087-2fc24822ebd4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "87\\,\\text{min}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15589/ma-source-field/7f6471e2e7c78c325461e6c2155d73bb460331165cc546a99096c7720ff874f6/b34caf75d45c2434d6db648f7d4eb2cc3aa66126e4c7fa3f14b308a6265ea097" :answer/id #uuid "d38f97ca-3e74-5b74-90a6-ef1513732aca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "89\\,\\text{min}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15589/ma-source-field/7f6471e2e7c78c325461e6c2155d73bb460331165cc546a99096c7720ff874f6/78370e4263cc27a90f67891f92375a8bf28ca812f1bd76811b00da3570fc962e" :answer/id #uuid "93cd5cdd-b047-544f-b7e7-fee685cf62f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "95\\,\\text{min}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15589/ma-source-field/7f6471e2e7c78c325461e6c2155d73bb460331165cc546a99096c7720ff874f6/81a7d6f4b2bdc9b8e9cec4b954ca4669e7ce894d2451c91ca777f780936c384e" :answer/id #uuid "ef24ffa0-3d6e-5335-9009-9906ff059c99" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "98\\,\\text{min}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15589/ma-source-field/7f6471e2e7c78c325461e6c2155d73bb460331165cc546a99096c7720ff874f6" :answer-field/id #uuid "fca47f9c-32af-5d7e-92a5-e9a1ab61bc65" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-15589/ma-source-field/7f6471e2e7c78c325461e6c2155d73bb460331165cc546a99096c7720ff874f6/e385ce8df70f14ca2e692d3af7a0b0a16669f00373850da3011cac836bd689df" "q-15589/ma-source-field/7f6471e2e7c78c325461e6c2155d73bb460331165cc546a99096c7720ff874f6/2cf3041fe613092a3cb91167de3811d7c800363142e441d7816e6898b8c506a7" "q-15589/ma-source-field/7f6471e2e7c78c325461e6c2155d73bb460331165cc546a99096c7720ff874f6/b34caf75d45c2434d6db648f7d4eb2cc3aa66126e4c7fa3f14b308a6265ea097" "q-15589/ma-source-field/7f6471e2e7c78c325461e6c2155d73bb460331165cc546a99096c7720ff874f6/78370e4263cc27a90f67891f92375a8bf28ca812f1bd76811b00da3570fc962e" "q-15589/ma-source-field/7f6471e2e7c78c325461e6c2155d73bb460331165cc546a99096c7720ff874f6/81a7d6f4b2bdc9b8e9cec4b954ca4669e7ce894d2451c91ca777f780936c384e"] :answer-field/correct "q-15589/ma-source-field/7f6471e2e7c78c325461e6c2155d73bb460331165cc546a99096c7720ff874f6/78370e4263cc27a90f67891f92375a8bf28ca812f1bd76811b00da3570fc962e" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-15589" :question/id #uuid "02ce9872-8986-5e67-bea1-b49d589c24ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-15589" :question/problem "The water boils in a pan at a temperature of ${100}^{∘}C.$ The pan with water is then placed to a room with a temperature of ${25}^{∘}C,$ and the temperature of water decreases. After $5$ minutes, it cools to ${90}^{∘}C.$ To the nearest minute, how long does it take for the water to have a temperature of ${30}^{∘}C?$ \n\n*Hint: You may assume that the temperature reading $T(t)$ of the water in the pan decreases at a rate that obeys Newton's law of cooling, where $T$ is measured in degrees Celsius and $t>0$ is the time, in minutes, since the water starts cooling.*" :question/worked-solution "Newton's law of cooling states that the rate at which the temperature $T(t)$ of a body changes is proportional to the difference between its temperature and its surroundings. Therefore, we have the inhibited decay equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-k(T-{T}_{S}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${T}_{S}$ is the temperature of the surroundings, and $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality.\n\nIn our case, ${T}_{S}={25}^{∘}\\text{C},$ and we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-k(T-25).\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate our differential equation by separating the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dT}{T-25} & =-k\\,dt \\\\ \\int \\frac{dT}{T-25} & =-k\\int dt \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|T-25| & =-kt+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this is the solution to an inhibited decay equation, we have $T-25>0$ for all $t>0.$\nNext, we solve for $T(t),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T-25 & ={e}^{-kt+C} \\\\ T-25 & ={e}^{C}{e}^{-kt} \\\\ T-25 & =K{e}^{-kt} \\\\ T & =25+K{e}^{-kt}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $K={e}^{C}$ is a constant of integration. \n\nWe're told that the initial temperature was ${100}^{∘}C.$ So, we apply the initial condition $T(0)=100,$ and solve for $K:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}100 & =25+K{e}^{0} \\\\ 100 & =25+K \\\\ K & =75\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following expression for $T(t):$\n\n$$\nT(t)=25+75{e}^{-kt}\n$$\n\nWe're also told that, after $5$ minutes, it cools to ${90}^{∘}C.$ So, applying the condition $T(5)=90,$ we can solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}90 & =25+75{e}^{-5k} \\\\ 65 & =75{e}^{-5k} \\\\ \\frac{13}{15} & ={e}^{-5k} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{13}{15}) & =-5k \\\\ k & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{13}{15})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, let ${t}_{1}$ be the time when the water has a temperature of ${30}^{∘}C.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({t}_{1}) & =30 \\\\ 25+75{e}^{-k{t}_{1}} & =30 \\\\ 75{e}^{-k{t}_{1}} & =5 \\\\ {e}^{-k{t}_{1}} & =\\frac{1}{15} \\\\ -k{t}_{1} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{15}) \\\\ {t}_{1} & =-\\frac{1}{k}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{15}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting in our value for $k,$ we conclude that the temperature of water will be ${30}^{∘}C$ after\n\n$$\n{t}_{1}=\\frac{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{15})}{-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{13}{15})}≈95\\,\\text{min},\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest minute." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-15589/ma-source-field/7f6471e2e7c78c325461e6c2155d73bb460331165cc546a99096c7720ff874f6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bfe4679b-9724-5502-89d4-05e7661a1b5f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-15589"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-20512/ma-source-field/d1f0e81af0136c9857cd93c7fb6f101488d8577f3cc6de0b95e882f28d83ad15/efaa7bd3d4f8e8110d9bcac6d204f4f88e0de8467ac2ed3c49c58654448589ee" :answer/id #uuid "fa67123d-ee59-563d-90e5-5d86c85b1243" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-11,4,4⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20512/ma-source-field/d1f0e81af0136c9857cd93c7fb6f101488d8577f3cc6de0b95e882f28d83ad15/46996c293a0e5a395194e12cf3aa4eaf1c1ba7c8384710202d2b89162326291b" :answer/id #uuid "23b6f110-fbc4-5322-8a05-6366ff4c13c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨1,4,-2⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20512/ma-source-field/d1f0e81af0136c9857cd93c7fb6f101488d8577f3cc6de0b95e882f28d83ad15/d43f2bc3959094d8945e65995fe070d4c5b54544529c2f925c851d0f9149a619" :answer/id #uuid "12ab6864-c814-589e-8f72-328eeae44af0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨13,-4,-4⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20512/ma-source-field/d1f0e81af0136c9857cd93c7fb6f101488d8577f3cc6de0b95e882f28d83ad15/b28998f32559b8196d6bf761d3b3745c7ddfa2f2372a591f566a3643d60bc3d0" :answer/id #uuid "e6302263-6554-5d2f-bdfe-094ceb26b042" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨3,2,-2⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20512/ma-source-field/d1f0e81af0136c9857cd93c7fb6f101488d8577f3cc6de0b95e882f28d83ad15/c51ba793173191e30f05b26d15bcd194e949fe064f36c078cd8064ee1f5e57da" :answer/id #uuid "337c9891-a990-5356-ae53-39e28e060932" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨5,4,-4⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20512/ma-source-field/d1f0e81af0136c9857cd93c7fb6f101488d8577f3cc6de0b95e882f28d83ad15" :answer-field/id #uuid "2a758e48-dc27-560b-a0af-fd01b7ea572b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-20512/ma-source-field/d1f0e81af0136c9857cd93c7fb6f101488d8577f3cc6de0b95e882f28d83ad15/efaa7bd3d4f8e8110d9bcac6d204f4f88e0de8467ac2ed3c49c58654448589ee" "q-20512/ma-source-field/d1f0e81af0136c9857cd93c7fb6f101488d8577f3cc6de0b95e882f28d83ad15/46996c293a0e5a395194e12cf3aa4eaf1c1ba7c8384710202d2b89162326291b" "q-20512/ma-source-field/d1f0e81af0136c9857cd93c7fb6f101488d8577f3cc6de0b95e882f28d83ad15/d43f2bc3959094d8945e65995fe070d4c5b54544529c2f925c851d0f9149a619" "q-20512/ma-source-field/d1f0e81af0136c9857cd93c7fb6f101488d8577f3cc6de0b95e882f28d83ad15/b28998f32559b8196d6bf761d3b3745c7ddfa2f2372a591f566a3643d60bc3d0" "q-20512/ma-source-field/d1f0e81af0136c9857cd93c7fb6f101488d8577f3cc6de0b95e882f28d83ad15/c51ba793173191e30f05b26d15bcd194e949fe064f36c078cd8064ee1f5e57da"] :answer-field/correct "q-20512/ma-source-field/d1f0e81af0136c9857cd93c7fb6f101488d8577f3cc6de0b95e882f28d83ad15/c51ba793173191e30f05b26d15bcd194e949fe064f36c078cd8064ee1f5e57da" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-20512" :question/id #uuid "3437106d-95df-5058-942b-4f64c5179bc5" :question/math-academy-id "q-20512" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y+2z=1 \\\\  & 2x+3y+4z=6 \\\\  & 3x+3y+4z=11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and hence solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 4 & 11\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 4 & 11\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 4 & 11\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y+2z=1 \\\\  & y=4 \\\\  & z=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. Substituting both $y=4$ and $z=-4$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+(4)+2(-4)=1\\,⟹\\,x=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=5,y=4$, and $z=-4.$ Or, in vector form, $⟨5,4,-4⟩.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-20512/ma-source-field/d1f0e81af0136c9857cd93c7fb6f101488d8577f3cc6de0b95e882f28d83ad15"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "739b1cbc-c1a7-547d-a9fb-1f244bd36827"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-20512"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-20849/ma-source-field/e15aa3980e973581b3107ffc08abdc430abb0b5426cd68af5d4ac003fc981600/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "d1c50146-0d7c-501d-bf37-4d8d838c3cef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20849/ma-source-field/e15aa3980e973581b3107ffc08abdc430abb0b5426cd68af5d4ac003fc981600/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "9c9b090b-3cbc-511c-95ab-35fc8c1fc057" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20849/ma-source-field/e15aa3980e973581b3107ffc08abdc430abb0b5426cd68af5d4ac003fc981600/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "26a77c96-4bef-5e82-8889-1c4a9ce7d523" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20849/ma-source-field/e15aa3980e973581b3107ffc08abdc430abb0b5426cd68af5d4ac003fc981600/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "61e0f80f-69b1-578c-857a-82bc0682835a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20849/ma-source-field/e15aa3980e973581b3107ffc08abdc430abb0b5426cd68af5d4ac003fc981600/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "05fd7882-e12b-5d1e-bda2-674211a5aad1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20849/ma-source-field/e15aa3980e973581b3107ffc08abdc430abb0b5426cd68af5d4ac003fc981600" :answer-field/id #uuid "56d7a736-a513-51fb-b585-d99caa2d0531" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-20849/ma-source-field/e15aa3980e973581b3107ffc08abdc430abb0b5426cd68af5d4ac003fc981600/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-20849/ma-source-field/e15aa3980e973581b3107ffc08abdc430abb0b5426cd68af5d4ac003fc981600/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-20849/ma-source-field/e15aa3980e973581b3107ffc08abdc430abb0b5426cd68af5d4ac003fc981600/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-20849/ma-source-field/e15aa3980e973581b3107ffc08abdc430abb0b5426cd68af5d4ac003fc981600/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-20849/ma-source-field/e15aa3980e973581b3107ffc08abdc430abb0b5426cd68af5d4ac003fc981600/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :answer-field/correct "q-20849/ma-source-field/e15aa3980e973581b3107ffc08abdc430abb0b5426cd68af5d4ac003fc981600/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-20849" :question/id #uuid "45b1f64f-9248-57a2-a310-050eb4c80ee5" :question/math-academy-id "q-20849" :question/problem "![](images/c9/c9371d5e2bb921b4f5e58423bbce492f2b555122ee42bd861040b57d01070353.png)\n\nFor the parametric curve (shown above)\n\n$$\nx=2(t+1),\\,y=4{t}^{2},\\,-1\\le t<1,\n$$\n\n find the derivative $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ at the point $P$ on the curve where $t=0.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=2,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=8t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{8t}{2}=4t.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=0$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =4(0) \\\\  & =0\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-20849/ma-source-field/e15aa3980e973581b3107ffc08abdc430abb0b5426cd68af5d4ac003fc981600"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8922ab07-5ac7-5f85-bfee-c30de7f4024a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-20849"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-21496/ma-source-field/e44d1ec315c16231fdb8d59e7d5fd9404991b33f85651a06f9c6b57c4e523650/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "23b5a4de-82e3-5600-a5e2-8553e265a482" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-21496/ma-source-field/e44d1ec315c16231fdb8d59e7d5fd9404991b33f85651a06f9c6b57c4e523650/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "13e59b84-50f4-570b-b93f-907264edf062" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-21496/ma-source-field/e44d1ec315c16231fdb8d59e7d5fd9404991b33f85651a06f9c6b57c4e523650/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" :answer/id #uuid "075ca13a-66f5-514e-be5e-b8fce546f7e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-21496/ma-source-field/e44d1ec315c16231fdb8d59e7d5fd9404991b33f85651a06f9c6b57c4e523650/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "0135acbf-05a9-5225-8572-13c90063bbc7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-21496/ma-source-field/e44d1ec315c16231fdb8d59e7d5fd9404991b33f85651a06f9c6b57c4e523650/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :answer/id #uuid "220c4644-028c-5dcb-955d-3b2d5604dc62" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-21496/ma-source-field/e44d1ec315c16231fdb8d59e7d5fd9404991b33f85651a06f9c6b57c4e523650" :answer-field/id #uuid "5e6ea143-756a-5eb6-a6ed-9e3449dbdb6b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-21496/ma-source-field/e44d1ec315c16231fdb8d59e7d5fd9404991b33f85651a06f9c6b57c4e523650/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-21496/ma-source-field/e44d1ec315c16231fdb8d59e7d5fd9404991b33f85651a06f9c6b57c4e523650/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-21496/ma-source-field/e44d1ec315c16231fdb8d59e7d5fd9404991b33f85651a06f9c6b57c4e523650/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" "q-21496/ma-source-field/e44d1ec315c16231fdb8d59e7d5fd9404991b33f85651a06f9c6b57c4e523650/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-21496/ma-source-field/e44d1ec315c16231fdb8d59e7d5fd9404991b33f85651a06f9c6b57c4e523650/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d"] :answer-field/correct "q-21496/ma-source-field/e44d1ec315c16231fdb8d59e7d5fd9404991b33f85651a06f9c6b57c4e523650/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-21496" :question/id #uuid "6bb098c4-0b9d-56fe-8eb4-70ba83a986f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-21496" :question/problem "For which value of $x$ does the function $f(x)={x}^{3}+\\frac{48}{x}$ defined for $x\\in (0,\\infty )$ have a local minimum?" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the stationary points. Differentiating $f(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =3{x}^{2}-\\frac{48}{{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving for ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ on $(0,\\infty )$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-\\frac{48}{{x}^{2}} & =0 \\\\ 3{x}^{4}-48 & =0 \\\\ 3({x}^{4}-16) & =0 \\\\ 3({x}^{2}+4)({x}^{2}-4) & =0 \\\\ 3({x}^{2}+4)(x+2)(x-2) & =0 \\\\ x & =\\pm 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $x=2$ is a stationary point on $(0,\\infty ).$ Next, to determine whether this point is a local maximum or minimum, we use the first derivative test.\n\nLet's choose the test points $x=1,3$ and evaluate the first derivative at these points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(1) & =3(1)^{2}-\\frac{48}{{1}^{2}}=-45<0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(3) & =3(3)^{2}-\\frac{48}{{3}^{2}}=27-\\frac{16}{3}=\\frac{65}{3}>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe summarize the information in a table, shown below.\n\n| $x$ | $(0,2)$ | $2$ | $(2,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Test Point | $1$ |  | $3$ |\n| ${f}^{′}$ | $-$ | $0$ | $+$ |\n| $f$ | $↘$ | min | $↗$ |\n\nFinally, let's use the table above to classify the critical point.\n\n- At $x=2,$ the first derivative changes sign from negative to positive. Therefore, $x=2$ is a local minimum.\n\nWe conclude that $f(x)$ has a local minimum at $x=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-21496/ma-source-field/e44d1ec315c16231fdb8d59e7d5fd9404991b33f85651a06f9c6b57c4e523650"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dbad38a0-e6cb-563a-8e9c-1cee08397083"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-21496"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-2549/ma-source-field/dca90a9c3e5a3a8340a6bd9c76376af96866513c569f446ffb615a31cb69e3f1/f2b80e5a11c9774fad5cfe3007a91eb0af75dd4b56983d93512be068bd04fd61" :answer/id #uuid "350623d5-cf3b-562c-adbc-4f53ac07cc99" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\pi \\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}\\text{/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2549/ma-source-field/dca90a9c3e5a3a8340a6bd9c76376af96866513c569f446ffb615a31cb69e3f1/34f28c184101788d90cae8d03ab323a736af9485fc6065c64602a2b57da082a3" :answer/id #uuid "967e7ed0-7817-52a2-8722-d7d6b2028465" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16\\pi \\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}\\text{/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2549/ma-source-field/dca90a9c3e5a3a8340a6bd9c76376af96866513c569f446ffb615a31cb69e3f1/748b65bf06275ce1849f1d229bbc2ece101e903fc326bb9480a9400067b92dc4" :answer/id #uuid "ffad3220-17fd-5911-9971-a3e690e83416" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24\\pi \\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}\\text{/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2549/ma-source-field/dca90a9c3e5a3a8340a6bd9c76376af96866513c569f446ffb615a31cb69e3f1/dee2cc55ff99f6ad9df62fd019e38db43d7e50d65a5f68edbe6791ad9d8936a0" :answer/id #uuid "b99d6896-ed6a-55b6-8e15-065a39717d54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi \\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}\\text{/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2549/ma-source-field/dca90a9c3e5a3a8340a6bd9c76376af96866513c569f446ffb615a31cb69e3f1/0cd7dd92b0df7955bf359b5ede2eeb4b71b2a19e08d914fbfbb5016c58bcad28" :answer/id #uuid "b1ea5dbf-e0e0-5b87-9716-69e18e732d25" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\pi \\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}\\text{/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2549/ma-source-field/dca90a9c3e5a3a8340a6bd9c76376af96866513c569f446ffb615a31cb69e3f1" :answer-field/id #uuid "86b9d34d-27a9-54ed-b870-554479215d16" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-2549/ma-source-field/dca90a9c3e5a3a8340a6bd9c76376af96866513c569f446ffb615a31cb69e3f1/f2b80e5a11c9774fad5cfe3007a91eb0af75dd4b56983d93512be068bd04fd61" "q-2549/ma-source-field/dca90a9c3e5a3a8340a6bd9c76376af96866513c569f446ffb615a31cb69e3f1/34f28c184101788d90cae8d03ab323a736af9485fc6065c64602a2b57da082a3" "q-2549/ma-source-field/dca90a9c3e5a3a8340a6bd9c76376af96866513c569f446ffb615a31cb69e3f1/748b65bf06275ce1849f1d229bbc2ece101e903fc326bb9480a9400067b92dc4" "q-2549/ma-source-field/dca90a9c3e5a3a8340a6bd9c76376af96866513c569f446ffb615a31cb69e3f1/dee2cc55ff99f6ad9df62fd019e38db43d7e50d65a5f68edbe6791ad9d8936a0" "q-2549/ma-source-field/dca90a9c3e5a3a8340a6bd9c76376af96866513c569f446ffb615a31cb69e3f1/0cd7dd92b0df7955bf359b5ede2eeb4b71b2a19e08d914fbfbb5016c58bcad28"] :answer-field/correct "q-2549/ma-source-field/dca90a9c3e5a3a8340a6bd9c76376af96866513c569f446ffb615a31cb69e3f1/34f28c184101788d90cae8d03ab323a736af9485fc6065c64602a2b57da082a3" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-2549" :question/id #uuid "236c5a80-1a72-598b-b891-11878898b571" :question/math-academy-id "q-2549" :question/problem "![](images/27/2771f90d4200f292afe8108a26b8a2e83e6f3a46194c89a18d1688943984b5af.png)\n\nA spherical balloon is inflated so that its radius increases at a rate of $1\\,\\text{cm/s}.$ How fast is the volume of the balloon increasing at the moment when the radius is $2\\,\\text{cm}?$" :question/worked-solution "Let $r$ be the radius of the balloon and $V$ its volume. Both $r$ and $V$ change with time. In particular, we are given\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}=1\\,\\text{cm/s},\n$$\n\nand we want to find $\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}$ when $r=2\\,\\text{cm}.$\n\nTo start, let's write down the volume formula for the sphere and then differentiate it using implicit differentiation. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =\\frac{4}{3}\\pi {r}^{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(V) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{4}{3}\\pi {r}^{3}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}r}(\\frac{4}{3}\\pi {r}^{3}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot 4\\pi {r}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}=1$ and $r=2,$ and solve for $\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =1\\cdot 4\\pi (2)^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =16\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the balloon is increasing at a rate of $16\\pi {\\text{ cm}}^{3}\\text{/s}$\n when the radius is $2\\,\\text{cm}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-2549/ma-source-field/dca90a9c3e5a3a8340a6bd9c76376af96866513c569f446ffb615a31cb69e3f1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dabb3127-172e-5a68-8e27-d22057f8ea8e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-2549"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-2870/ma-source-field/99549ef511efc310e19a15f08816b80b0b4533f3f9dd090f620d4e12fe4fee4c/4a3ad8ebe42b7895f5987a6a7a1e9c31b4796b6c56e1fa3ad176f434988efd67" :answer/id #uuid "112e9965-7e8a-5453-8d21-40a47cdfca08" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\pi \\,\\text{cm}\\text{/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2870/ma-source-field/99549ef511efc310e19a15f08816b80b0b4533f3f9dd090f620d4e12fe4fee4c/3014744c0cff48b429e0946231decaabcb8205d3b53d93cfc0d17660733f5bfc" :answer/id #uuid "0402c49a-95bf-5a4c-8db7-76e1232ae67c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\,8\\pi \\,\\text{cm}\\text{/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2870/ma-source-field/99549ef511efc310e19a15f08816b80b0b4533f3f9dd090f620d4e12fe4fee4c/7fec0e9b86a27c88f83ed71e4fcf376a21f0e74e0638653fc08d4ad823140aab" :answer/id #uuid "5fad6157-8ec0-522c-a83c-2d09b502068f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{8}\\,\\text{cm/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2870/ma-source-field/99549ef511efc310e19a15f08816b80b0b4533f3f9dd090f620d4e12fe4fee4c/3c1ec121a9bac83b4844ab48570e12e670a3749cc2319caf5c05a84605e8e95e" :answer/id #uuid "c0e22878-a171-5db7-ae1d-822a413a7af0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8\\pi }{5}\\,\\text{cm/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2870/ma-source-field/99549ef511efc310e19a15f08816b80b0b4533f3f9dd090f620d4e12fe4fee4c/f16c715aab506893b83ffce3ddaa26fe3e3004b0afcff3fb617af2303e45042e" :answer/id #uuid "6152d76a-2613-532a-801b-10af2c97cb7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{5}\\,\\text{cm/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2870/ma-source-field/99549ef511efc310e19a15f08816b80b0b4533f3f9dd090f620d4e12fe4fee4c" :answer-field/id #uuid "ec61e892-1bbe-5a6b-9b14-17fd1b7ef765" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-2870/ma-source-field/99549ef511efc310e19a15f08816b80b0b4533f3f9dd090f620d4e12fe4fee4c/4a3ad8ebe42b7895f5987a6a7a1e9c31b4796b6c56e1fa3ad176f434988efd67" "q-2870/ma-source-field/99549ef511efc310e19a15f08816b80b0b4533f3f9dd090f620d4e12fe4fee4c/3014744c0cff48b429e0946231decaabcb8205d3b53d93cfc0d17660733f5bfc" "q-2870/ma-source-field/99549ef511efc310e19a15f08816b80b0b4533f3f9dd090f620d4e12fe4fee4c/7fec0e9b86a27c88f83ed71e4fcf376a21f0e74e0638653fc08d4ad823140aab" "q-2870/ma-source-field/99549ef511efc310e19a15f08816b80b0b4533f3f9dd090f620d4e12fe4fee4c/3c1ec121a9bac83b4844ab48570e12e670a3749cc2319caf5c05a84605e8e95e" "q-2870/ma-source-field/99549ef511efc310e19a15f08816b80b0b4533f3f9dd090f620d4e12fe4fee4c/f16c715aab506893b83ffce3ddaa26fe3e3004b0afcff3fb617af2303e45042e"] :answer-field/correct "q-2870/ma-source-field/99549ef511efc310e19a15f08816b80b0b4533f3f9dd090f620d4e12fe4fee4c/3c1ec121a9bac83b4844ab48570e12e670a3749cc2319caf5c05a84605e8e95e" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-2870" :question/id #uuid "a45a10dd-0c29-5839-ade5-5e0193cac871" :question/math-academy-id "q-2870" :question/problem "![](images/59/598fa373c0312c910c1a13b435a35e6745d3c912884b36b208b7c2d4fca42f75.png)\n\nA circle is decreasing in area at a rate of $8\\pi \\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}\\text{/s}.$ Calculate the rate at which the circumference of the circle is decreasing at the moment when the radius is  $5\\,\\text{cm}.$" :question/worked-solution "In this situation, we want to find $\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}$ at the moment when $r=5,$ and we are also told that  $\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=-8\\pi .$\n\nTo start, let's set up an equation relating the area $A$ and the circumference $C$ of the circle. Since $C=2\\pi r$ and $A=\\pi {r}^{2},$ the relationship between $A$ and $C$ is\n\n$$\nA=\\pi {r}^{2}=\\pi {(\\frac{C}{2\\pi })}^{2}=\\frac{{C}^{2}}{4\\pi }.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating this relationship with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(A) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{{C}^{2}}{4\\pi }) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}C}(\\frac{{C}^{2}}{4\\pi }) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{C}{2\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen $r=5\\,\\text{cm},$ $C=2\\pi (5)=10\\pi \\text{ cm}.$ Hence, substituting $\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=-8\\pi $ and $C=10\\pi $, and solving for $\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-8\\pi  & =\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{10\\pi }{2\\pi } \\\\ -8\\pi  & =\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot 5 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t} & =-\\frac{8\\pi }{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the circumference is decreasing at a rate of $\\frac{8\\pi }{5}\\text{ cm/s}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-2870/ma-source-field/99549ef511efc310e19a15f08816b80b0b4533f3f9dd090f620d4e12fe4fee4c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b2dbfe46-55f0-5d6a-b410-164f0aa2345f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-2870"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-29664/ma-source-field/161a4147179d5992442a3587de65a2157d710f884a1dbeffc321d697b0ef16a9/c3e74ce6fba7b7bd77c7afbf20a82e8f73f6cac3363858b8840c65664e418e03" :answer/id #uuid "8c3be72d-8de9-5e24-a778-ee5537402bbc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6\\,561" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29664/ma-source-field/161a4147179d5992442a3587de65a2157d710f884a1dbeffc321d697b0ef16a9/93ba270014b2121e0d07324bf08630808d6ed9bfb1e523439708be4e1492051c" :answer/id #uuid "0d4cbb58-b903-5380-9c08-172acb79c3a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6\\,631" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29664/ma-source-field/161a4147179d5992442a3587de65a2157d710f884a1dbeffc321d697b0ef16a9/5172a7fa160e878951e4187c255e106b57da0d14098cfe25d30cce3dbd3535c3" :answer/id #uuid "9c07c6a6-5b40-55a4-9250-674b5ab51617" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6\\,731" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29664/ma-source-field/161a4147179d5992442a3587de65a2157d710f884a1dbeffc321d697b0ef16a9/48ed8822e91c61d2180f4e9f6c1b03af7fc6ed780f3ab54702820deafad2d24e" :answer/id #uuid "35051668-a56c-5024-9510-5bb50d0360fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6\\,741" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29664/ma-source-field/161a4147179d5992442a3587de65a2157d710f884a1dbeffc321d697b0ef16a9/af3979f69e3c75cfe7f3145a4d599cb170a6cd2ea2b65bc8aeb427117c37252c" :answer/id #uuid "6fbfb4e9-a306-5d6f-a040-1f5b9ed69042" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6\\,851" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29664/ma-source-field/161a4147179d5992442a3587de65a2157d710f884a1dbeffc321d697b0ef16a9" :answer-field/id #uuid "4440a234-4417-5c7c-aab8-361ac22515f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-29664/ma-source-field/161a4147179d5992442a3587de65a2157d710f884a1dbeffc321d697b0ef16a9/c3e74ce6fba7b7bd77c7afbf20a82e8f73f6cac3363858b8840c65664e418e03" "q-29664/ma-source-field/161a4147179d5992442a3587de65a2157d710f884a1dbeffc321d697b0ef16a9/93ba270014b2121e0d07324bf08630808d6ed9bfb1e523439708be4e1492051c" "q-29664/ma-source-field/161a4147179d5992442a3587de65a2157d710f884a1dbeffc321d697b0ef16a9/5172a7fa160e878951e4187c255e106b57da0d14098cfe25d30cce3dbd3535c3" "q-29664/ma-source-field/161a4147179d5992442a3587de65a2157d710f884a1dbeffc321d697b0ef16a9/48ed8822e91c61d2180f4e9f6c1b03af7fc6ed780f3ab54702820deafad2d24e" "q-29664/ma-source-field/161a4147179d5992442a3587de65a2157d710f884a1dbeffc321d697b0ef16a9/af3979f69e3c75cfe7f3145a4d599cb170a6cd2ea2b65bc8aeb427117c37252c"] :answer-field/correct "q-29664/ma-source-field/161a4147179d5992442a3587de65a2157d710f884a1dbeffc321d697b0ef16a9/48ed8822e91c61d2180f4e9f6c1b03af7fc6ed780f3ab54702820deafad2d24e" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-29664" :question/id #uuid "0fa4866c-44a3-53be-9ea4-1b3c073da31b" :question/math-academy-id "q-29664" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=-\\frac{3}{4}$ for $-{180}^{∘}<x<{180}^{∘},$ what is the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to the nearest integer?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=-\\frac{4}{3}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{4}{3})=(-53.130\\,1…)^{∘}≈-{53.130}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $-{53.130}^{∘}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=-{53.130}^{∘}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add and subtract integer multiples of ${180}^{∘}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={180}^{∘}+x={180}^{∘}-{53.130}^{∘}={126.870}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are $x=-{53.130}^{∘},{126.870}^{∘}.$\n\nFinally, the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ is \n\n$$\n-53.130\\cdot 126.870≈-6\\,741\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-29664/ma-source-field/161a4147179d5992442a3587de65a2157d710f884a1dbeffc321d697b0ef16a9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74c9c0f6-034c-5d9c-935a-ca27dec1a648"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-29664"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-29938/ma-source-field/fb917fd2ca354a692e4851043222d078e776120f5e61c2a38efc7a5b1ed19775/d0795dccb83c33dee9f6c40fc5861981194d922d39108f0d1718f2db6c872d68" :answer/id #uuid "21c0594d-dee0-5fde-9687-2438c3bda33b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\,764" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29938/ma-source-field/fb917fd2ca354a692e4851043222d078e776120f5e61c2a38efc7a5b1ed19775/3eb7e86a5301d81e22123b1f8828df783a8aa2579e4ae66cbac8a2a4a641d5de" :answer/id #uuid "ab6f005d-5267-58e5-84bf-a80272331a4e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\,176" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29938/ma-source-field/fb917fd2ca354a692e4851043222d078e776120f5e61c2a38efc7a5b1ed19775/b0268ffab97bb8fb45c260106dab456aa5c59a1a3724c3711e908fb5105be6b7" :answer/id #uuid "198aafc0-07ef-5e53-9034-41f2a9658b0c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\,746" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29938/ma-source-field/fb917fd2ca354a692e4851043222d078e776120f5e61c2a38efc7a5b1ed19775/a0228fd582809fc506469c07c6d83c7757563ccc7b4eb0eebff8794ce0778fc9" :answer/id #uuid "ce65e29e-1b9d-54dc-94af-379795c62563" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\,741" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29938/ma-source-field/fb917fd2ca354a692e4851043222d078e776120f5e61c2a38efc7a5b1ed19775/524c6e0f946ce3994a022ac951e768a72c1813cf14016487cd5276decc7f3b62" :answer/id #uuid "7e3a07e3-abf9-52a3-90a9-53487e034b7f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7\\,641" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29938/ma-source-field/fb917fd2ca354a692e4851043222d078e776120f5e61c2a38efc7a5b1ed19775" :answer-field/id #uuid "d68ef59f-9eeb-59d5-b977-da3a30f3eafc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-29938/ma-source-field/fb917fd2ca354a692e4851043222d078e776120f5e61c2a38efc7a5b1ed19775/d0795dccb83c33dee9f6c40fc5861981194d922d39108f0d1718f2db6c872d68" "q-29938/ma-source-field/fb917fd2ca354a692e4851043222d078e776120f5e61c2a38efc7a5b1ed19775/3eb7e86a5301d81e22123b1f8828df783a8aa2579e4ae66cbac8a2a4a641d5de" "q-29938/ma-source-field/fb917fd2ca354a692e4851043222d078e776120f5e61c2a38efc7a5b1ed19775/b0268ffab97bb8fb45c260106dab456aa5c59a1a3724c3711e908fb5105be6b7" "q-29938/ma-source-field/fb917fd2ca354a692e4851043222d078e776120f5e61c2a38efc7a5b1ed19775/a0228fd582809fc506469c07c6d83c7757563ccc7b4eb0eebff8794ce0778fc9" "q-29938/ma-source-field/fb917fd2ca354a692e4851043222d078e776120f5e61c2a38efc7a5b1ed19775/524c6e0f946ce3994a022ac951e768a72c1813cf14016487cd5276decc7f3b62"] :answer-field/correct "q-29938/ma-source-field/fb917fd2ca354a692e4851043222d078e776120f5e61c2a38efc7a5b1ed19775/a0228fd582809fc506469c07c6d83c7757563ccc7b4eb0eebff8794ce0778fc9" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-29938" :question/id #uuid "fa37b599-4ad5-59f0-a1aa-7677947192cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-29938" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{5}{4}$ for $-{180}^{∘}\\le x<{180}^{∘},$ what is the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to the nearest integer?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x},$ therefore the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\\frac{4}{5}.\n$$\n\nNow, we have to find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{4}{5})=(53.130\\,1…)^{∘}≈{53.130}^{∘}\n$$\n\nSince ${53.130}^{∘}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={53.130}^{∘}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the first quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={53.130}^{∘}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x>0,$ the second solution must lie in the second quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}={53.130}^{∘}.$\n\n![](images/60/605af77803fb027c09833b50801fe4b8e6a42a2b623af94a732d0f2f222f9f4a.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $2$nd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={180}^{∘}-{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}-{53.130}^{∘} \\\\  & ={126.870}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x={53.130}^{∘},{126.870}^{∘}.$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}≈53.130\\cdot 126.870≈6\\,741.\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-29938/ma-source-field/fb917fd2ca354a692e4851043222d078e776120f5e61c2a38efc7a5b1ed19775"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "65e15de1-ee72-55ea-accb-1124f3a0ac0c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-29938"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-32531/ma-source-field/cff88df0a0e62b0ae4132dd30db0d5a707cf7586cff5ce9ddf0c53ef7918958d/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" :answer/id #uuid "dde7cc49-7da0-570d-8620-a8c63e1c4ed1" :answer/type :answe