{:db/id [:question/id #uuid "65b5aaee-5eaf-5370-809f-ff7bd458f787"] :question/problem "Given that the intersection of the elliptic cone $3(x+4)^{2}+8{y}^{2}=12{z}^{2}$ and the plane $z=-2$ is an ellipse, what is the length of its major axis?" :question/worked-solution "To find the intersection of the elliptic cone and the plane $z=-2,$ we substitute $z=-2$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(x+4)^{2}+8{y}^{2} & =12{z}^{2} \\\\ 3(x+4)^{2}+8{y}^{2} & =12(-2)^{2} \\\\ 3(x+4)^{2}+8{y}^{2} & =48 \\\\ \\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{6} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{{4}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{6})^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of an ellipse with a semi-major axis of length $a=4.$ Therefore, the major axis has length $2a=8.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-35620/ma-source-field/dccd123cd571ec167209c90932bb96eda86925a1d2af6edcf4f84292e4170a7d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-36751/ma-source-field/2bf811cd2c5d4c53b2d24d2d049063dba31f8e17898697f9ea528244c26b5f2e/a3a5487afcc81a1c06c56ceaee82744a099a79debc8be0e8469f77e68bf12a04" :answer/id #uuid "2b8676d3-b996-5159-ad55-61435ab23a57" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36751/ma-source-field/2bf811cd2c5d4c53b2d24d2d049063dba31f8e17898697f9ea528244c26b5f2e/f98c18a27dcb118caf5a5576c91aab2f7c6ef2dcdc9bdea8485ada011f865eac" :answer/id #uuid "c656b630-9296-566d-94e1-6ddab8563e42" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36751/ma-source-field/2bf811cd2c5d4c53b2d24d2d049063dba31f8e17898697f9ea528244c26b5f2e/82c79a11c5f316588a4977bf9de059017422d38604e630b6407357df3b622d75" :answer/id #uuid "3e1a8aa3-46ff-5b95-94c5-aa562df4b40b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\