 "q-36751" :question/id #uuid "d8eadfe0-8324-566b-8c56-2906c1bb6d35" :question/math-academy-id "q-36751" :question/problem "Find an eigenvector of\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]$\nthat corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =3.$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the eigenvectors of a matrix, we need to find non-zero solutions of the matrix equation \n\n$$\n(A-\\lambda I)\\text{x}=0.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have $\\lambda =3.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-\\lambda  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the eigenvectors corresponding to this eigenvalue, we have to solve the corresponding homogeneous system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we row-reduce the augmented matrix $M$ to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are two pivot columns (the $2$nd and the $3$rd). Thus, ${x}_{1}$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we obtain ${x}_{3}=0.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get ${x}_{2}=0.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{1}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting, for instance, ${x}_{1}=1,$ we get the eigenvector\n$v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-36751/ma-source-field/2bf811cd2c5d4c53b2d24d2d049063dba31f8e17898697f9ea528244c26b5f2e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4def2d61-0093-53cf-bcbb-1d2c3e6e1738"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-36751"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-36911/ma-source-field/a4e2d59120f3312b1505a2fed52b1eed7f5f463de87650d9a9f00d433a06b886/228d7b42fcb34515143bb5c9b68cc81052255c360fff1053199a2147dbd7eb12" :answer/id #uuid "c3c6467b-917f-5aae-9cc9-3d8de87bf705" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36911/ma-source-field/a4e2d59120f3312b1505a2fed52b1eed7f5f463de87650d9a9f00d433a06b886/aca3fb0d9ddb49350c290ac929c3cc1d4fe3619668acb3d7b8d6d89671359f83" :answer/id #uuid "4b5d5b3b-9e1f-57a7-8376-c15ae99d31d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36911/ma-source-field/a4e2d59120f3312b1505a2fed52b1eed7f5f463de87650d9a9f00d433a06b886/7a5aab969ffcdbe5ac6bd1a68897506c93bac105dd752828cf140c8ec9e1f647" :answer/id #uuid "8a0c76fb-2820-5cf1-9645-b9dbc230a965" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1,2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36911/ma-source-field/a4e2d59120f3312b1505a2fed52b1eed7f5f463de87650d9a9f00d433a06b886/981a2951e3fccc9ba81c501537ab818060069591c658c07fba6936fa5fd0dd27" :answer/id #uuid "bef1175c-5920-532e-b7b5-9da5b087ef6f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(3,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36911/ma-source-field/a4e2d59120f3312b1505a2fed52b1eed7f5f463de87650d9a9f00d433a06b886/464b9ac5ac22bfcc69adaf42253a8d7a5eef4a84e7c96c7715039d251f95788a" :answer/id #uuid "95acc209-e214-5661-af27-7731166005f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{3}{4})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36911/ma-source-field/a4e2d59120f3312b1505a2fed52b1eed7f5f463de87650d9a9f00d433a06b886" :answer-field/id #uuid "3ad0dc77-76f9-5eaa-aa66-ed1f16aa44f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-36911/ma-source-field/a4e2d59120f3312b1505a2fed52b1eed7f5f463de87650d9a9f00d433a06b886/228d7b42fcb34515143bb5c9b68cc81052255c360fff1053199a2147dbd7eb12" "q-36911/ma-source-field/a4e2d59120f3312b1505a2fed52b1eed7f5f463de87650d9a9f00d433a06b886/aca3fb0d9ddb49350c290ac929c3cc1d4fe3619668acb3d7b8d6d89671359f83" "q-36911/ma-source-field/a4e2d59120f3312b1505a2fed52b1eed7f5f463de87650d9a9f00d433a06b886/7a5aab969ffcdbe5ac6bd1a68897506c93bac105dd752828cf140c8ec9e1f647" "q-36911/ma-source-field/a4e2d59120f3312b1505a2fed52b1eed7f5f463de87650d9a9f00d433a06b886/981a2951e3fccc9ba81c501537ab818060069591c658c07fba6936fa5fd0dd27" "q-36911/ma-source-field/a4e2d59120f3312b1505a2fed52b1eed7f5f463de87650d9a9f00d433a06b886/464b9ac5ac22bfcc69adaf42253a8d7a5eef4a84e7c96c7715039d251f95788a"] :answer-field/correct "q-36911/ma-source-field/a4e2d59120f3312b1505a2fed52b1eed7f5f463de87650d9a9f00d433a06b886/aca3fb0d9ddb49350c290ac929c3cc1d4fe3619668acb3d7b8d6d89671359f83" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-36911" :question/id #uuid "7795ea1b-86ec-5a3d-baba-dbdd67574697" :question/math-academy-id "q-36911" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)+2(y-3)^{2}$, find the points $(x,y)$ where $∇f(x,y)=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)+2(y-3)^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}\\cdot 2x+0 \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+1} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+2(y-3)^{2}) \\\\  & =0+2\\cdot 2(y-3) \\\\  & =4(y-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $∇f(x,y)=\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,i+4(y-3)\\,j.$\n\nNow, we solve $∇f(x,y)=0:$ \n\n$$\n\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,i+4(y-3)\\,j=0\\text{ }i+0\\text{ }j\n$$\n\nSo, by equating the coefficients of $i$ and $j,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+1}=0 \\\\ 4(y-3)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get $x=0$ and from the second equation, we obtain $y=3.$ \n\nTherefore, $∇f(x,y)=0$ at the point $(0,3).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-36911/ma-source-field/a4e2d59120f3312b1505a2fed52b1eed7f5f463de87650d9a9f00d433a06b886"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e8d807a6-7896-5045-a14a-908b58831340"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-36911"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-37180/ma-source-field/46b2cfa9491114d88b804ad669fcbf2950ce5bc72fc4649eb8f7843dcfa60350/5f0a71d842ee5c32d48b20272af32a240f9b54f86154740c26f11f2bc83f53d7" :answer/id #uuid "451e0e4f-f1c3-5f2c-a984-6761ce64e2da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.5P-1\\,23,\\,P(0)=2\\,500" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37180/ma-source-field/46b2cfa9491114d88b804ad669fcbf2950ce5bc72fc4649eb8f7843dcfa60350/38d9b4a80e5c36380af5db5802ed305f28716ddc3b8e505e257a56860c5e8b5a" :answer/id #uuid "b3b512b5-d109-5b7f-afe6-8012cddf53df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dP}{dt}=12\\,510-18P,\\,P(0)=690" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37180/ma-source-field/46b2cfa9491114d88b804ad669fcbf2950ce5bc72fc4649eb8f7843dcfa60350/a34c654dcac9001f079ec25779eac0f8058d7e177e2ae93929dc4dcc6593bbe6" :answer/id #uuid "848a4d3c-7246-5b73-b528-cdd85bf23fbb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dP}{dt}=16\\,256-4P,\\,P(0)=4\\,070" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37180/ma-source-field/46b2cfa9491114d88b804ad669fcbf2950ce5bc72fc4649eb8f7843dcfa60350/8ddaaa3c22c182078534a19f8f7ed63f84d580d196766a60c493201bcad522d9" :answer/id #uuid "c372f938-bf0a-5da5-a0e8-947b58733787" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dP}{dt}=2\\,580-0.6P,\\,P(0)=4\\,400" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37180/ma-source-field/46b2cfa9491114d88b804ad669fcbf2950ce5bc72fc4649eb8f7843dcfa60350/68057005a1a5d1829183e2576095ff2c02215b574ddfcb08e8b9d3897f2d661f" :answer/id #uuid "30e14fdd-8b43-5b70-9434-f7996dbad376" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dP}{dt}=9P-6\\,066,\\,P(0)=680" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37180/ma-source-field/46b2cfa9491114d88b804ad669fcbf2950ce5bc72fc4649eb8f7843dcfa60350" :answer-field/id #uuid "f34c38b1-0c67-5df9-bd25-f72ef39097ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-37180/ma-source-field/46b2cfa9491114d88b804ad669fcbf2950ce5bc72fc4649eb8f7843dcfa60350/5f0a71d842ee5c32d48b20272af32a240f9b54f86154740c26f11f2bc83f53d7" "q-37180/ma-source-field/46b2cfa9491114d88b804ad669fcbf2950ce5bc72fc4649eb8f7843dcfa60350/38d9b4a80e5c36380af5db5802ed305f28716ddc3b8e505e257a56860c5e8b5a" "q-37180/ma-source-field/46b2cfa9491114d88b804ad669fcbf2950ce5bc72fc4649eb8f7843dcfa60350/a34c654dcac9001f079ec25779eac0f8058d7e177e2ae93929dc4dcc6593bbe6" "q-37180/ma-source-field/46b2cfa9491114d88b804ad669fcbf2950ce5bc72fc4649eb8f7843dcfa60350/8ddaaa3c22c182078534a19f8f7ed63f84d580d196766a60c493201bcad522d9" "q-37180/ma-source-field/46b2cfa9491114d88b804ad669fcbf2950ce5bc72fc4649eb8f7843dcfa60350/68057005a1a5d1829183e2576095ff2c02215b574ddfcb08e8b9d3897f2d661f"] :answer-field/correct "q-37180/ma-source-field/46b2cfa9491114d88b804ad669fcbf2950ce5bc72fc4649eb8f7843dcfa60350/38d9b4a80e5c36380af5db5802ed305f28716ddc3b8e505e257a56860c5e8b5a" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-37180" :question/id #uuid "6960a095-e760-5362-9086-48e7e2e653fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-37180" :question/problem "Which of the following initial value problems is an inhibited growth problem?" :question/worked-solution "An inhibited growth initial value problem has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=k(a-y),\\,y(0)={y}_{0}\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>y$ for all $t\\ge 0.$\n\nFrom the given options, the only inhibited growth problem is\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=12\\,510-18P,\\,P(0)=690,\n$$\n\nsince\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=12\\,510-18P=18(695-P).\n$$\n\nIn this case, $k=18,a=695,$ and ${y}_{0}=690.$ Notice that $a>{y}_{0},$ which is required for inhibited growth. \n\nThe other options do not represent inhibited growth. In particular, the initial value problems\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=16\\,256-4P=4(4\\,064-P),\\,P(0)=4\\,070,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=2\\,580-0.6P=0.6(4\\,300-P),\\,P(0)=4\\,400\n$$\n\ndo *not* represent an inhibited growth model because ${y}_{0}=4\\,070>a=4\\,064,$ and ${y}_{0}=4\\,400>a=4\\,300.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-37180/ma-source-field/46b2cfa9491114d88b804ad669fcbf2950ce5bc72fc4649eb8f7843dcfa60350"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ade69467-c229-509d-9bdc-b28935b2d1d8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-37180"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186125049 :question/answer-fields 17592186122864] {:db/id "q-37250/ma-source-field/be371bac7a0b427c6a256bb9ddc7b6cde62d9a98bf8ff917f763faac0d7e7b7d/a0b0c84f7474b29c632359c82fd91876fa5a80fc037da48c563f31aaa7ddc045" :answer/id #uuid "1dbfc55b-9986-5204-a717-051bef9ec970" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37250/ma-source-field/be371bac7a0b427c6a256bb9ddc7b6cde62d9a98bf8ff917f763faac0d7e7b7d/399a1171be63caa83f3b05773062d220261fc0ca32bc76ca944970d42ebede7b" :answer/id #uuid "fe222dc3-726c-55f2-a5d5-184f99572360" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37250/ma-source-field/be371bac7a0b427c6a256bb9ddc7b6cde62d9a98bf8ff917f763faac0d7e7b7d/074db705e16e1e57f8a2aff94b5fe57d6f39b7233e5e76f422f3f665da482360" :answer/id #uuid "c86e3f43-49a4-5b7f-9408-e35c02f28b65" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37250/ma-source-field/be371bac7a0b427c6a256bb9ddc7b6cde62d9a98bf8ff917f763faac0d7e7b7d/2510a3241ddb528e10e21b59d7837aa92aa4a577bbc545fb6b7d9214aa86bd40" :answer/id #uuid "e9db2e1f-0ee4-54d1-ae6f-0983601a839e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37250/ma-source-field/be371bac7a0b427c6a256bb9ddc7b6cde62d9a98bf8ff917f763faac0d7e7b7d/6bdca15713155dde1a913268225566fa646f0fe8ce116bb7b2dbbe92011c897b" :answer/id #uuid "ad98892c-f9b4-525c-8046-a410518643b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37250/ma-source-field/be371bac7a0b427c6a256bb9ddc7b6cde62d9a98bf8ff917f763faac0d7e7b7d" :answer-field/id #uuid "0b2a91b4-7ef6-5580-9c3e-14e555eca865" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-37250/ma-source-field/be371bac7a0b427c6a256bb9ddc7b6cde62d9a98bf8ff917f763faac0d7e7b7d/a0b0c84f7474b29c632359c82fd91876fa5a80fc037da48c563f31aaa7ddc045" "q-37250/ma-source-field/be371bac7a0b427c6a256bb9ddc7b6cde62d9a98bf8ff917f763faac0d7e7b7d/399a1171be63caa83f3b05773062d220261fc0ca32bc76ca944970d42ebede7b" "q-37250/ma-source-field/be371bac7a0b427c6a256bb9ddc7b6cde62d9a98bf8ff917f763faac0d7e7b7d/074db705e16e1e57f8a2aff94b5fe57d6f39b7233e5e76f422f3f665da482360" "q-37250/ma-source-field/be371bac7a0b427c6a256bb9ddc7b6cde62d9a98bf8ff917f763faac0d7e7b7d/2510a3241ddb528e10e21b59d7837aa92aa4a577bbc545fb6b7d9214aa86bd40" "q-37250/ma-source-field/be371bac7a0b427c6a256bb9ddc7b6cde62d9a98bf8ff917f763faac0d7e7b7d/6bdca15713155dde1a913268225566fa646f0fe8ce116bb7b2dbbe92011c897b"] :answer-field/correct "q-37250/ma-source-field/be371bac7a0b427c6a256bb9ddc7b6cde62d9a98bf8ff917f763faac0d7e7b7d/074db705e16e1e57f8a2aff94b5fe57d6f39b7233e5e76f422f3f665da482360" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "6b036f0f-ab37-53c9-a8c1-aa9fe52bf1e7"] :question/problem "Consider the following matrices:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,D=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,P=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & 1 & 1 \\\\ ∗ & 0 & 0 \\\\ ∗ & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nGiven that $D={P}^{-1}AP,$ find the first column of the matrix $P.$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagonal matrix $D$, we deduce that the eigenvalues of $A$ are \n\n$\\,$ ${\\lambda }_{1}=-1,\\,$ ${\\lambda }_{2}=1,\\,$ ${\\lambda }_{3}=3.$\n\nSo, the first column of $P$ corresponds to the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=-1.$\n\nNow, we need to find an eigenvector that corresponds to ${\\lambda }_{1}=-1.$ Computing $A-(-1)I,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-(-1)I & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}]-(-1)[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations with the augmented matrix $M$ that we reduce to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & -4 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}↔{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-\\frac{1}{3}){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has two pivot columns ($1$st and $2$nd). Thus, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we obtain ${x}_{2}={x}_{3}.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get ${x}_{1}={x}_{3}.$\nHence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting ${x}_{3}=1,$ we get the eigenvector \n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $P=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-37250/ma-source-field/be371bac7a0b427c6a256bb9ddc7b6cde62d9a98bf8ff917f763faac0d7e7b7d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186198951 :question/answer-fields 17592186197546] {:db/id "q-37701/ma-source-field/46e30dafca23b43876cc921e6109289f77d2f2326b4069f480f02aa881349062/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "d5cd5906-d8a2-5c66-aea8-20457b721c86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37701/ma-source-field/46e30dafca23b43876cc921e6109289f77d2f2326b4069f480f02aa881349062/abde0d57d9ac2e041e7dd4e9cfaa1838e326189442d77c6c65f1feb179cf1498" :answer/id #uuid "47e529a6-93ea-513d-8135-657ae263a7d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37701/ma-source-field/46e30dafca23b43876cc921e6109289f77d2f2326b4069f480f02aa881349062/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" :answer/id #uuid "549d228e-ff4d-5856-a054-7a41e02feaf7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37701/ma-source-field/46e30dafca23b43876cc921e6109289f77d2f2326b4069f480f02aa881349062/0064d374f806cba8ea43a11831d2980495c6733de7e909ec06431bd236f4f2b3" :answer/id #uuid "74fcf4d5-ab6d-50ee-8a97-7f767db1d054" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37701/ma-source-field/46e30dafca23b43876cc921e6109289f77d2f2326b4069f480f02aa881349062/c8cc0193c097b7d38e4091db7b8ea0b55b90f570b6dfeef91f6d5caca670d84e" :answer/id #uuid "5ac4715e-6ff4-560f-92e3-b1a7dcf09470" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37701/ma-source-field/46e30dafca23b43876cc921e6109289f77d2f2326b4069f480f02aa881349062" :answer-field/id #uuid "badca932-e160-50c7-80e4-3918dd2ca9d7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-37701/ma-source-field/46e30dafca23b43876cc921e6109289f77d2f2326b4069f480f02aa881349062/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-37701/ma-source-field/46e30dafca23b43876cc921e6109289f77d2f2326b4069f480f02aa881349062/abde0d57d9ac2e041e7dd4e9cfaa1838e326189442d77c6c65f1feb179cf1498" "q-37701/ma-source-field/46e30dafca23b43876cc921e6109289f77d2f2326b4069f480f02aa881349062/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" "q-37701/ma-source-field/46e30dafca23b43876cc921e6109289f77d2f2326b4069f480f02aa881349062/0064d374f806cba8ea43a11831d2980495c6733de7e909ec06431bd236f4f2b3" "q-37701/ma-source-field/46e30dafca23b43876cc921e6109289f77d2f2326b4069f480f02aa881349062/c8cc0193c097b7d38e4091db7b8ea0b55b90f570b6dfeef91f6d5caca670d84e"] :answer-field/correct "q-37701/ma-source-field/46e30dafca23b43876cc921e6109289f77d2f2326b4069f480f02aa881349062/abde0d57d9ac2e041e7dd4e9cfaa1838e326189442d77c6c65f1feb179cf1498" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "5440dc48-4c46-5737-826b-cf98fbacdffa"] :question/worked-solution "Let $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ be the measures of the angles of the triangle. We wish to maximize the function\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\operatorname{sin}⁡z,\n$$\n\nsubject to the constraint\n\n$$\nx+y+z=\\pi .\n$$\n\nNote that we also have the constraints $0<x,y,z<\\pi .$ \n\nLet $g(x,y,z)=x+y+z.$ Therefore, by the method of Lagrange multipliers, we must solve the following system:\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y,z)=\\lambda ∇g(x,y,z),\\,g(x,y,z)=\\pi \n$$\n\nWe start by solving the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\lambda ∇g(x,y,z) \\\\ ⟨{f}_{x}(x,y,z),{f}_{y}(x,y,z),{f}_{z}(x,y,z)⟩ & =\\lambda ⟨{g}_{x}(x,y,z),{g}_{y}(x,y,z),{g}_{z}(x,y,z)⟩ \\\\ ⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\operatorname{sin}⁡z,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\operatorname{sin}⁡z,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\operatorname{cos}⁡z⟩ & =\\lambda ⟨1,1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\operatorname{sin}⁡z=\\lambda  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\operatorname{sin}⁡z=\\lambda  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\operatorname{cos}⁡z=\\lambda \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first and second equations above, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\operatorname{sin}⁡z & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\operatorname{sin}⁡z \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\operatorname{sin}⁡z-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\operatorname{sin}⁡z & =0 \\\\ (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)\\operatorname{sin}⁡z & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(y-x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡z & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $0<z<\\pi ,$ we have that $\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\ne 0.$ On the other hand, if $y-x=\\pi \\cdot n,$ with $n$ an integer, we obtain that $x>\\pi $ or $y>\\pi ,$ which contradicts the constraints. Therefore, we can conclude that $x=y.$\n\nSimilarly, from the second and third equations, we get that $z=y=x.$ So, using the constraint equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y+z & =\\pi  \\\\ x+x+x & =\\pi  \\\\ 3x & =\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the maximum value of $f$ is reached at the point $(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3}),$ and the maximum value is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** It's easy to show that the obtained point is indeed the maximum (and not the minimum). To do that, we could compare the value of the function at this point with the value of the function at any other (arbitrary) point belonging to the domain. For example, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & <f(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-37701/ma-source-field/46e30dafca23b43876cc921e6109289f77d2f2326b4069f480f02aa881349062"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-37846/ma-source-field/d809a074c41dc0409abec96d379bea2339297729d60ea9f5e3f5e66a75391fb1/3c18e8dc6829c868136a882a333831910c94a82cbcf98128fd48c94767f8da39" :answer/id #uuid "aea3c10a-5a5b-5b56-ac38-0531c16322a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "D=[\\begin{aligned}-9 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37846/ma-source-field/d809a074c41dc0409abec96d379bea2339297729d60ea9f5e3f5e66a75391fb1/c876e58aef36217bdae1fbcbb1f0642503a63d46390e7a6e0752f271b6fa5fb7" :answer/id #uuid "842abd30-146b-5529-8174-62765bece360" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "D=[\\begin{aligned}-9 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37846/ma-source-field/d809a074c41dc0409abec96d379bea2339297729d60ea9f5e3f5e66a75391fb1/9ab2e50ba0ae37560fb1b9de01e383867a251e895196b122d2c3ba9f10667d7d" :answer/id #uuid "11ba3c2a-7e4a-5f75-b416-64d7e2c0bb58" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "D=[\\begin{aligned}-9 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37846/ma-source-field/d809a074c41dc0409abec96d379bea2339297729d60ea9f5e3f5e66a75391fb1/38afe3565f8d0326dd8d3c9f4616ed1d358bce4b7314bc02aee4958e15c65903" :answer/id #uuid "89f3e2af-1d0c-5ede-94d8-b2f1171885f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "D=[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37846/ma-source-field/d809a074c41dc0409abec96d379bea2339297729d60ea9f5e3f5e66a75391fb1/fde7c7e8c5c0e1280c4619c1897573fc8396a25055092e595f0052889d677717" :answer/id #uuid "a4e2d4db-4322-5304-a102-6991fb8129e3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ is not diagonalizable" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37846/ma-source-field/d809a074c41dc0409abec96d379bea2339297729d60ea9f5e3f5e66a75391fb1" :answer-field/id #uuid "72ff45fc-3165-5e0a-8ffa-750ac771413e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-37846/ma-source-field/d809a074c41dc0409abec96d379bea2339297729d60ea9f5e3f5e66a75391fb1/3c18e8dc6829c868136a882a333831910c94a82cbcf98128fd48c94767f8da39" "q-37846/ma-source-field/d809a074c41dc0409abec96d379bea2339297729d60ea9f5e3f5e66a75391fb1/c876e58aef36217bdae1fbcbb1f0642503a63d46390e7a6e0752f271b6fa5fb7" "q-37846/ma-source-field/d809a074c41dc0409abec96d379bea2339297729d60ea9f5e3f5e66a75391fb1/9ab2e50ba0ae37560fb1b9de01e383867a251e895196b122d2c3ba9f10667d7d" "q-37846/ma-source-field/d809a074c41dc0409abec96d379bea2339297729d60ea9f5e3f5e66a75391fb1/38afe3565f8d0326dd8d3c9f4616ed1d358bce4b7314bc02aee4958e15c65903" "q-37846/ma-source-field/d809a074c41dc0409abec96d379bea2339297729d60ea9f5e3f5e66a75391fb1/fde7c7e8c5c0e1280c4619c1897573fc8396a25055092e595f0052889d677717"] :answer-field/correct "q-37846/ma-source-field/d809a074c41dc0409abec96d379bea2339297729d60ea9f5e3f5e66a75391fb1/3c18e8dc6829c868136a882a333831910c94a82cbcf98128fd48c94767f8da39" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-37846" :question/id #uuid "21c29510-ffed-5744-82ad-55435a6f5d16" :question/math-academy-id "q-37846" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -9 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nDetermine whether $A=PD{P}^{-1}$ for some invertible matrix $P$ and a diagonal matrix $D,$ where $P$ and $D$ are both real. In the affirmative case, find a possible diagonal matrix $D.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to determine whether $D$ is diagonalizable over $R.$ \n\nWe start by computing the eigenvalues of $A.$ To do that, we solve the characteristic equation, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -9-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-9-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ 4 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-9-\\lambda )((1-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )-16) & =0 \\\\ (-9-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda -15) & =0 \\\\ (-9-\\lambda )(\\lambda +3)(\\lambda -5) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues of $A$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-9,\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-3$ and ${\\lambda }_{3}=5.$ Note that all $\\lambda $'s are simple roots of the characteristic polynomial.\n\nSince all of the eigenvalues are simple roots of the characteristic polynomial, $A$ is diagonalizable. \n\nWe construct a diagonal matrix $D$ by writing the eigenvalues in the main diagonal. Therefore, one possible matrix $D$ is\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}-9 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\,\\,-3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNote that the diagonal matrix $D$ is unique up to the ordering of the eigenvalues. Therefore, another possible diagonal matrix is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\,\\,-9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-37846/ma-source-field/d809a074c41dc0409abec96d379bea2339297729d60ea9f5e3f5e66a75391fb1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "05cb6509-dc1c-53b7-a495-4cfec2abdfe0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-37846"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-37959/ma-source-field/c2d15658d8bfa4dbccaeaccd0a148e0df706592dec474283987e4e3830a8836c/c9ec5d6cdf4e67c7f8bce68475bed400e56bf403f3d09b5928f78b6baa512eab" :answer/id #uuid "a8ffaf7b-87f0-5e5a-9948-e594f73a381c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "27" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37959/ma-source-field/c2d15658d8bfa4dbccaeaccd0a148e0df706592dec474283987e4e3830a8836c/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" :answer/id #uuid "887c1d3f-618f-5539-bd11-c056d0fb757f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37959/ma-source-field/c2d15658d8bfa4dbccaeaccd0a148e0df706592dec474283987e4e3830a8836c/cee37ae0a2921bd3973a5cb0592c822dbbfafcfefba8d7007910ead797b9112f" :answer/id #uuid "4e036078-2a13-5c04-aa70-916208c74b46" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "48" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37959/ma-source-field/c2d15658d8bfa4dbccaeaccd0a148e0df706592dec474283987e4e3830a8836c/d6944c4d51ee6e8916d5e2815a8478bad91a2f9e9e9bcd499b503b9fbcb165ab" :answer/id #uuid "0d6e9774-9622-56f0-879d-0c6a9f0675fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "54" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37959/ma-source-field/c2d15658d8bfa4dbccaeaccd0a148e0df706592dec474283987e4e3830a8836c/0674b229b15216f6ea870ccaaf87984357f5d6af66421aad0753c15d921d419a" :answer/id #uuid "3a12923a-fb30-547a-bfbe-786af7498fc6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "64" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37959/ma-source-field/c2d15658d8bfa4dbccaeaccd0a148e0df706592dec474283987e4e3830a8836c" :answer-field/id #uuid "7725e026-6e16-549e-8d1c-ac0a5575460e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-37959/ma-source-field/c2d15658d8bfa4dbccaeaccd0a148e0df706592dec474283987e4e3830a8836c/c9ec5d6cdf4e67c7f8bce68475bed400e56bf403f3d09b5928f78b6baa512eab" "q-37959/ma-source-field/c2d15658d8bfa4dbccaeaccd0a148e0df706592dec474283987e4e3830a8836c/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" "q-37959/ma-source-field/c2d15658d8bfa4dbccaeaccd0a148e0df706592dec474283987e4e3830a8836c/cee37ae0a2921bd3973a5cb0592c822dbbfafcfefba8d7007910ead797b9112f" "q-37959/ma-source-field/c2d15658d8bfa4dbccaeaccd0a148e0df706592dec474283987e4e3830a8836c/d6944c4d51ee6e8916d5e2815a8478bad91a2f9e9e9bcd499b503b9fbcb165ab" "q-37959/ma-source-field/c2d15658d8bfa4dbccaeaccd0a148e0df706592dec474283987e4e3830a8836c/0674b229b15216f6ea870ccaaf87984357f5d6af66421aad0753c15d921d419a"] :answer-field/correct "q-37959/ma-source-field/c2d15658d8bfa4dbccaeaccd0a148e0df706592dec474283987e4e3830a8836c/cee37ae0a2921bd3973a5cb0592c822dbbfafcfefba8d7007910ead797b9112f" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-37959" :question/id #uuid "b8d6d6ad-6f2f-560c-8794-1cc77ef79232" :question/math-academy-id "q-37959" :question/problem "Using the method of Lagrange multipliers, determine the minimum sum of the squares of three positive numbers whose sum is $12.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $x,y$, and $z$ be the three numbers. We wish to minimize the function\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2},\n$$\n\nsubject to the constraint \n\n$$\nx+y+z=12.\n$$\n\nNote that we also have the constraints $x>0,y>0,z>0.$\n\nLet $g(x,y,z)=x+y+z.$ Therefore, by the method of Lagrange multipliers, we must solve the following system:\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y,z)=\\lambda ∇g(x,y,z),\\,g(x,y,z)=12\n$$\n\nWe start by solving the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\lambda ∇g(x,y,z) \\\\ ⟨{f}_{x}(x,y,z),{f}_{y}(x,y,z),{f}_{z}(x,y,z)⟩ & =\\lambda ⟨{g}_{x}(x,y,z),{g}_{y}(x,y,z),{g}_{z}(x,y,z)⟩ \\\\ ⟨2x,2y,2z⟩ & =\\lambda ⟨1,1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x=\\lambda  \\\\ 2y=\\lambda  \\\\ 2z=\\lambda \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives $x=y=z.$ \n\nNow, using the constraint equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y+z & =12 \\\\ x+x+x & =12 \\\\ 3x & =12 \\\\ x & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the minimum value of $f$ is reached at the point $(4,4,4),$ and the minimum value is \n\n$$\nf(4,4,4)={4}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{4}^{2}=48.\n$$\n\n**Note:** It's easy to show that the obtained point is indeed the minimum (and not the maximum). To do that, we could compare the value of the function at this point with the value of the function at any other (arbitrary) point belonging to the domain. For example, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(5,5,2) & ={5}^{2}+{5}^{2}+{2}^{2} \\\\  & =54 \\\\  & >f(4,4,4).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-37959/ma-source-field/c2d15658d8bfa4dbccaeaccd0a148e0df706592dec474283987e4e3830a8836c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "849449fb-bb08-54a3-b8ea-9f33ddd7a3e5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-37959"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-38012/ma-source-field/d328ecd9381f2f32f2a132434ee9892e21ef9c9c1871cf57d462d6a1ef783a37/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer/id #uuid "1fd1ef26-855c-566b-b9a7-5c052f7787bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38012/ma-source-field/d328ecd9381f2f32f2a132434ee9892e21ef9c9c1871cf57d462d6a1ef783a37/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer/id #uuid "189ac4b0-ba2c-501e-8f95-bc84de29cfe0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38012/ma-source-field/d328ecd9381f2f32f2a132434ee9892e21ef9c9c1871cf57d462d6a1ef783a37/774940da4ab3b26727b8db6c1c90fb931ece0a7759ec47b6581e5af495721ce1" :answer/id #uuid "aeede097-4be9-58a3-86d7-462ab2d71c2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38012/ma-source-field/d328ecd9381f2f32f2a132434ee9892e21ef9c9c1871cf57d462d6a1ef783a37/2ebc133599183e5fdb5b6248a8ea00bdd0440ff336252ee383591a8699a758ca" :answer/id #uuid "1f36e9cc-aacc-5192-9693-90df97d5095f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38012/ma-source-field/d328ecd9381f2f32f2a132434ee9892e21ef9c9c1871cf57d462d6a1ef783a37/4b2b724bb83a84bbf9d414637c58251512548c01b9eccf5ed44c9d3fd1c3cc6b" :answer/id #uuid "fad570d2-bffe-52f4-9e6f-1b6feb83030c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Im}(T)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38012/ma-source-field/d328ecd9381f2f32f2a132434ee9892e21ef9c9c1871cf57d462d6a1ef783a37" :answer-field/id #uuid "ea905565-2ed7-50de-9d3c-01672c6f67a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-38012/ma-source-field/d328ecd9381f2f32f2a132434ee9892e21ef9c9c1871cf57d462d6a1ef783a37/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" "q-38012/ma-source-field/d328ecd9381f2f32f2a132434ee9892e21ef9c9c1871cf57d462d6a1ef783a37/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" "q-38012/ma-source-field/d328ecd9381f2f32f2a132434ee9892e21ef9c9c1871cf57d462d6a1ef783a37/774940da4ab3b26727b8db6c1c90fb931ece0a7759ec47b6581e5af495721ce1" "q-38012/ma-source-field/d328ecd9381f2f32f2a132434ee9892e21ef9c9c1871cf57d462d6a1ef783a37/2ebc133599183e5fdb5b6248a8ea00bdd0440ff336252ee383591a8699a758ca" "q-38012/ma-source-field/d328ecd9381f2f32f2a132434ee9892e21ef9c9c1871cf57d462d6a1ef783a37/4b2b724bb83a84bbf9d414637c58251512548c01b9eccf5ed44c9d3fd1c3cc6b"] :answer-field/correct "q-38012/ma-source-field/d328ecd9381f2f32f2a132434ee9892e21ef9c9c1871cf57d462d6a1ef783a37/4b2b724bb83a84bbf9d414637c58251512548c01b9eccf5ed44c9d3fd1c3cc6b" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-38012" :question/id #uuid "4809e77f-c615-585e-bbe9-4304896c33b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-38012" :question/problem "The linear transformation $T$ and the vector $b\\in {R}^{4}$ are given below. Determine if there exists a vector $x\\in {R}^{4}$ such that $T(x)=b.$\nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{4},$ where ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3},{x}_{4}$ are the components of $x.$  \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+2{x}_{4}+2{x}_{3} \\\\ 5{x}_{2}-7{x}_{4}-3{x}_{1}-{x}_{3} \\\\ 4{x}_{2}+{x}_{4}+5{x}_{3}+2{x}_{1} \\\\ -7{x}_{3}-{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-{x}_{4}\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write down the standard matrix of $T:$\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 5 & -1 & -7 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -7 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSince $T$ is the standard matix of $T,$ we have $\\text{Im}(T)=\\text{Col}(T).$ In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Im}(T),$ we need to check if the equation $Tx=b$ is consistent. \n\nSo, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[T\\,|\\,b]$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 5 & -1 & -7 & -8 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 5 & 1 & -9 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -7 & -1 & 10\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 1 & -3 & -15 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -5 & 1 & 13\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-3{R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -14 & 0 & -18 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 14\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the foruth equation, we get the false statement $0=14.$ Therefore, the system is inconsistent, and we conclude that  $b\\notin \\text{Im}(T).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-38012/ma-source-field/d328ecd9381f2f32f2a132434ee9892e21ef9c9c1871cf57d462d6a1ef783a37"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9a08e0a4-22c3-5139-848d-6f1027a61056"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-38012"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186176481 :question/answer-fields 17592186174994] {:db/id "q-38229/ma-source-field/8a232d69219d73f74b4c197045e9521474a3e0e1f1466b5437b802d8bbbcfcf5/228d7b42fcb34515143bb5c9b68cc81052255c360fff1053199a2147dbd7eb12" :answer/id #uuid "0108eb21-5320-5ff8-96d7-8f8de5fcef1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38229/ma-source-field/8a232d69219d73f74b4c197045e9521474a3e0e1f1466b5437b802d8bbbcfcf5/582cd71aeac5eafecb77c6f9f5c1bde2004ee7fc2a9336ab1f49a69e317721e8" :answer/id #uuid "bf907f2a-341b-5baa-a98d-8d7e0ddb910a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=3x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38229/ma-source-field/8a232d69219d73f74b4c197045e9521474a3e0e1f1466b5437b802d8bbbcfcf5/770e48394050f1cd126034e12257978ecdbe471bb38fa5fbc8c9558a9bfcb4f5" :answer/id #uuid "1cd9ad35-c837-57f3-ade6-3a3db7427a6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{3}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38229/ma-source-field/8a232d69219d73f74b4c197045e9521474a3e0e1f1466b5437b802d8bbbcfcf5/a20e462a24b2d65cab7429839bc46b524d25f7f1678fb82590234c6d14c4d796" :answer/id #uuid "e20ea794-ad35-5073-91ed-1a4d6170f723" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38229/ma-source-field/8a232d69219d73f74b4c197045e9521474a3e0e1f1466b5437b802d8bbbcfcf5/07d4d169afe54b72e6508fedd544e5d357fac0ff0f623249ab3b7f264f513fcf" :answer/id #uuid "a9fe1b78-433c-504f-a583-950509a9b7ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38229/ma-source-field/8a232d69219d73f74b4c197045e9521474a3e0e1f1466b5437b802d8bbbcfcf5" :answer-field/id #uuid "de87dec5-6939-5a03-ab02-65e0d9863a39" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-38229/ma-source-field/8a232d69219d73f74b4c197045e9521474a3e0e1f1466b5437b802d8bbbcfcf5/228d7b42fcb34515143bb5c9b68cc81052255c360fff1053199a2147dbd7eb12" "q-38229/ma-source-field/8a232d69219d73f74b4c197045e9521474a3e0e1f1466b5437b802d8bbbcfcf5/582cd71aeac5eafecb77c6f9f5c1bde2004ee7fc2a9336ab1f49a69e317721e8" "q-38229/ma-source-field/8a232d69219d73f74b4c197045e9521474a3e0e1f1466b5437b802d8bbbcfcf5/770e48394050f1cd126034e12257978ecdbe471bb38fa5fbc8c9558a9bfcb4f5" "q-38229/ma-source-field/8a232d69219d73f74b4c197045e9521474a3e0e1f1466b5437b802d8bbbcfcf5/a20e462a24b2d65cab7429839bc46b524d25f7f1678fb82590234c6d14c4d796" "q-38229/ma-source-field/8a232d69219d73f74b4c197045e9521474a3e0e1f1466b5437b802d8bbbcfcf5/07d4d169afe54b72e6508fedd544e5d357fac0ff0f623249ab3b7f264f513fcf"] :answer-field/correct "q-38229/ma-source-field/8a232d69219d73f74b4c197045e9521474a3e0e1f1466b5437b802d8bbbcfcf5/582cd71aeac5eafecb77c6f9f5c1bde2004ee7fc2a9336ab1f49a69e317721e8" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "326587d3-f0fa-5430-a120-481fbe187c4a"] :question/problem "Let\n$T=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}]$\nbe the standard matrix of the linear transformation $T.$ Then $T$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $T$ has proportional rows, and yet $T$ is not the zero matrix. \n\nTherefore, $\\text{rank}(T)=1$ and $T$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto a line that passes through the origin.\n\nMoreover, the line must pass through the origin $(0,0)$ and the points $(1,3)$ and $(2,6),$ which are defined by the columns of the matrix $T.$ \n\nComputing the slope $m$ of this line, we get\n\n$$\nm=\\frac{6-3}{2-1}=3.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $T$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto the line $y=3x.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-38229/ma-source-field/8a232d69219d73f74b4c197045e9521474a3e0e1f1466b5437b802d8bbbcfcf5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-39626/ma-source-field/4805d65090e2b846d7f311685a71feff8f4e65e42b49eec083daca20177e0eea/eddc584b31d4a80179e9498da1aeab49ea2c84f0426c04a753bb5632fe5ce44f" :answer/id #uuid "c93fce89-b164-5698-86ec-5e8583da03a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39626/ma-source-field/4805d65090e2b846d7f311685a71feff8f4e65e42b49eec083daca20177e0eea/15aa5158a63ae21ae09e9dece186da3669d10ceb90ec12310dde180f2a81dc1d" :answer/id #uuid "efe5e0de-876b-5327-9906-468b6bb4ce4e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39626/ma-source-field/4805d65090e2b846d7f311685a71feff8f4e65e42b49eec083daca20177e0eea/f64e376bfaa4d22b6756953610ba2f9d92564306c58ad1273f1969e8f73754ed" :answer/id #uuid "a82b517a-ad12-53fd-947a-2d5015a0fc1b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39626/ma-source-field/4805d65090e2b846d7f311685a71feff8f4e65e42b49eec083daca20177e0eea/abc22af8800e8889dc7c5b92858ee2d1c27d174c12815983f27101758b8c4dce" :answer/id #uuid "a0c0b411-9dec-5c9e-a4c7-e717d9fd0e54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39626/ma-source-field/4805d65090e2b846d7f311685a71feff8f4e65e42b49eec083daca20177e0eea/6dd2cfa7d7cbcbcc84bd5effc5fab4c9b8c1682b3bb21c80f7136001e3036c90" :answer/id #uuid "d6b5c424-dcd8-543b-8f0d-5fef2732067d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39626/ma-source-field/4805d65090e2b846d7f311685a71feff8f4e65e42b49eec083daca20177e0eea" :answer-field/id #uuid "d6e41552-50f9-524e-afed-203ff9c4cd4e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-39626/ma-source-field/4805d65090e2b846d7f311685a71feff8f4e65e42b49eec083daca20177e0eea/eddc584b31d4a80179e9498da1aeab49ea2c84f0426c04a753bb5632fe5ce44f" "q-39626/ma-source-field/4805d65090e2b846d7f311685a71feff8f4e65e42b49eec083daca20177e0eea/15aa5158a63ae21ae09e9dece186da3669d10ceb90ec12310dde180f2a81dc1d" "q-39626/ma-source-field/4805d65090e2b846d7f311685a71feff8f4e65e42b49eec083daca20177e0eea/f64e376bfaa4d22b6756953610ba2f9d92564306c58ad1273f1969e8f73754ed" "q-39626/ma-source-field/4805d65090e2b846d7f311685a71feff8f4e65e42b49eec083daca20177e0eea/abc22af8800e8889dc7c5b92858ee2d1c27d174c12815983f27101758b8c4dce" "q-39626/ma-source-field/4805d65090e2b846d7f311685a71feff8f4e65e42b49eec083daca20177e0eea/6dd2cfa7d7cbcbcc84bd5effc5fab4c9b8c1682b3bb21c80f7136001e3036c90"] :answer-field/correct "q-39626/ma-source-field/4805d65090e2b846d7f311685a71feff8f4e65e42b49eec083daca20177e0eea/eddc584b31d4a80179e9498da1aeab49ea2c84f0426c04a753bb5632fe5ce44f" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-39626" :question/id #uuid "43c590fa-d89b-58cd-94e7-3ff278816239" :question/math-academy-id "q-39626" :question/problem "Find a basis of ${H}^{⊥}$ if  $H=\\text{Span}{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}.$" :question/worked-solution "A vector $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$ belongs to ${H}^{⊥}$ if $x\\cdot {h}_{1}=0$ and $x\\cdot {h}_{2}=0.$ Therefore, we need to solve the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot {h}_{1}=0 \\\\ x\\cdot {h}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nwith the augmented matrix $M,$ which we reduce to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nIn the reduced matrix above, we have $2$ pivot columns (the $1$st and the $2$nd one), so ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. From the  second equation we get ${x}_{2}=0$ and then from the first equation we obtain  ${x}_{1}=-{x}_{3}.$ So, any vector in ${H}^{⊥}$ has the form \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$ is a basis of ${H}^{⊥}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-39626/ma-source-field/4805d65090e2b846d7f311685a71feff8f4e65e42b49eec083daca20177e0eea"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2b2f7e06-54f8-5a9b-a926-362fb087b59c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-39626"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-6529/ma-source-field/c984ec2f421096dd61cdf16192357b5f156ea9136f466e9cf522fe1cfaaec020/fb9543263a9223701b044b4df1253dbf56223b34eb1fa1274a3f985cff2b06f3" :answer/id #uuid "c2fca619-c21c-5cab-8f22-24ee4428c112" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\,628\\,800" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-6529/ma-source-field/c984ec2f421096dd61cdf16192357b5f156ea9136f466e9cf522fe1cfaaec020/7beb12bd99f915d23107fa2dba6779415d081f6e297561834593fef6323fdcfa" :answer/id #uuid "189d79b0-0941-5a64-9438-aab05bf6fa93" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\,628\\,820" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-6529/ma-source-field/c984ec2f421096dd61cdf