\\text{factor of the leading coefficient}}.\n$$\n\nFor the given polynomial $f(x),$ the constant term is $-3$ and the leading coefficient is $2.$ So, any rational roots of $f(x)$ must take the form\n\n$$\n\\pm \\frac{\\text{factor of }-3}{\\text{factor of }2}.\n$$\n\nOf the given answer choices, only $-\\frac{3}{2}$ takes the above form since the numerator $(3)$ is a factor of $-3$ and the denominator $(2)$ is a factor of $2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-6664/ma-source-field/8d930d297ed5be0282578fe372ebde2197efa929799a7be205c76b2134c7e5d8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82ccfef3-569a-5ddf-9a69-cae323a0a312"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-6664"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186083897 :question/answer-fields 17592186082283] {:db/id "q-6671/ma-source-field/968caa56e409c39e35cc6396b2590279c934e1ab600786ae8e2e8b047908f3a1/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "269d0de3-6a01-5def-89db-3dc958c2558c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-6671/ma-source-field/968caa56e409c39e35cc6396b2590279c934e1ab600786ae8e2e8b047908f3a1/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer/id #uuid "b5f49533-db03-5f90-9f04-b99e950b449d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-6671/ma-source-field/968caa56e409c39e35cc6396b2590279c934e1ab600786ae8e2e8b047908f3a1/e53026d2e72b5a9665afb169ba986753fff36dfc4557e460320cb8d9594cece8" :answer/id #uuid "093668c9-e9ba-5cdb-99a9-79d2c36efe70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-6671/ma-source-field/968caa56e409c39e35cc6396b2590279c934e1ab600786ae8e2e8b047908f3a1/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "bfd1cd6a-285c-548a-adba-d82870244265" :answer/type :answer.