ust take the form\n\n$$\n\\pm \\frac{\\text{factor of the constant term}}{\\text{factor of the leading coefficient}}.\n$$\n\nFor the given polynomial $f(x),$ the constant term is $-4$ and the leading coefficient is $4.$ So, any rational roots of $f(x)$ must take the form\n\n$$\n\\pm \\frac{\\text{factor of }-4}{\\text{factor of }4}.\n$$\n\nOf the given answer choices, only $-6$ does not take the above form. The value $-6$ can be interpreted as a fraction $-\\frac{6}{1},$ and the numerator $(6)$ is not a factor of $-4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-6671/ma-source-field/968caa56e409c39e35cc6396b2590279c934e1ab600786ae8e2e8b047908f3a1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-7210/ma-source-field/88a2ee9e795740613479062c53d3846094059eab66d1407477c1f4502df6558b/a1738f50832e9f1a958967d2b4fe72e7afef3705c5d7836cf9ee044a1c12e158" :answer/id #uuid "b7e2897f-2d72-56a4-bcc5-a06d675b471f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=\\frac{1}{15}\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7210/ma-source-field/88a2ee9e795740613479062c53d3846094059eab66d1407477c1f4502df6558b/bdf05d74b043d37ad021520c03b4dbdfca142f6230686583a32baa8674b5e3da" :answer/id #uuid "a134fc89-5f1c-5a05-9bfd-f3a9d2290923" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7210/ma-source-field/88a2ee9e795740613479062c53d3846094059eab66d1407477c1f4502df6558b/c2841ad9f7d635a6860e9899bf622c179609ffef3ee4db8d221ca7183fd4a1af" :answer/id #uuid "d372b5ec-aee8-50bb-8607-45719a03988b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=\\frac{3}{10}\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7210/ma-source-field/88a2ee9e795740613479062c53d3846094059eab66d1407477c1f4502df6558b/1ba79d8473e96d00f9a5880beeb1be1cd8a02ce48ee763b76594766294a918c4" :answer/id #uuid "7b7ecb47-348a-575c-b016-4544f1974784" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=\\frac{3}{5}\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7210/ma-source-field/88a2ee9e795740613479062c53d3846094059eab66d1407477c1f4502df6558b/c23cff141e546c99f6fa5e101b05cd60ca4888ceaa3a357e4466f827a5727784" :answer/id #uuid "89511689-d194-586c-b3c5-3518510b8c56" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=\\frac{5}{3}\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7210/ma-source-field/88a2ee9e795740613479062c53d3846094059eab66d1407477c1f4502df6558b" :answer-field/id #uuid "fead9c5f-966c-5594-b2e5-c190cdcde2f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-7210/ma-source-field/88a2ee9e795740613479062c53d3846094059eab66d1407477c1f4502df6558b/a1738f50832e9f1a958967d2b4fe72e7afef3705c5d7836cf9ee044a1c12e158" "q-7210/ma-source-field/88a2ee9e795740613479062c53d3846094059eab66d1407477c1f4502df6558b/bdf05d74b043d37ad021520c03b4dbdfca142f6230686583a32baa8674b5e3da" "q-7210/ma-source-field/88a2ee9e795740613479062c53d3846094059eab66d1407477c1f4502df6558b/c2841ad9f7d635a6860e9899bf622c179609ffef3ee4db8d221ca7183fd4a1af" "q-7210/ma-source-field/88a2ee9e795740613479062c53d3846094059eab66d1407477c1f4502df6558b/1ba79d8473e96d00f9a5880beeb1be1cd8a02ce48ee763b76594766294a918c4" "q-7210/ma-source-field/88a2ee9e795740613479062c53d3846094059eab66d1407477c1f4502df6558b/c23cff141e546c99f6fa5e101b05cd60ca4888ceaa3a357e4466f827a5727784"] :answer-field/correct "q-7210/ma-source-field/88a2ee9e795740613479062c53d3846094059eab66d1407477c1f4502df6558b/c23cff141e546c99f6fa5e101b05cd60ca4888ceaa3a357e4466f827a5727784" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-7210" :question/id #uuid "4cc9f66e-fd87-5f99-8445-a69528565ab3" :question/math-academy-id "q-7210" :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration, measured in $\\text{m}/{\\text{s}}^{2},$ given by the function $a(t)=\\sqrt{t}-{t}^{3/2}$, where $t>0$ is the time in seconds. If the particle has velocity $v=\\frac{4}{15}\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}$ when $t=1\\,\\text{s}$, determine the moment in time when the particle is stationary." :question/worked-solution "The particle is stationary when $v=0\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}.$\n\nFirst, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (\\sqrt{t}-{t}^{3/2})\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{t}^{3/2}-\\frac{2}{5}{t}^{5/2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(1)=\\frac{4}{15}.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{15} & =\\frac{2}{3}(1)^{3/2}-\\frac{2}{5}(1)^{5/2}+C \\\\ \\frac{4}{15} & =\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{2}{5}+C \\\\ \\frac{4}{15} & =\\frac{4}{15}+C \\\\ C & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity $v$ of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=\\frac{2}{3}{t}^{3/2}-\\frac{2}{5}{t}^{5/2}.$\n\nNow, we find the moments in time when $v=0\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}{t}^{3/2}-\\frac{2}{5}{t}^{5/2}=0 \\\\ \\frac{2}{5}{t}^{3/2}(\\frac{5}{3}-t) & =0 \\\\ t & =0,\\,\\frac{5}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $t>0$, the particle is stationary when $t=\\frac{5}{3}\\,\\text{s}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-7210/ma-source-field/88a2ee9e795740613479062c53d3846094059eab66d1407477c1f4502df6558b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c28b400d-9ec3-53c6-8e33-0133598ed143"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-7210"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-7945/ma-source-field/cc1bf3d8c5a402bd5a37453db5da3ca9e356af22982aebed03c7f3cfae65a57f/6ad07af0457fe965772f75854675049c88ddf4f0d74046124b969a43c76b0fa9" :answer/id #uuid "f263605b-a3cd-5db3-ab7d-ef1aab9f3dff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7945/ma-source-field/cc1bf3d8c5a402bd5a37453db5da3ca9e356af22982aebed03c7f3cfae65a57f/62d16cbc11fc3f331992e0fa2dcd4fc77397b11a7322a01369670623a145c604" :answer/id #uuid "8bcb109b-8e0c-537f-97bd-617cfaf0f544" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7945/ma-source-field/cc1bf3d8c5a402bd5a37453db5da3ca9e356af22982aebed03c7f3cfae65a57f/f4b0bde7e622028251a6c2ea276463a2b42cd9d9046540957de2b709a4c74920" :answer/id #uuid "8b77ea03-f99e-5649-8358-600824460ebc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7945/ma-source-field/cc1bf3d8c5a402bd5a37453db5da3ca9e356af22982aebed03c7f3cfae65a57f/3760ca40e03299ea9a0636e2b997169f0c9cd80c67acea57b5a54f16344e8bf4" :answer/id #uuid "306a57a1-c90d-5377-92c1-ce8a4090bf78" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7945/ma-source-field/cc1bf3d8c5a402bd5a37453db5da3ca9e356af22982aebed03c7f3cfae65a57f/935aa158fd2c399ea2cda88ceb19dd30c987a40c650abf8e1a4e9380b623f35e" :answer/id #uuid "236f7032-923a-5882-b067-96dd10890441" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7945/ma-source-field/cc1bf3d8c5a402bd5a37453db5da3ca9e356af22982aebed03c7f3cfae65a57f" :answer-field/id #uuid "aedcf9db-ed57-5dd9-8b52-eb742bee0864" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-7945/ma-source-field/cc1bf3d8c5a402bd5a37453db5da3ca9e356af22982aebed03c7f3cfae65a57f/6ad07af0457fe965772f75854675049c88ddf4f0d74046124b969a43c76b0fa9" "q-7945/ma-source-field/cc1bf3d8c5a402bd5a37453db5da3ca9e356af22982aebed03c7f3cfae65a57f/62d16cbc11fc3f331992e0fa2dcd4fc77397b11a7322a01369670623a145c604" "q-7945/ma-source-field/cc1bf3d8c5a402bd5a37453db5da3ca9e356af22982aebed03c7f3cfae65a57f/f4b0bde7e622028251a6c2ea276463a2b42cd9d9046540957de2b709a4c74920" "q-7945/ma-source-field/cc1bf3d8c5a402bd5a37453db5da3ca9e356af22982aebed03c7f3cfae65a57f/3760ca40e03299ea9a0636e2b997169f0c9cd80c67acea57b5a54f16344e8bf4" "q-7945/ma-source-field/cc1bf3d8c5a402bd5a37453db5da3ca9e356af22982aebed03c7f3cfae65a57f/935aa158fd2c399ea2cda88ceb19dd30c987a40c650abf8e1a4e9380b623f35e"] :answer-field/correct "q-7945/ma-source-field/cc1bf3d8c5a402bd5a37453db5da3ca9e356af22982aebed03c7f3cfae65a57f/6ad07af0457fe965772f75854675049c88ddf4f0d74046124b969a43c76b0fa9" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-7945" :question/id #uuid "e922303e-f1e5-5b8d-b2da-04cdac58e3ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-7945" :question/problem "Calculate ${Q}^{-1}$, where\n$Q=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Given a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\nQ=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe inverse of $Q$ can be found using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Q}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(Q)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the determinant:\n\n$$\ndet(Q)=(-3)\\cdot (-2)-5\\cdot 1=1\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, then, the inverse is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Q}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(Q)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can verify the result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q{Q}^{-1} & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓ \\\\ {Q}^{-1}Q & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-7945/ma-source-field/cc1bf3d8c5a402bd5a37453db5da3ca9e356af22982aebed03c7f3cfae65a57f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bea23649-e835-540a-b238-7b89ed330cd3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-7945"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186088385 :question/answer-fields 17592186086933] {:db/id "q-8005/ma-source-field/f281d1d76b77551afb40ede7a71403b2a1734493c7d841c95e4b14deb413822f/2129cb262d4b6f13839338907d08edeb4924afb9ddd32580db2ae6ecdb27a09f" :answer/id #uuid "c1fa6e68-6023-531a-88de-a62dd4b4692b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(5,\\pm 12)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8005/ma-source-field/f281d1d76b77551afb40ede7a71403b2a1734493c7d841c95e4b14deb413822f/1e75cf98e16f847b2e29e1edc0cfee2d00c876319b78d0a3bf8a025d9b63b57f" :answer/id #uuid "fd6983c6-2a3a-5a74-9155-3140c3b16817" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(5,\\pm \\frac{3}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8005/ma-source-field/f281d1d76b77551afb40ede7a71403b2a1734493c7d841c95e4b14deb413822f/d1455ca56dc137e03442e2c503d04f3d9707c3a68234481a15645d0aa5acb667" :answer/id #uuid "c143c2b9-589b-5044-8878-4be12b83a9e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(5,\\pm \\frac{3}{4})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8005/ma-source-field/f281d1d76b77551afb40ede7a71403b2a1734493c7d841c95e4b14deb413822f/e9b8c15c8743e385f38cd6b538b549f01607ebd648c1eeef93f747cd3b9e2c42" :answer/id #uuid "6792e8d3-e7b8-5579-b7f7-7456877be5f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(5,\\pm \\frac{9}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8005/ma-source-field/f281d1d76b77551afb40ede7a71403b2a1734493c7d841c95e4b14deb413822f/872aa5cf77671853e4b1d8b77e16a95a2fb44f1632ad20f36a9d05f683bcd5b4" :answer/id #uuid "065f5013-a6a4-59df-9c2e-0ed50e4f3f57" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(5,\\pm \\frac{9}{4})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8005/ma-source-field/f281d1d76b77551afb40ede7a71403b2a1734493c7d841c95e4b14deb413822f" :answer-field/id #uuid "3572ea5b-ba63-553c-87ba-5e4b8e0f9213" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-8005/ma-source-field/f281d1d76b77551afb40ede7a71403b2a1734493c7d841c95e4b14deb413822f/2129cb262d4b6f13839338907d08edeb4924afb9ddd32580db2ae6ecdb27a09f" "q-8005/ma-source-field/f281d1d76b77551afb40ede7a71403b2a1734493c7d841c95e4b14deb413822f/1e75cf98e16f847b2e29e1edc0cfee2d00c876319b78d0a3bf8a025d9b63b57f" "q-8005/ma-source-field/f281d1d76b77551afb40ede7a71403b2a1734493c7d841c95e4b14deb413822f/d1455ca56dc137e03442e2c503d04f3d9707c3a68234481a15645d0aa5acb667" "q-8005/ma-source-field/f281d1d76b77551afb40ede7a71403b2a1734493c7d841c95e4b14deb413822f/e9b8c15c8743e385f38cd6b538b549f01607ebd648c1eeef93f747cd3b9e2c42" "q-8005/ma-source-field/f281d1d76b77551afb40ede7a71403b2a1734493c7d841c95e4b14deb413822f/872aa5cf77671853e4b1d8b77e16a95a2fb44f1632ad20f36a9d05f683bcd5b4"] :answer-field/correct "q-8005/ma-source-field/f281d1d76b77551afb40ede7a71403b2a1734493c7d841c95e4b14deb413822f/872aa5cf77671853e4b1d8b77e16a95a2fb44f1632ad20f36a9d05f683bcd5b4" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "2125dbf2-368d-5ee6-b919-9a772694e1b8"] :question/problem "Calculate the points where the hyperbola $9{x}^{2}-16{y}^{2}=144$ intersects the line $x=5.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $x=5,$ we substitute $x=5$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{x}^{2}-16{y}^{2} & =144 \\\\ 9(5)^{2}-16{y}^{2} & =144 \\\\ -16{y}^{2} & =144-225 \\\\ -16{y}^{2} & =-81 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =\\frac{81}{16} \\\\ y & =\\pm \\frac{9}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the hyperbola intersects the vertical line $x=5$ at the points $(5,\\pm \\frac{9}{4}).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-8005/ma-source-field/f281d1d76b77551afb40ede7a71403b2a1734493c7d841c95e4b14deb413822f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186088443 :question/answer-fields 17592186087281] {:db/id "q-8739/ma-source-field/7419184d52652888cdc7cc1388be9d8b3cf71198a28886b6129d06c39c5e3860/b519682a75292841123b1ce86787b5dd662b4e6b965927abc60e62d4d2ac6445" :answer/id #uuid "f65a218e-09b9-5f93-833d-5222a9ab1b89" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2xy}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8739/ma-source-field/7419184d52652888cdc7cc1388be9d8b3cf71198a28886b6129d06c39c5e3860/a72d21a1579be0fdb4bec5abc0dc8fcb32bb41c1a1bee11c06599214d2b84bdc" :answer/id #uuid "02b3bcfe-b179-54e6-9f39-7cf2b8a2012c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{xy}{x+y}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8739/ma-source-field/7419184d52652888cdc7cc1388be9d8b3cf71198a28886b6129d06c39c5e3860/56a068f02350856ca7ac3f66446175a5b3f2d91253091b460dd68fba21dcc4cf" :answer/id #uuid "6836dad2-0a5e-566e-82e6-ae2f1e00252c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8739/ma-source-field/7419184d52652888cdc7cc1388be9d8b3cf71198a28886b6129d06c39c5e3860/ba9d43db73e4f2cfe3e32b6186859d177645f131d0b625e271148c55051c7968" :answer/id #uuid "9438294d-1900-5c07-88ff-915745bfe633" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{x}^{2}y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8739/ma-source-field/7419184d52652888cdc7cc1388be9d8b3cf71198a28886b6129d06c39c5e3860/a7d7ae98171b9fc15c0827f68d7626f47c86f74cf79c2d78e25272ce25ba964c" :answer/id #uuid "501f1379-0915-537f-a01b-ac50f840b151" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8739/ma-source-field/7419184d52652888cdc7cc1388be9d8b3cf71198a28886b6129d06c39c5e3860" :answer-field/id #uuid "f23bfdfe-607b-5b9b-8499-14f49fb7f966" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-8739/ma-source-field/7419184d52652888cdc7cc1388be9d8b3cf71198a28886b6129d06c39c5e3860/b519682a75292841123b1ce86787b5dd662b4e6b965927abc60e62d4d2ac6445" "q-8739/ma-source-field/7419184d52652888cdc7cc1388be9d8b3cf71198a28886b6129d06c39c5e3860/a72d21a1579be0fdb4bec5abc0dc8fcb32bb41c1a1bee11c06599214d2b84bdc" "q-8739/ma-source-field/7419184d52652888cdc7cc1388be9d8b3cf71198a28886b6129d06c39c5e3860/56a068f02350856ca7ac3f66446175a5b3f2d91253091b460dd68fba21dcc4cf" "q-8739/ma-source-field/7419184d52652888cdc7cc1388be9d8b3cf71198a28886b6129d06c39c5e3860/ba9d43db73e4f2cfe3e32b6186859d177645f131d0b625e271148c55051c7968" "q-8739/ma-source-field/7419184d52652888cdc7cc1388be9d8b3cf71198a28886b6129d06c39c5e3860/a7d7ae98171b9fc15c0827f68d7626f47c86f74cf79c2d78e25272ce25ba964c"] :answer-field/correct "q-8739/ma-source-field/7419184d52652888cdc7cc1388be9d8b3cf71198a28886b6129d06c39c5e3860/b519682a75292841123b1ce86787b5dd662b4e6b965927abc60e62d4d2ac6445" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "32964a8b-4376-5c16-9f30-00e530a869bb"] :question/worked-solution "A first-order ordinary differential equation that is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y)\n$$\n\nis said to be homogeneous if it satisfies the following property:\n\n$$\nf(tx,ty)=f(x,y)\\,\n$$\n\nThe only option in which this is the case is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2xy}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nWe can check this using one of two methods.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nLet $f(x,y)=\\frac{2xy}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.$\n\nWe see that both the numerator and denominator are homogeneous polynomials of degree $2.$ Therefore, $f(x,y)$ is a homogeneous function of degree $2-2=0.$\n\nHence, the original differential equation is homogeneous.\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo check this in detail using the definition, we first write:\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\frac{2xy}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\n$$\n\nWe can check that this is homogeneous showing that $f(tx,ty)=f(x,y),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(tx,ty) & =\\frac{2(tx)(ty)}{(tx)^{2}+(ty)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{2}\\cdot 2xy}{{t}^{2}{x}^{2}+{t}^{2}{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\text{ }\\frac{{t}^{2}\\cdot 2xy}{{t}^{2}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2xy}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f(tx,ty)=f(x,y),$ the original differential equation is homogeneous." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-8739/ma-source-field/7419184d52652888cdc7cc1388be9d8b3cf71198a28886b6129d06c39c5e3860"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-9455/ma-source-field/e1df2a8454b5db1c426e40647ede9e07ae262d0a6898670ae0af63256b29c06e/abc4e01626eb87b45206b4cbe5fadc3db03bb1c6e9e7425dea4cb5a219c87fae" :answer/id #uuid "69c7f2cb-d61b-5cdc-861e-23298cb144fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-1,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9455/ma-source-field/e1df2a8454b5db1c426e40647ede9e07ae262d0a6898670ae0af63256b29c06e/f8f5c5c5a92e426c4a187ab875cfbbfb5810b5f5d8cbecd52ddcec8ce5053ecb" :answer/id #uuid "28a44386-df41-518f-8ae9-cef9716a3c9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-2,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9455/ma-source-field/e1df2a8454b5db1c426e40647ede9e07ae262d0a6898670ae0af63256b29c06e/ff992f3bfbf9256bb8a93ba4418b1d3fc4bf7775122685039de83403d09a1dca" :answer/id #uuid "5d5b9915-2978-596b-92f1-cfabfd14d751" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9455/ma-source-field/e1df2a8454b5db1c426e40647ede9e07ae262d0a6898670ae0af63256b29c06e/91d27013c76788268e2e33b95f23b5af7cdbb49f9e629538a767340569105ede" :answer/id #uuid "dbcb670c-d405-5c08-9091-71944243229a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9455/ma-source-field/e1df2a8454b5db1c426e40647ede9e07ae262d0a6898670ae0af63256b29c06e/981a2951e3fccc9ba81c501537ab818060069591c658c07fba6936fa5fd0dd27" :answer/id #uuid "f534141f-98d2-518e-8d13-f38f36b9c409" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(3,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9455/ma-source-field/e1df2a8454b5db1c426e40647ede9e07ae262d0a6898670ae0af63256b29c06e" :answer-field/id #uuid "8b632b56-6e53-5e1f-878e-88fefa9697ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-9455/ma-source-field/e1df2a8454b5db1c426e40647ede9e07ae262d0a6898670ae0af63256b29c06e/abc4e01626eb87b45206b4cbe5fadc3db03bb1c6e9e7425dea4cb5a219c87fae" "q-9455/ma-source-field/e1df2a8454b5db1c426e40647ede9e07ae262d0a6898670ae0af63256b29c06e/f8f5c5c5a92e426c4a187ab875cfbbfb5810b5f5d8cbecd52ddcec8ce5053ecb" "q-9455/ma-source-field/e1df2a8454b5db1c426e40647ede9e07ae262d0a6898670ae0af63256b29c06e/ff992f3bfbf9256bb8a93ba4418b1d3fc4bf7775122685039de83403d09a1dca" "q-9455/ma-source-field/e1df2a8454b5db1c426e40647ede9e07ae262d0a6898670ae0af63256b29c06e/91d27013c76788268e2e33b95f23b5af7cdbb49f9e629538a767340569105ede" "q-9455/ma-source-field/e1df2a8454b5db1c426e40647ede9e07ae262d0a6898670ae0af63256b29c06e/981a2951e3fccc9ba81c501537ab818060069591c658c07fba6936fa5fd0dd27"] :answer-field/correct "q-9455/ma-source-field/e1df2a8454b5db1c426e40647ede9e07ae262d0a6898670ae0af63256b29c06e/ff992f3bfbf9256bb8a93ba4418b1d3fc4bf7775122685039de83403d09a1dca" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-9455" :question/id #uuid "ede784c5-2ada-5719-b4c5-5216ffbee9f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-9455" :question/problem "Calculate the point where the ellipse $\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}=1$ intercepts the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "To calculate the $x$-intercept, we need to substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the ellipse and solve the resulting equation for $x.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{(0-3)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{9}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{3}+1 & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{3} & =0 \\\\ (x-1)^{2} & =0 \\\\ x-1 & =0 \\\\ x & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ellipse intercepts the $x$-axis at $(1,0).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-9455/ma-source-field/e1df2a8454b5db1c426e40647ede9e07ae262d0a6898670ae0af63256b29c06e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74a508c1-2379-590f-85f5-386a1990f137"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-9455"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-9463/ma-source-field/8d1daa471e098d7afa517ac1edf7b98bad440c690beb2e61bf49fbaf7a293c89/6044746d81a998f29c58985dbf134c104c838c50c710fbac3b136834478dc847" :answer/id #uuid "0f343484-a699-582b-93b6-8580ce102cad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9463/ma-source-field/8d1daa471e098d7afa517ac1edf7b98bad440c690beb2e61bf49fbaf7a293c89/ff54de989731767e89ed471a3eb4118cafc39b059c87b75411d559c5f8b9e6d5" :answer/id #uuid "755a9ebe-6c9e-5651-a4a6-444f42e9a0c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,-2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9463/ma-source-field/8d1daa471e098d7afa517ac1edf7b98bad440c690beb2e61bf49fbaf7a293c89/f30fb0f59fafb6752d784950cc322d7f2032f94280c61093320bd35b48f74686" :answer/id #uuid "607ea23b-094c-5908-a370-4bdf12579651" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,-3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9463/ma-source-field/8d1daa471e098d7afa517ac1edf7b98bad440c690beb2e61bf49fbaf7a293c89/85cb4fac0396602d43dca2c00e3ca71b29816b8e6c6a13d1cfa7f3ced25f7b78" :answer/id #uuid "e924fddc-0dc6-5ba8-acd9-24bab71e7fce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9463/ma-source-field/8d1daa471e098d7afa517ac1edf7b98bad440c690beb2e61bf49fbaf7a293c89/aca3fb0d9ddb49350c290ac929c3cc1d4fe3619668acb3d7b8d6d89671359f83" :answer/id #uuid "94835f02-7621-51ce-954d-340cd9791c06" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9463/ma-source-field/8d1daa471e098d7afa517ac1edf7b98bad440c690beb2e61bf49fbaf7a293c89" :answer-field/id #uuid "cb7e3acc-02eb-5c66-99aa-f399d8802e22" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-9463/ma-source-field/8d1daa471e098d7afa517ac1edf7b98bad440c690beb2e61bf49fbaf7a293c89/6044746d81a998f29c58985dbf134c104c838c50c710fbac3b136834478dc847" "q-9463/ma-source-field/8d1daa471e098d7afa517ac1edf7b98bad440c690beb2e61bf49fbaf7a293c89/ff54de989731767e89ed471a3eb4118cafc39b059c87b75411d559c5f8b9e6d5" "q-9463/ma-source-field/8d1daa471e098d7afa517ac1edf7b98bad440c690beb2e61bf49fbaf7a293c89/f30fb0f59fafb6752d784950cc322d7f2032f94280c61093320bd35b48f74686" "q-9463/ma-source-field/8d1daa471e098d7afa517ac1edf7b98bad440c690beb2e61bf49fbaf7a293c89/85cb4fac0396602d43dca2c00e3ca71b29816b8e6c6a13d1cfa7f3ced25f7b78" "q-9463/ma-source-field/8d1daa471e098d7afa517ac1edf7b98bad440c690beb2e61bf49fbaf7a293c89/aca3fb0d9ddb49350c290ac929c3cc1d4fe3619668acb3d7b8d6d89671359f83"] :answer-field/correct "q-9463/ma-source-field/8d1daa471e098d7afa517ac1edf7b98bad440c690beb2e61bf49fbaf7a293c89/ff54de989731767e89ed471a3eb4118cafc39b059c87b75411d559c5f8b9e6d5" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-9463" :question/id #uuid "a595f2ed-1b5a-5c72-8ee3-ba4dbc0311ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-9463" :question/problem "Calculate the point where the ellipse $\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{4}=1$ intercepts the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "To calculate the $y$-intercept, we need to substitute $x=0$ in the equation of the ellipse and solve the resulting equation for $y.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(0+3)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{9}{9}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ 1+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{4} & =0 \\\\ (y+2)^{2} & =0 \\\\ y+2 & =0 \\\\ y & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ellipse intercepts the $y$-axis at the point $(0,-2).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-9463/ma-source-field/8d1daa471e098d7afa517ac1edf7b98bad440c690beb2e61bf49fbaf7a293c89"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a57ec9ff-99fd-5a3d-9a89-e76ded9d01cb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-9463"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-10485/ma-source-field/9f26ccb9963c0e6bd54a02d27819834c749c008051900e0b3ad57f6af8296f21/0be40a41fff2075dcd7ae30d0e6284ddf7b2ec7e519882e4636a79e6edbe7cee" :answer/id #uuid "5420a5d8-e27c-54cd-8d4a-8807ed506a3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\pm 2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10485/ma-source-field/9f26ccb9963c0e6bd54a02d27819834c749c008051900e0b3ad57f6af8296f21/7f44eea92af5c9acdec8919ce008f32aaa724d76d416ab5243173911577f9642" :answer/id #uuid "7aae46ab-d345-5f44-b157-efc8fa3bed1b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\pm 3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10485/ma-source-field/9f26ccb9963c0e6bd54a02d27819834c749c008051900e0b3ad57f6af8296f21/2d72fb9577d14e692ee0c494e42dfc349f511e1def3de9a4ad7e2ebebd23a09a" :answer/id #uuid "b3896d35-3d39-5b8b-8500-59d135ad3570" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\pm 4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10485/ma-source-field/9f26ccb9963c0e6bd54a02d27819834c749c008051900e0b3ad57f6af8296f21/73626b9872a8e0d9a206aee09c0a6f81b943d849a126e247740edbf6c67b430a" :answer/id #uuid "54e5febe-e5c5-53fd-b8eb-4a5c7c0dad20" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\pm 9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10485/ma-source-field/9f26ccb9963c0e6bd54a02d27819834c749c008051900e0b3ad57f6af8296f21/4aeeff6d6e23b3e6c864fe16bbdcb96d8a4485d83a90b65be5cee6551d2f4ec7" :answer/id #uuid "6a6fdac5-53dc-5a87-9dff-5c99baea1ce1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "There are no points of intersection" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10485/ma-source-field/9f26ccb9963c0e6bd54a02d27819834c749c008051900e0b3ad57f6af8296f21" :answer-field/id #uuid "703485af-d39d-5b69-a26a-bac078d2ad7f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-10485/ma-source-field/9f26ccb9963c0e6bd54a02d27819834c749c008051900e0b3ad57f6af8296f21/0be40a41fff2075dcd7ae30d0e6284ddf7b2ec7e519882e4636a79e6edbe7cee" "q-10485/ma-source-field/9f26ccb9963c0e6bd54a02d27819834c749c008051900e0b3ad57f6af8296f21/7f44eea92af5c9acdec8919ce008f32aaa724d76d416ab5243173911577f9642" "q-10485/ma-source-field/9f26ccb9963c0e6bd54a02d27819834c749c008051900e0b3ad57f6af8296f21/2d72fb9577d14e692ee0c494e42dfc349f511e1def3de9a4ad7e2ebebd23a09a" "q-10485/ma-source-field/9f26ccb9963c0e6bd54a02d27819834c749c008051900e0b3ad57f6af8296f21/73626b9872a8e0d9a206aee09c0a6f81b943d849a126e247740edbf6c67b430a" "q-10485/ma-source-field/9f26ccb9963c0e6bd54a02d27819834c749c008051900e0b3ad57f6af8296f21/4aeeff6d6e23b3e6c864fe16bbdcb96d8a4485d83a90b65be5cee6551d2f4ec7"] :answer-field/correct "q-10485/ma-source-field/9f26ccb9963c0e6bd54a02d27819834c749c008051900e0b3ad57f6af8296f21/4aeeff6d6e23b3e6c864fe16bbdcb96d8a4485d83a90b65be5cee6551d2f4ec7" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-10485" :question/id #uuid "296c1691-3fdb-50aa-926f-7c3fb307cb51" :question/math-academy-id "q-10485" :question/problem "Calculate the $x$-coordinates of the points where the hyperbola $\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}=1$ intersects the line $y=x.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=x,$ we first replace $y$ with $x$ in the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{4{x}^{2}}{36}-\\frac{9{x}^{2}}{36} & =1 \\\\ -\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{36} & =1 \\\\ 5{x}^{2} & =-36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe cannot take the square root of a negative number. Therefore, the equation has no real solutions. So, the hyperbola does not intersect the line $y=x.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-10485/ma-source-field/9f26ccb9963c0e6bd54a02d27819834c749c008051900e0b3ad57f6af8296f21"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55a53010-eddc-5115-8c70-0f32d0144384"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-10485"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-10662/ma-source-field/cb667763d3551ccb3c36e9aa55347327bfaf4895f2b3af2aa2ebc6cb7808f259/d12f3eab7d014ee6f62ea4da45400f845bf25815fe269402d40f5fc15bd06428" :answer/id #uuid "3bac1b8f-a5a2-5c6f-9f74-53d3dc54a0d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1-3y \\\\ y \\\\ 2+y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10662/ma-source-field/cb667763d3551ccb3c36e9aa55347327bfaf4895f2b3af2aa2ebc6cb7808f259/d65ee32cb9ad4f9d7490e948b14ec725cd5e1cf9dfca19e9f928a9daa3a6ae32" :answer/id #uuid "ca74fa9e-2937-5e51-b664-ed9cfa05d409" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2-y-z \\\\ 1+z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10662/ma-source-field/cb667763d3551ccb3c36e9aa55347327bfaf4895f2b3af2aa2ebc6cb7808f259/2ad9c8488680f9b40b0e98054bf263394b4ffeda8666caa2f4b04facb70acbe8" :answer/id #uuid "6ffe24a8-fe0e-5039-81c0-fb9631f878a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2-y-z \\\\ 4-z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10662/ma-source-field/cb667763d3551ccb3c36e9aa55347327bfaf4895f2b3af2aa2ebc6cb7808f259/4be504387d90d8d79cc479bc793620480c6b0b6565c5111a96aa6fd6e85aee1a" :answer/id #uuid "30c4ec68-4b39-55b5-8e7c-bbe84a2b4057" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3y \\\\ y \\\\ 4y-1\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10662/ma-source-field/cb667763d3551ccb3c36e9aa55347327bfaf4895f2b3af2aa2ebc6cb7808f259/6d6811ceb4fb69a54ce1b24e6804e5f0148bafa1b76b847b06436eb966d36b67" :answer/id #uuid "bc323d4c-6ab9-5df2-881f-281eabd5b981" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No solution" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10662/ma-source-field/cb667763d3551ccb3c36e9aa55347327bfaf4895f2b3af2aa2ebc6cb7808f259" :answer-field/id #uuid "2f5eaa46-bf95-53b6-ace1-3bd33b1c4991" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-10662/ma-source-field/cb667763d3551ccb3c36e9aa55347327bfaf4895f2b3af2aa2ebc6cb7808f259/d12f3eab7d014ee6f62ea4da45400f845bf25815fe269402d40f5fc15bd06428" "q-10662/ma-source-field/cb667763d3551ccb3c36e9aa55347327bfaf4895f2b3af2aa2ebc6cb7808f259/d65ee32cb9ad4f9d7490e948b14ec725cd5e1cf9dfca19e9f928a9daa3a6ae32" "q-10662/ma-source-field/cb667763d3551ccb3c36e9aa55347327bfaf4895f2b3af2aa2ebc6cb7808f259/2ad9c8488680f9b40b0e98054bf263394b4ffeda8666caa2f4b04facb70acbe8" "q-10662/ma-source-field/cb667763d3551ccb3c36e9aa55347327bfaf4895f2b3af2aa2ebc6cb7808f259/4be504387d90d8d79cc479bc793620480c6b0b6565c5111a96aa6fd6e85aee1a" "q-10662/ma-source-field/cb667763d3551ccb3c36e9aa55347327bfaf4895f2b3af2aa2ebc6cb7808f259/6d6811ceb4fb69a54ce1b24e6804e5f0148bafa1b76b847b06436eb966d36b67"] :answer-field/correct "q-10662/ma-source-field/cb667763d3551ccb3c36e9aa55347327bfaf4895f2b3af2aa2ebc6cb7808f259/6d6811ceb4fb69a54ce1b24e6804e5f0148bafa1b76b847b06436eb966d36b67" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-10662" :question/id #uuid "06de5100-449e-5af5-b65a-4e9e27bdf01a" :question/math-academy-id "q-10662" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+y+z=2 \\\\ 0x+y-3z=1 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince there are no such numbers $x,y,z$ that form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y+0z=-3,$ we can conclude that our system has no solution." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-10662/ma-source-field/cb667763d3551ccb3c36e9aa55347327bfaf4895f2b3af2aa2ebc6cb7808f259"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f2f6a868-46fe-5529-a464-b6f3e0243d30"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-10662"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186092522 :question/answer-fields 17592186089273] {:db/id "q-11983/ma-source-field/cbf012bfd393c7a7a396b66ce0f9ac3343be277c252007b0c7c654ba2cd71624/4b87a18a476b316d9ff9ee3a4d131adad4b65c55bbdd00ab9fb16bc4acf6946c" :answer/id #uuid "b8a6ca2d-3dc9-5356-a637-77388249f113" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\lambda =-2$ and $\\lambda =-\\sqrt{3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11983/ma-source-field/cbf012bfd393c7a7a396b66ce0f9ac3343be277c252007b0c7c654ba2cd71624/bc0b90695d6329159bdb4d327f1e3cfb86258c1bf16fd4c21e4cf5bb2c83c95d" :answer/id #uuid "87da898e-ea6a-541f-9651-68144afb0f0f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\lambda =-2$ and $\\lambda =\\sqrt{3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11983/ma-source-field/cbf012bfd393c7a7a396b66ce0f9ac3343be277c252007b0c7c654ba2cd71624/496e5c92c516b760444495b2beeb76df268be64870c9c4ce31ba9b69bdee756e" :answer/id #uuid "403a1993-2eb3-586b-abbd-dfbb80940fae" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\lambda =4$ (double root)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11983/ma-source-field/cbf012bfd393c7a7a396b66ce0f9ac3343be277c252007b0c7c654ba2cd71624/8d2c1ed9e61dc9ffbf9afed1df43a9078a3b55cbf5f64dc9e4be374fe20be0cd" :answer/id #uuid "21c5c9ca-97c8-5152-9b6c-25a5632a907d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\lambda =\\sqrt{3}$ and $\\lambda =2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11983/ma-source-field/cbf012bfd393c7a7a396b66ce0f9ac3343be277c252007b0c7c654ba2cd71624/bdb0c7f5d4b7fe04d9e602641d68ea6fc24fa542d5f2becc060b84154e0c0aca" :answer/id #uuid "46e8370f-0146-536e-a75f-2dc4592b1276" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11983/ma-source-field/cbf012bfd393c7a7a396b66ce0f9ac3343be277c252007b0c7c654ba2cd71624" :answer-field/id #uuid "b1ec3bb9-10bd-5719-b579-dd5c85d65b96" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-11983/ma-source-field/cbf012bfd393c7a7a396b66ce0f9ac3343be277c252007b0c7c654ba2cd71624/4b87a18a476b316d9ff9ee3a4d131adad4b65c55bbdd00ab9fb16bc4acf6946c" "q-11983/ma-source-field/cbf012bfd393c7a7a396b66ce0f9ac3343be277c252007b0c7c654ba2cd71624/bc0b90695d6329159bdb4d327f1e3cfb86258c1bf16fd4c21e4cf5bb2c83c95d" "q-11983/ma-source-field/cbf012bfd393c7a7a396b66ce0f9ac3343be277c252007b0c7c654ba2cd71624/496e5c92c516b760444495b2beeb76df268be64870c9c4ce31ba9b69bdee756e" "q-11983/ma-source-field/cbf012bfd393c7a7a396b66ce0f9ac3343be277c252007b0c7c654ba2cd71624/8d2c1ed9e61dc9ffbf9afed1df43a9078a3b55cbf5f64dc9e4be374fe20be0cd" "q-11983/ma-source-field/cbf012bfd393c7a7a396b66ce0f9ac3343be277c252007b0c7c654ba2cd71624/bdb0c7f5d4b7fe04d9e602641d68ea6fc24fa542d5f2becc060b84154e0c0aca"] :answer-field/correct "q-11983/ma-source-field/cbf012bfd393c7a7a396b66ce0f9ac3343be277c252007b0c7c654ba2cd71624/8d2c1ed9e61dc9ffbf9afed1df43a9078a3b55cbf5f64dc9e4be374fe20be0cd" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "b1fb4b20-223a-5224-b15e-06a76416065c"] :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & 0 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 4 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(A-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 4 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (\\sqrt{3}-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda )-0\\cdot 4 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -\\sqrt{3})(\\lambda -2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =\\sqrt{3}$ and $\\lambda =2.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are the entries on the main diagonal." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-11983/ma-source-field/cbf012bfd393c7a7a396b66ce0f9ac3343be277c252007b0c7c654ba2cd71624"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-12008/ma-source-field/8c210d80a754a3e8daa8f72f7d3eff8cccbb8cf1244124274d82daba14e8850a/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "cabd1c0f-3241-5f02-a31b-66428bbc54cc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12008/ma-source-field/8c210d80a754a3e8daa8f72f7d3eff8cccbb8cf1244124274d82daba14e8850a/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "8c8d3009-744a-5594-85d0-81623acfa040" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12008/ma-source-field/8c210d80a754a3e8daa8f72f7d3eff8cccbb8cf1244124274d82daba14e8850a/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "af31ad74-3d71-5216-82f4-241c0fe0d883" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12008/ma-source-field/8c210d80a754a3e8daa8f72f7d3eff8cccbb8cf1244124274d82daba14e8850a/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "55344227-ef64-559d-b72e-d67580b900d1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12008/ma-source-field/8c210d80a754a3e8daa8f72f7d3eff8cccbb8cf1244124274d82daba14e8850a/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" :answer/id #uuid "1acecbea-2330-5d66-8f7e-c711b7d73ea2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12008/ma-source-field/8c210d80a754a3e8daa8f72f7d3eff8cccbb8cf1244124274d82daba14e8850a" :answer-field/id #uuid "e3af571d-ad32-5475-bbe0-4ca42f82e8b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-12008/ma-source-field/8c210d80a754a3e8daa8f72f7d3eff8cccbb8cf1244124274d82daba14e8850a/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-12008/ma-source-field/8c210d80a754a3e8daa8f72f7d3eff8cccbb8cf1244124274d82daba14e8850a/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-12008/ma-source-field/8c210d80a754a3e8daa8f72f7d3eff8cccbb8cf1244124274d82daba14e8850a/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-12008/ma-source-field/8c210d80a754a3e8daa8f72f7d3eff8cccbb8cf1244124274d82daba14e8850a/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-12008/ma-source-field/8c210d80a754a3e8daa8f72f7d3eff8cccbb8cf1244124274d82daba14e8850a/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25"] :answer-field/correct "q-12008/ma-source-field/8c210d80a754a3e8daa8f72f7d3eff8cccbb8cf1244124274d82daba14e8850a/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-12008" :question/id #uuid "d2b3861b-a381-5b7c-bc56-9232209a631c" :question/math-academy-id "q-12008" :question/problem "Let \n$T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x+y \\\\ 4x+3y\\end{aligned}].$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $T(kv)=kT(v)$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vector $v$ and real scalar $k$\nII. $T({v}_{1}+{v}_{2})=T({v}_{1})+T({v}_{2})$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$\nIII. $T$ is a linear transformation" :question/worked-solution "A linear transformation $T$ satisfies two properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & T[\\begin{aligned}kx \\\\ ky\\end{aligned}]=kT[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}], \\\\  & T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Checking the first condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T[\\begin{aligned}kx \\\\ ky\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}kx+ky \\\\ 4kx+3ky\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =k[\\begin{aligned}x+y \\\\ 4x+3y\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =kT[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Checking the second condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} \\\\ 4({x}_{1}+{x}_{2})+3({y}_{1}+{y}_{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{y}_{1} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+3{y}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}+{y}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{2}+3{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{T}$ is a linear transformation.\n\nAs a result, all three statements are true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-12008/ma-source-field/8c210d80a754a3e8daa8f72f7d3eff8cccbb8cf1244124274d82daba14e8850a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8c04b23-e341-57e9-a072-985e4b536e5a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-12008"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-12043/ma-source-field/44050165b3f2b92dc602e3bb69796f55d7f77187f639e84b6053fa5330e8ee36/9268e85b3c7f046b09543b25597692b7ebd6d944eb024975e1db64e626f34a4a" :answer/id #uuid "63d77cc9-bcd1-5fdf-b729-52e06ccab36b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Dilation with scale factor $12$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12043/ma-source-field/44050165b3f2b92dc602e3bb69796f55d7f77187f639e84b6053fa5330e8ee36/f87753f66403a0595fdf0f5a25c3e881069d5c729f8d641afe0f47a65a4201dc" :answer/id #uuid "90b07ab8-256d-5a91-b9cc-79d3fb993b83" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Dilation with scale factor $\\frac{1}{12}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12043/ma-source-field/44050165b3f2b92dc602e3bb69796f55d7f77187f639e84b6053fa5330e8ee36/83351679bef40cdde3e69e55c2c6f08222a317ed82557f1e3ec0abdce5a513f4" :answer/id #uuid "015f808a-c2bc-507e-8f20-bbd2cb4811ff" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Reflection across the $y$-axis" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12043/ma-source-field/44050165b3f2b92dc602e3bb69796f55d7f77187f639e84b6053fa5330e8ee36/fce25706ad846e84aee0bb5f1f92768d6e5c92bb13c1953f1297f12eadf3e6b0" :answer/id #uuid "c91805f4-1cf7-5369-8fb0-b501bd5870f1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Reflection in the line $x=12$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12043/ma-source-field/44050165b3f2b92dc602e3bb69796f55d7f77187f639e84b6053fa5330e8ee36/e37ecd3d677144201dd1a2e78fde156cc49022e18509cf04a18c58aba0184cb6" :answer/id #uuid "2b02233e-2dae-5a79-9684-11c096b79aaf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Reflection in the line $y=12$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12043/ma-source-field/44050165b3f2b92dc602e3bb69796f55d7f77187f639e84b6053fa5330e8ee36" :answer-field/id #uuid "853df19f-413a-5dcd-bd31-575962e