m "![](images/13/13b9598c77cd522d0d3aeee4f5abd2390822431aa49ed787b73a110113ab821c.png)\n\nFind the $x$-intercepts of the circle $(x+4)^{2}+{y}^{2}=25,$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "We must have $y=0$ at the $x$-intercepts. \n\nSo, we need to substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the circle and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+4)^{2}+{y}^{2} & =25 \\\\ (x+4)^{2}+{0}^{2} & =25 \\\\ (x+4)^{2} & =25 \\\\ x+4 & =\\pm \\sqrt{25} \\\\ x+4 & =\\pm 5 \\\\ x & =-4\\pm 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercepts occur at the points $(-9,0)$ and $(1,0).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-15681/ma-source-field/8ceaf668802de3835dd3b0de48a66b094a3645b0e2de0fb1778ef4666359b3be"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8b022811-fdd6-56a1-92ee-388e7ea53a4c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-15681"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-15684/ma-source-field/7cac9ff0f15240d60752fd432e46bea7a26edf79d55c46d53f61bf511f59ac13/b87afc01dffc6730e4ddaeea40e3d1adc70252ace1b905205f8fff12f80c5be2" :answer/id #uuid "0bca8a34-0b3e-5171-929c-8b379129db00" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-5,0)$ and $(7,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15684/ma-source-field/7cac9ff0f15240d60752fd432e46bea7a26edf79d55c46d53f61bf511f59ac13/15c2d687a9c16c8176f2bf515409769dd2be2f2e9c8dbced2dbb449cd060932a" :answer/id #uuid "b6302339-3d66-5e7b-88a3-48ff6e08f3e0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-5,0)$ and $(8,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15684/ma-source-field/7cac9ff0f15240d60752fd432e46bea7a26edf79d55c46d53f61bf511f59ac13/5f43d413d433a1f1815510ce427436d7dae9982f2aa5f2c9e79fe0d488d9455a" :answer/id #uuid "bd167719-ad84-5223-8f5d-835bbaa95ad2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-5.5,0)$ and $(7.5,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15684/ma-source-field/7cac9ff0f15240d60752fd432e46bea7a26edf79d55c46d53f61bf511f59ac13/c02c0ec6196be6ef362c249f24af17a1e1c23107bb8af2d774cf90fa67de508d" :answer/id #uuid "2d1c78a6-2f99-5181-bd25-00d1a3010a31" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-6,0)$ and $(7,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15684/ma-source-field/7cac9ff0f15240d60752fd432e46bea7a26edf79d55c46d53f61bf511f59ac13/8b8bb75a66b6096b0b2ca21ac73eb5369d264688a41aa3ce59e24a89d42758ce" :answer/id #uuid "30ea2584-387d-5bad-8718-caaee9f8c176" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-6,0)$ and $(8,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15684/ma-source-field/7cac9ff0f15240d60752fd432e46bea7a26edf79d55c46d53f61bf511f59ac13" :answer-field/id #uuid "d7f39783-8476-55ac-a74e-97c264bb6280" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-15684/ma-source-field/7cac9ff0f15240d60752fd432e46bea7a26edf79d55c46d53f61bf511f59ac13/b87afc01dffc6730e4ddaeea40e3d1adc70252ace1b905205f8fff12f80c5be2" "q-15684/ma-source-field/7cac9ff0f15240d60752fd432e46bea7a26edf79d55c46d53f61bf511f59ac13/15c2d687a9c16c8176f2bf515409769dd2be2f2e9c8dbced2dbb449cd060932a" "q-15684/ma-source-field/7cac9ff0f15240d60752fd432e46bea7a26edf79d55c46d53f61bf511f59ac13/5f43d413d433a1f1815510ce427436d7dae9982f2aa5f2c9e79fe0d488d9455a" "q-15684/ma-source-field/7cac9ff0f15240d60752fd432e46bea7a26edf79d55c46d53f61bf511f59ac13/c02c0ec6196be6ef362c249f24af17a1e1c23107bb8af2d774cf90fa67de508d" "q-15684/ma-source-field/7cac9ff0f15240d60752fd432e46bea7a26edf79d55c46d53f61bf511f59ac13/8b8bb75a66b6096b0b2ca21ac73eb5369d264688a41aa3ce59e24a89d42758ce"] :answer-field/correct "q-15684/ma-source-field/7cac9ff0f15240d60752fd432e46bea7a26edf79d55c46d53f61bf511f59ac13/b87afc01dffc6730e4ddaeea40e3d1adc70252ace1b905205f8fff12f80c5be2" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-15684" :question/id #uuid "1d50f11f-d6f2-5605-88f1-8c45f7404cb9" :question/math-academy-id "q-15684" :question/problem "![](images/c6/c6d356b443128da569a6b60065769cdb56e2e0059db7b146a3c4035d18a32228.png)\n\nFind the $x$-intercepts of the circle $(x-1)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=45,$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "We must have $y=0$ at the $x$-intercepts. \n\nSo, we need to substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the circle and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & =45 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+(0-3)^{2} & =45 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+9 & =45 \\\\ (x-1)^{2} & =36 \\\\ x-1 & =\\pm \\sqrt{36} \\\\ x & =1\\pm 6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercepts occur at the points $(-5,0)$ and $(7,0).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-15684/ma-source-field/7cac9ff0f15240d60752fd432e46bea7a26edf79d55c46d53f61bf511f59ac13"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8b022811-fdd6-56a1-92ee-388e7ea53a4c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-15684"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186079067 :question/answer-fields 17592186077150] {:db/id "q-5144/ma-source-field/eeab2b1d30bf936155d0702c4e0a453f4ee52c0b337f41f3176a07e213fb8eba/8e99eeffbc3e3df3ff2c01340ababf0b9293916cb4542a0e22b1156e4437d738" :answer/id #uuid "445b916b-1ba8-5248-91b4-ef8043ebe2f7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "center: $(-2,3)$, radius: $4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-5144/ma-source-field/eeab2b1d30bf936155d0702c4e0a453f4ee52c0b337f41f3176a07e213fb8eba/6aeebc0d1a24606aeb314a2ed2fe52278f1a1a73b668a7b9f83cfee60a40d1b3" :answer/id #uuid "3958fd13-48da-5731-9bd7-2332d7318f31" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "center: $(2,-3)$, radius: $16$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-5144/ma-source-field/eeab2b1d30bf936155d0702c4e0a453f4ee52c0b337f41f3176a07e213fb8eba/36ff7c848980258c9d4932b7101f98821a602fde46f9737581b447fcdf0867ed" :answer/id #uuid "ae470676-bc8c-59ed-9ddf-e6bfad4e99f2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "center: $(2,-3)$, radius: $4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-5144/ma-source-field/eeab2b1d30bf936155d0702c4e0a453f4ee52c0b337f41f3176a07e213fb8eba/b365db0d23a00be7f1b9b2e1aaec75b6841604b761bd47b063040bc4da276a90" :answer/id #uuid "6d7bd3d5-18da-5a40-acfa-fa44fce357be" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "center: $(3,-2)$, radius: $16$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-5144/ma-source-field/eeab2b1d30bf936155d0702c4e0a453f4ee52c0b337f41f3176a07e213fb8eba/91ce83a61523460c879d5efec1e417ef2cbe90e5f10826f4146313384297a521" :answer/id #uuid "1caf2e7f-b2a3-5b2b-9e2c-a85b6dd512fd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "center: $(3,-2)$, radius: $8$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-5144/ma-source-field/eeab2b1d30bf936155d0702c4e0a453f4ee52c0b337f41f3176a07e213fb8eba" :answer-field/id #uuid "8f64383e-34d9-58e2-8c5a-1486b312000b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-5144/ma-source-field/eeab2b1d30bf936155d0702c4e0a453f4ee52c0b337f41f3176a07e213fb8eba/8e99eeffbc3e3df3ff2c01340ababf0b9293916cb4542a0e22b1156e4437d738" "q-5144/ma-source-field/eeab2b1d30bf936155d0702c4e0a453f4ee52c0b337f41f3176a07e213fb8eba/6aeebc0d1a24606aeb314a2ed2fe52278f1a1a73b668a7b9f83cfee60a40d1b3" "q-5144/ma-source-field/eeab2b1d30bf936155d0702c4e0a453f4ee52c0b337f41f3176a07e213fb8eba/36ff7c848980258c9d4932b7101f98821a602fde46f9737581b447fcdf0867ed" "q-5144/ma-source-field/eeab2b1d30bf936155d0702c4e0a453f4ee52c0b337f41f3176a07e213fb8eba/b365db0d23a00be7f1b9b2e1aaec75b6841604b761bd47b063040bc4da276a90" "q-5144/ma-source-field/eeab2b1d30bf936155d0702c4e0a453f4ee52c0b337f41f3176a07e213fb8eba/91ce83a61523460c879d5efec1e417ef2cbe90e5f10826f4146313384297a521"] :answer-field/correct "q-5144/ma-source-field/eeab2b1d30bf936155d0702c4e0a453f4ee52c0b337f41f3176a07e213fb8eba/8e99eeffbc3e3df3ff2c01340ababf0b9293916cb4542a0e22b1156e4437d738" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "dd6c82b9-14ab-538d-aa0f-037306546c3d"] :question/problem "Find the center and radius of the circle whose equation is ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+4x-6y=3.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the center and radius of the circle, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+4x-6y & =3 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+4x)+({y}^{2}-6y) & =3 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 2x+{2}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot 3y+{3}^{2}) & =3+{2}^{2}+{3}^{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 2x+4)+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot 3y+9) & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect squares and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & ={4}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-2))^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & ={4}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(-2,3)$ and its radius is $4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-5144/ma-source-field/eeab2b1d30bf936155d0702c4e0a453f4ee52c0b337f41f3176a07e213fb8eba"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-5183/ma-source-field/6d5444b3e9ae373000144f7fe6c23c862cfc2a290d071d498ab613f2c32ec604/ae2bb86a0eb60e76881e8eb45a2724efdf8d6c7490385dbf4f3a979e49d4deb4" :answer/id #uuid "4a914338-4d65-53bf-b781-37800f0d7a7e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "center: $(-4,-5)$, radius: $4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-5183/ma-source-field/6d5444b3e9ae373000144f7fe6c23c862cfc2a290d071d498ab613f2c32ec604/3cc09ef683ed3149de5f9de5806b5c3c1c919f5a23276faf9215ed53b69b6a96" :answer/id #uuid "da01d3e1-9120-5411-866d-68f2c61e8b78" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "center: $(-4,-5)$, radius: $7$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-5183/ma-source-field/6d5444b3e9ae373000144f7fe6c23c862cfc2a290d071d498ab613f2c32ec604/7a860ed154417b566499c136f63497ff726535a5d3a05c025463fdb4a923b269" :answer/id #uuid "7347a868-a565-5dcd-9bc6-dcb157568620" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "center: $(-4,-5)$, radius: $8$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-5183/ma-source-field/6d5444b3e9ae373000144f7fe6c23c862cfc2a290d071d498ab613f2c32ec604/c3158a6cea8e2bd4967e85caeae6057c925f672ed83d5f5fe7a197e443f564a0" :answer/id #uuid "dff6112c-7516-520a-ad8d-0c