$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-8x-10y+{x}^{2} & =8 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-8x)+({y}^{2}-10y) & =8 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 4x+{4}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot 5y+{5}^{2}) & =8+{4}^{2}+{5}^{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 4x+{4}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot 5y+{5}^{2}) & =49\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect squares and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-4)^{2}+(y-5)^{2} & ={7}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(4,5)$ and its radius is $7.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-5183/ma-source-field/6d5444b3e9ae373000144f7fe6c23c862cfc2a290d071d498ab613f2c32ec604"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "697f9bd8-9edf-5643-8cdb-a821b6dce09c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-5183"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-6913/ma-source-field/e710ece9b4531d9026b3d8479d5ec85dc1d2bb96389ba6dbff7c421116706256/25de97e0cbf440101fa2f4e8740e4610708c595cc7aac47b53097fbc80ac64e1" :answer/id #uuid "b2a272db-6815-53ec-87da-5a281c0b5932" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-2,\\,x=0,\\,x=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-6913/ma-source-field/e710ece9b4531d9026b3d8479d5ec85dc1d2bb96389ba6dbff7c421116706256/965aa5c98136d8e35adef10437bec7dcaa5ea245557ace16b44703e422ea6239" :answer/id #uuid "4649603f-3d59-5567-ab7b-c75a268bb6c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-\\sqrt{2},\\,x=0,\\,x=\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-6913/ma-source-field/e710ece9b4531d9026b3d8479d5ec85dc1d2bb96389ba6dbff7c421116706256/2a5ccdf4c5ff93070db5428c796ddf8a07da996ff5ecd4a5bcb616f8a02f59f8" :answer/id #uuid "81bc4acc-cf96-53dd-9604-97c51e416cf4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-\\sqrt{2},\\,x=\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-6913/ma-source-field/e710ece9b4531d9026b3d8479d5ec85dc1d2bb96389ba6dbff7c421116706256/517b13fa7d7411493417798333c215e538be20515774e23158b4c71536604686" :answer/id #uuid "d3972294-8bb0-593a-9b73-d4e09973c691" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=0$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-6913/ma-source-field/e710ece9b4531d9026b3d8479d5ec85dc1d2bb96389ba6dbff7c421116706256/e5d103e2c07ae759d9eddce65c552ccfa6a5a00acf0aea2f18942b9a819f2577" :answer/id #uuid "6b3a157a-5fe4-53f2-9241-98666b5d0e07" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The function has no vertical asymptotes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-6913/ma-source-field/e710ece9b4531d9026b3d8479d5ec85dc1d2bb96389ba6dbff7c421116706256" :answer-field/id #uuid "cdc4a2be-1828-5c44-9645-c520108c6c2f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-6913/ma-source-field/e710ece9b4531d9026b3d8479d5ec85dc1d2bb96389ba6dbff7c421116706256/25de97e0cbf440101fa2f4e8740e4610708c595cc7aac47b53097fbc80ac64e1" "q-6913/ma-source-field/e710ece9b4531d9026b3d8479d5ec85dc1d2bb96389ba6dbff7c421116706256/965aa5c98136d8e35adef10437bec7dcaa5ea245557ace16b44703e422ea6239" "q-6913/ma-source-field/e710ece9b4531d9026b3d8479d5ec85dc1d2bb96389ba6dbff7c421116706256/2a5ccdf4c5ff93070db5428c796ddf8a07da996ff5ecd4a5bcb616f8a02f59f8" "q-6913/ma-source-field/e710ece9b4531d9026b3d8479d5ec85dc1d2bb96389ba6dbff7c421116706256/517b13fa7d7411493417798333c215e538be20515774e23158b4c71536604686" "q-6913/ma-source-field/e710ece9b4531d9026b3d8479d5ec85dc1d2bb96389ba6dbff7c421116706256/e5d103e2c07ae759d9eddce65c552ccfa6a5a00acf0aea2f18942b9a819f2577"] :answer-field/correct "q-6913/ma-source-field/e710ece9b4531d9026b3d8479d5ec85dc1d2bb96389ba6dbff7c421116706256/e5d103e2c07ae759d9eddce65c552ccfa6a5a00acf0aea2f18942b9a819f2577" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-6913" :question/id #uuid "2d87d550-5004-5d22-b9a3-b2335e96082d" :question/math-academy-id "q-6913" :question/problem "Find all of the vertical asymptotes of the function $f(x)=\\frac{x}{{x}^{3}+2x}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the vertical asymptotes of a rational function, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors. Then, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x.$\n\nFactoring the numerator and denominator and canceling any common factors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{x}{{x}^{3}+2x} \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{x({x}^{2}+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{x}}{\\cancel{x}({x}^{2}+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we set the denominator equal to zero:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+2=0\n$$\n\nThis equation does not have any real solutions. Therefore, $f(x)$ does not have any vertical asymptotes." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-6913/ma-source-field/e710ece9b4531d9026b3d8479d5ec85dc1d2bb96389ba6dbff7c421116706256"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b0b57da-f9af-5fab-a337-51ee4cb28f9e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-6913"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186088283 :question/answer-fields 17592186086322] {:db/id "q-6993/ma-source-field/7ba5fe28d4499a76274cbfc47755abefc655b1944e4d89f02cfaaef70595a153/1e9f29c284d3d4384ce2a5e04c1013d29b18bf826f8ff61e900714021a9e3327" :answer/id #uuid "9c5baf21-1bf2-5b1b-bfa8-dcd597f29533" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-6993/ma-source-field/7ba5fe28d4499a76274cbfc47755abefc655b1944e4d89f02cfaaef70595a153/1906c09d3250b980be598715c4c6a25321df1d4eddd30dfdf9bf029564db3276" :answer/id #uuid "d61fc313-6be1-5c44-9928-321ac1588795" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-6993/ma-source-field/7ba5fe28d4499a76274cbfc47755abefc655b1944e4d89f02cfaaef70595a153/96efe327aa5df1953454aa8a0acb24299d8e2e2f538b2a5f40d98e7332b886b7" :answer/id #uuid "8c3ffe47-5182-54d6-be67-f2bcfb1c8dcc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-6993/ma-source-field/7ba5fe28d4499a76274cbfc47755abefc655b1944e4d89f02cfaaef70595a153/4feedb526b42a6330326ae286db118832dd2fb8a6461fa34068de015b5ade8cd" :answer/id #uuid "064738ba-95d8-5a57-a3ad-d540d417ad9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-6993/ma-source-field/7ba5fe28d4499a76274cbfc47755abefc655b1944e4d89f02cfaaef70595a153/3e622b14fb9e8408568d99d85f4dbc69d704ea59c7efa30ae415e06682e77843" :answer/id #uuid "8cf39b51-f47c-5795-b708-ce55aa495338" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No horizontal asymptotes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-6993/ma-source-field/7ba5fe28d4499a76274cbfc47755abefc655b1944e4d89f02cfaaef70595a153" :answer-field/id #uuid "add2fe99-72af-58a7-aa92-3850d67de2fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-6993/ma-source-field/7ba5fe28d4499a76274cbfc47755abefc655b1944e4d89f02cfaaef70595a153/1e9f29c284d3d4384ce2a5e04c1013d29b18bf826f8ff61e900714021a9e3327" "q-6993/ma-source-field/7ba5fe28d4499a76274cbfc47755abefc655b1944e4d89f02cfaaef70595a153/1906c09d3250b980be598715c4c6a25321df1d4eddd30dfdf9bf029564db3276" "q-6993/ma-source-field/7ba5fe28d4499a76274cbfc47755abefc655b1944e4d89f02cfaaef70595a153/96efe327aa5df1953454aa8a0acb24299d8e2e2f538b2a5f40d98e7332b886b7" "q-6993/ma-source-field/7ba5fe28d4499a76274cbfc47755abefc655b1944e4d89f02cfaaef70595a153/4feedb526b42a6330326ae286db118832dd2fb8a6461fa34068de015b5ade8cd" "q-6993/ma-source-field/7ba5fe28d4499a76274cbfc47755abefc655b1944e4d89f02cfaaef70595a153/3e622b14fb9e8408568d99d85f4dbc69d704ea59c7efa30ae415e06682e77843"] :answer-field/correct "q-6993/ma-source-field/7ba5fe28d4499a76274cbfc47755abefc655b1944e4d89f02cfaaef70595a153/3e622b14fb9e8408568d99d85f4dbc69d704ea59c7efa30ae415e06682e77843" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "0e542b04-fff9-5d2f-9fc8-db21225d104b"] :question/problem "Determine the horizontal asymptote of $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{3}+3}{4{x}^{2}-6x}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the horizontal asymptote of a rational function, we divide every term in the numerator and denominator by the dominant term in the denominator, and then we let $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nIgnoring the coefficient, the dominant term in the denominator is ${x}^{2}.$ So, we divide every term in the numerator and denominator by ${x}^{2},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{{x}^{3}+3}{4{x}^{2}-6x} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}})}{(\\frac{4{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{6x}{{x}^{2}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}})}{(4-\\frac{6}{x})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, when $x$ is very large, the terms $\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}}$ and $\\frac{6}{x}$ become very small. Therefore, as $x\\to \\infty ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{(x+\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}})}{(4-\\frac{6}{x})} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{x+0}{4-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is not a constant, which means that $y=f(x)$ does not have a horizontal asymptote." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-6993/ma-source-field/7ba5fe28d4499a76274cbfc47755abefc655b1944e4d89f02cfaaef70595a153"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-7596/ma-source-field/f10b3b16918688aa7837e5d8c9bc9dfaad299103a67556128840e507accecf70/96fc253e0c66345f8ca564a17c0c1fae992c5ec5b278e6bbbdeea53d550648cd" :answer/id #uuid "d5b72ba2-9df1-5acc-b385-173c4e36f9a6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$18$ and $9$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7596/ma-source-field/f10b3b16918688aa7837e5d8c9bc9dfaad299103a67556128840e507accecf70/40148c9d7ac7b6262b45f56e187242cedf0c466f8f8f43dbe9f8d735919ed2b0" :answer/id #uuid "801b88de-1112-5c33-bd1b-ddb864de2c6f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$3\\sqrt{2}$ and $3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7596/ma-source-field/f10b3b16918688aa7837e5d8c9bc9dfaad299103a67556128840e507accecf70/5fd750aaa374560dd76ad0a7b30c83e276a4ec78a7dfea009715277281a572d5" :answer/id #uuid "dcd49079-798b-58f7-8490-cd6fb613a033" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$6$ and $3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7596/ma-source-field/f10b3b16918688aa7837e5d8c9bc9dfaad299103a67556128840e507accecf70/03b9d70ffca29267772c5c89ef9afbae091da50fa5e35c66893876411122ed3d" :answer/id #uuid "d2368068-c473-5919-aff6-53a14b246b5c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$6\\sqrt{2}$ and $3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7596/ma-source-field/f10b3b16918688aa7837e5d8c9bc9dfaad299103a67556128840e507accecf70/c699f2ff3c9baae9ac49bf2286be75cce58afc93074ffbac97c38b57ea33060a" :answer/id #uuid "7c6ef04e-258f-5d68-a139-8ed8a39c2ddc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$6\\sqrt{2}$ and $6$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7596/ma-source-field/f10b3b16918688aa7837e5d8c9bc9dfaad299103a67556128840e507accecf70" :answer-field/id #uuid "bef4ba21-7e9c-5949-8c09-0a45d37f8298" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-7596/ma-source-field/f10b3b16918688aa7837e5d8c9bc9dfaad299103a67556128840e507accecf70/96fc253e0c66345f8ca564a17c0c1fae992c5ec5b278e6bbbdeea53d550648cd" "q-7596/ma-source-field/f10b3b16918688aa7837e5d8c9bc9dfaad299103a67556128840e507accecf70/40148c9d7ac7b6262b45f56e187242cedf0c466f8f8f43dbe9f8d735919ed2b0" "q-7596/ma-source-field/f10b3b16918688aa7837e5d8c9bc9dfaad299103a67556128840e507accecf70/5fd750aaa374560dd76ad0a7b30c83e276a4ec78a7dfea009715277281a572d5" "q-7596/ma-source-field/f10b3b16918688aa7837e5d8c9bc9dfaad299103a67556128840e507accecf70/03b9d70ffca29267772c5c89ef9afbae091da50fa5e35c66893876411122ed3d" "q-7596/ma-source-field/f10b3b16918688aa7837e5d8c9bc9dfaad299103a67556128840e507accecf70/c699f2ff3c9baae9ac49bf2286be75cce58afc93074ffbac97c38b57ea33060a"] :answer-field/correct "q-7596/ma-source-field/f10b3b16918688aa7837e5d8c9bc9dfaad299103a67556128840e507accecf70/c699f2ff3c9baae9ac49bf2286be75cce58afc93074ffbac97c38b57ea33060a" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-7596" :question/id #uuid "480a616c-8c80-5f81-b3d5-aa7488c0665b" :question/math-academy-id "q-7596" :question/problem "What are the lengths of the major and minor axes of an ellipse with equation \n$\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{18}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=9$ and ${b}^{2}=18.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=9,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{9}=3.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=18,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{18}=3\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $b=3\\sqrt{2},$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=3.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 3\\sqrt{2}=6\\sqrt{2},$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 3=6.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-7596/ma-source-field/f10b3b16918688aa7837e5d8c9bc9dfaad299103a67556128840e507accecf70"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-7596"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-7597/ma-source-field/4fec8ab60a622320bd06647a5005767fe2428d72f2205af62688b76e806abc02/b6b4843be470cec5c0f9008c4662f65a21e8758c2b1e0ce3d9c0f48693dcc468" :answer/id #uuid "b48bdeab-9afb-508b-a31f-840d2716535b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$10$ and $8$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7597/ma-source-field/4fec8ab60a622320bd06647a5005767fe2428d72f2205af62688b76e806abc02/78be9a384f78807f18f8d80eaa7b91a3fdff8b40ed26e0d72a32b8e9f5ccd9a4" :answer/id #uuid "71576bd8-08e5-58e9-999c-df3860cd2885" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$20$ and $16$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7597/ma-source-field/4fec8ab60a622320bd06647a5005767fe2428d72f2205af62688b76e806abc02/6a7004d084b2d346df9a3d8e434b1412014527000e696e6d1ef1af37e183d648" :answer/id #uuid "6565345d-7cca-5723-8a4a-06b781ec17a7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2\\sqrt{5}$ and $4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7597/ma-source-field/4fec8ab60a622320bd06647a5005767fe2428d72f2205af62688b76e806abc02/5a51552a2a5cd5c79e23e95115ade746abeb43ef25553e1701226da1e7510043" :answer/id #uuid "dcb6c4d2-fc5f-560f-9373-4f7a33529527" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$4\\sqrt{5}$ and $8$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7597/ma-source-field/4fec8ab60a622320bd06647a5005767fe2428d72f2205af62688b76e806abc02/c9a320c544e7dc8e51eda8f9456d821856bb320ad2432a70e6675de2da0645d5" :answer/id #uuid "7fd4bf3f-6eb6-53a8-9729-d9955e874477" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\sqrt{5}$ and $2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7597/ma-source-field/4fec8ab60a622320bd06647a5005767fe2428d72f2205af62688b76e806abc02" :answer-field/id #uuid "abca09ba-0b0a-5885-90fb-fd1d7d5af56c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-7597/ma-source-field/4fec8ab60a622320bd06647a5005767fe2428d72f2205af62688b76e806abc02/b6b4843be470cec5c0f9008c4662f65a21e8758c2b1e0ce3d9c0f48693dcc468" "q-7597/ma-source-field/4fec8ab60a622320bd06647a5005767fe2428d72f2205af62688b76e806abc02/78be9a384f78807f18f8d80eaa7b91a3fdff8b40ed26e0d72a32b8e9f5ccd9a4" "q-7597/ma-source-field/4fec8ab60a622320bd06647a5005767fe2428d72f2205af62688b76e806abc02/6a7004d084b2d346df9a3d8e434b1412014527000e696e6d1ef1af37e183d648" "q-7597/ma-source-field/4fec8ab60a622320bd06647a5005767fe2428d72f2205af62688b76e806abc02/5a51552a2a5cd5c79e23e95115ade746abeb43ef25553e1701226da1e7510043" "q-7597/ma-source-field/4fec8ab60a622320bd06647a5005767fe2428d72f2205af62688b76e806abc02/c9a320c544e7dc8e51eda8f9456d821856bb320ad2432a70e6675de2da0645d5"] :answer-field/correct "q-7597/ma-source-field/4fec8ab60a622320bd06647a5005767fe2428d72f2205af62688b76e806abc02/5a51552a2a5cd5c79e23e95115ade746abeb43ef25553e1701226da1e7510043" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-7597" :question/id #uuid "e572cb8d-0721-59ec-897a-5e0fa685feb4" :question/math-academy-id "q-7597" :question/problem "What are the lengths of the major and minor axes of an ellipse with equation \n$\\frac{{x}^{2}}{20}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=20$ and ${b}^{2}=16.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=20,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{20}=2\\sqrt{5}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=16,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{16}=4.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $a=2\\sqrt{5},$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=4.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{5}=4\\sqrt{5},$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 4=8.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-7597/ma-source-field/4fec8ab60a622320bd06647a5005767fe2428d72f2205af62688b76e806abc02"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-7597"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-7639/ma-source-field/a9a59b9e6512818bceaddc8d6d22a76e3215b0064328d56c3d47844a4fe79d64/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "b3f7d8da-7727-5a58-ab68-96bc81e72057" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7639/ma-source-field/a9a59b9e6512818bceaddc8d6d22a76e3215b0064328d56c3d47844a4fe79d64/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "306281a3-80c8-5e0a-9a37-cd54c88c73c6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7639/ma-source-field/a9a59b9e6512818bceaddc8d6d22a76e3215b0064328d56c3d47844a4fe79d64/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "5b8c75df-6d72-5de6-8aa7-4da99784ebe0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7639/ma-source-field/a9a59b9e6512818bceaddc8d6d22a76e3215b0064328d56c3d47844a4fe79d64/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "f7f334c8-c362-5bc3-bb42-acf3a7888901" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7639/ma-source-field/a9a59b9e6512818bceaddc8d6d22a76e3215b0064328d56c3d47844a4fe79d64/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "ec7d741b-53e6-5079-a8a5-dd4f4717842f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7639/ma-source-field/a9a59b9e6512818bceaddc8d6d22a76e3215b0064328d56c3d47844a4fe79d64" :answer-field/id #uuid "e14f3866-43ea-5b8f-9948-a2dc29883068" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-7639/ma-source-field/a9a59b9e6512818bceaddc8d6d22a76e3215b0064328d56c3d47844a4fe79d64/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-7639/ma-source-field/a9a59b9e6512818bceaddc8d6d22a76e3215b0064328d56c3d47844a4fe79d64/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-7639/ma-source-field/a9a59b9e6512818bceaddc8d6d22a76e3215b0064328d56c3d47844a4fe79d64/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-7639/ma-source-field/a9a59b9e6512818bceaddc8d6d22a76e3215b0064328d56c3d47844a4fe79d64/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-7639/ma-source-field/a9a59b9e6512818bceaddc8d6d22a76e3215b0064328d56c3d47844a4fe79d64/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981"] :answer-field/correct "q-7639/ma-source-field/a9a59b9e6512818bceaddc8d6d22a76e3215b0064328d56c3d47844a4fe79d64/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-7639" :question/id #uuid "fd2cdae2-5e26-5778-ab7e-65d79d794e32" :question/math-academy-id "q-7639" :question/problem "Consider the ellipse whose equation is ${x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}-2x+12y=-11.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. Its center is $(1,-3)$\nII. The length of the major axis  is $2\\sqrt{2}$\nIII. The length of the minor axis is $4$" :question/worked-solution "First, we must group the $x$ and $y$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}-2x+12y & =-11 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2x)+(2{y}^{2}+12y) & =-11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we complete the square for both the $x$ and $y$ terms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}^{2}-2x)+(2{y}^{2}+12y) & =-11 \\\\ [{x}^{2}-2x]+2[{y}^{2}+6y] & =-11 \\\\ [(x-1)^{2}-{1}^{2}]+2[(y+3)^{2}-{3}^{2}] & =-11 \\\\ [(x-1)^{2}-1]+2[(y+3)^{2}-9] & =-11 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}-1+2(y+3)^{2}-18 & =-11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rearrange the equation into the desired form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)^{2}-1+2(y+3)^{2}-18 & =-11 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+2(y+3)^{2} & =-11+1+18 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+2(y+3)^{2} & =8 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{(2\\sqrt{2})^{2}}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $2\\sqrt{2}>2,$ the length of the major axis is $2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{2}=4\\sqrt{2},$ the length of the minor axis is $2\\cdot 2=4,$ and the ellipse is centered at $(1,-3).$\n\nTherefore,  I and III are true, and II is false." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-7639/ma-source-field/a9a59b9e6512818bceaddc8d6d22a76e3215b0064328d56c3d47844a4fe79d64"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d21d6066-f7c8-5a47-b150-d0ae25d2d60b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-7639"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-7643/ma-source-field/a0cf9550adb6f3e6fbd34b77c391df7fcaedec4b7db4cfc5a042d8a03291bda4/26b096bce36c63f274eed2844a7d3b09612ebc01a12309c05b9eb1ada685d00e" :answer/id #uuid "2b6bcede-bd93-5e91-b587-867ae663acd1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\pm 2,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7643/ma-source-field/a0cf9550adb6f3e6fbd34b77c391df7fcaedec4b7db4cfc5a042d8a03291bda4/21222b9c4748093197e8e6a8fabbba14cf9b24871c4c9556fbb1213d9d4bcb0a" :answer/id #uuid "02fe5fe7-b348-53e0-8947-15f0c37ed27c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\pm 3,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7643/ma-source-field/a0cf9550adb6f3e6fbd34b77c391df7fcaedec4b7db4cfc5a042d8a03291bda4/f0c0a6114dce0a0d588de48c33c9e31bf2359371fd92cba8fb2e6bacf392c8cd" :answer/id #uuid "185228aa-01c2-5fd7-a5ac-217c7d571287" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-1,0)$ and $(2,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7643/ma-source-field/a0cf9550adb6f3e6fbd34b77c391df7fcaedec4b7db4cfc5a042d8a03291bda4/e2bf556aa3c4cccb29751419480707eb1814af037331c05437656ef617118c80" :answer/id #uuid "00403835-be99-5078-bb45-9f705d557d03" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,0)$ and $(2,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7643/ma-source-field/a0cf9550adb6f3e6fbd34b77c391df7fcaedec4b7db4cfc5a042d8a03291bda4/a097f40d36ee3f4b2efc742b6eca487975630e4cc092c741ac5b96963bd7d832" :answer/id #uuid "6d0fc8b9-a163-539b-9c0f-8eb06fff83e1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,0)$ and $(4,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7643/ma-source-field/a0cf9550adb6f3e6fbd34b77c391df7fcaedec4b7db4cfc5a042d8a03291bda4" :answer-field/id #uuid "384638bd-72a6-5df4-a17b-400ec33ad1b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-7643/ma-source-field/a0cf9550adb6f3e6fbd34b77c391df7fcaedec4b7db4cfc5a042d8a03291bda4/26b096bce36c63f274eed2844a7d3b09612ebc01a12309c05b9eb1ada685d00e" "q-7643/ma-source-field/a0cf9550adb6f3e6fbd34b77c391df7fcaedec4b7db4cfc5a042d8a03291bda4/21222b9c4748093197e8e6a8fabbba14cf9b24871c4c9556fbb1213d9d4bcb0a" "q-7643/ma-source-field/a0cf9550adb6f3e6fbd34b77c391df7fcaedec4b7db4cfc5a042d8a03291bda4/f0c0a6114dce0a0d588de48c33c9e31bf2359371fd92cba8fb2e6bacf392c8cd" "q-7643/ma-source-field/a0cf9550adb6f3e6fbd34b77c391df7fcaedec4b7db4cfc5a042d8a03291bda4/e2bf556aa3c4cccb29751419480707eb1814af037331c05437656ef617118c80" "q-7643/ma-source-field/a0cf9550adb6f3e6fbd34b77c391df7fcaedec4b7db4cfc5a042d8a03291bda4/a097f40d36ee3f4b2efc742b6eca487975630e4cc092c741ac5b96963bd7d832"] :answer-field/correct "q-7643/ma-source-field/a0cf9550adb6f3e6fbd34b77c391df7fcaedec4b7db4cfc5a042d8a03291bda4/a097f40d36ee3f4b2efc742b6eca487975630e4cc092c741ac5b96963bd7d832" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-7643" :question/id #uuid "85a05273-d7c5-5a81-9a38-af7c6efc1cfa" :question/math-academy-id "q-7643" :question/problem "Calculate the points where the ellipse \n$\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{12}=1$ intercepts the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "To calculate the $x$-intercept, we need to substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the ellipse and solve the resulting equation for $x.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{12} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(0+3)^{2}}{12} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{9}{12} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{3}{4} & =1 \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+12 & =16 \\\\ (x-2)^{2} & =4 \\\\ x-2 & =\\pm 2 \\\\ x & =2\\pm 2 \\\\ x & =0,4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-7643/ma-source-field/a0cf9550adb6f3e6fbd34b77c391df7fcaedec4b7db4cfc5a042d8a03291bda4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74a508c1-2379-590f-85f5-386a1990f137"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-7643"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-7644/ma-source-field/f85a39f03d8631c53b7e3deab775