q-7915/ma-source-field/f7b7d0cd7d49af33309e2375604ae82586dd7813e587181cb24666ba4e7c89d6/afe4b97c823938f24ee0f462e6dae1ce1a6e74074abfb6f3f9af3b253499f0cc"] :answer-field/correct "q-7915/ma-source-field/f7b7d0cd7d49af33309e2375604ae82586dd7813e587181cb24666ba4e7c89d6/f6ed8c3e8ac11c4c476e856e67261d9addd41c460d2f0404e6d3f3a72ad0633a" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-7915" :question/id #uuid "17761662-c8e1-5053-be1d-f17ca1632a52" :question/math-academy-id "q-7915" :question/problem "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 6\\end{aligned}],\\,Q=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,R=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "- For the matrix $P$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(P)=4\\cdot 6-8\\cdot 3=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(P)=0,$ we conclude that $P$ is not invertible. Since $P$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $P$ is singular.\n\n- For the matrix $Q$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(Q)=1\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot (-1)=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(Q)=0,$ we conclude that $Q$ is not invertible. Since $Q$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $Q$ is singular.\n\n- The matrix $R$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix. So, it is not invertible. Since the matrix is not square, we can't say that it's singular.\n\nTherefore, only $P$ and $Q$ are singular." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-7915/ma-source-field/f7b7d0cd7d49af33309e2375604ae82586dd7813e587181cb24666ba4e7c89d6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c6056ee-15f3-5b5c-8a14-173ea1da1381"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-7915"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-8049/ma-source-field/50c060e5810a3c2f4788ae384dc3174ce81e725784df06f4a987f59f3e9caea0/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "b529905e-a877-50ee-aa7b-eaa49f3e381c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8049/ma-source-field/50c060e5810a3c2f4788ae384dc3174ce81e725784df06f4a987f59f3e9caea0/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "9fe865ac-e938-502a-af64-2906292df08f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8049/ma-source-field/50c060e5810a3c2f4788ae384dc3174ce81e725784df06f4a987f59f3e9caea0/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "5760bb5a-46a2-50c2-a5f5-3d9d162ce69f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8049/ma-source-field/50c060e5810a3c2f4788ae384dc3174ce81e725784df06f4a987f59f3e9caea0/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "37f747c4-2d3b-5fc7-9c34-d271a78f7358" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8049/ma-source-field/50c060e5810a3c2f4788ae384dc3174ce81e725784df06f4a987f59f3e9caea0/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" :answer/id #uuid "4d878238-fc2c-51a3-9450-0461f9c5a8f1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8049/ma-source-field/50c060e5810a3c2f4788ae384dc3174ce81e725784df06f4a987f59f3e9caea0" :answer-field/id #uuid "71152846-626d-5dbd-a0ab-1425eb8ae515" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-8049/ma-source-field/50c060e5810a3c2f4788ae384dc3174ce81e725784df06f4a987f59f3e9caea0/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-8049/ma-source-field/50c060e5810a3c2f4788ae384dc3174ce81e725784df06f4a987f59f3e9caea0/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-8049/ma-source-field/50c060e5810a3c2f4788ae384dc3174ce81e725784df06f4a987f59f3e9caea0/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-8049/ma-source-field/50c060e5810a3c2f4788ae384dc3174ce81e725784df06f4a987f59f3e9caea0/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-8049/ma-source-field/50c060e5810a3c2f4788ae384dc3174ce81e725784df06f4a987f59f3e9caea0/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25"] :answer-field/correct "q-8049/ma-source-field/50c060e5810a3c2f4788ae384dc3174ce81e725784df06f4a987f59f3e9caea0/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-8049" :question/id #uuid "72a3fd90-5133-5a81-a0e8-33ac74b2d520" :question/math-academy-id "q-8049" :question/problem "Let \n$T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ x\\end{aligned}].$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $T(kv)=kT(v)$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vector $v$ and real scalar $k$\nII. $T({v}_{1}+{v}_{2})=T({v}_{1})+T({v}_{2})$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$\nIII. $T$ is **NOT** a linear transformation" :question/worked-solution "A linear transformation $T$ satisfies two properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & T[\\begin{aligned}kx \\\\ ky\\end{aligned}]=kT[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}], \\\\  & T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Checking the first condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T[\\begin{aligned}kx \\\\ ky\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ kx\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne kT[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{T}$ is not a linear transformation.\n\n- Checking the second condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, only statement III is true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-8049/ma-source-field/50c060e5810a3c2f4788ae384dc3174ce81e725784df06f4a987f59f3e9caea0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8c04b23-e341-57e9-a072-985e4b536e5a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-8049"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-8054/ma-source-field/53c7ddf8ddc00b934ee89e0216bf262db4f3527c9c107dac538ec3d7bd02e0ee/a868feefac40bb7b0111347167c383122fd4a9aadbd951f54e5afb18f41996b4" :answer/id #uuid "72639a3d-6ded-5b32-8272-74477a63f9ae" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Dilation with scale factor $3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8054/ma-source-field/53c7ddf8ddc00b934ee89e0216bf262db4f3527c9c107dac538ec3d7bd02e0ee/45b3f3a947a62cbb84343e51a596f8f94e1255e046e3dfde9740d1e89c324c95" :answer/id #uuid "b95051d2-50e5-54f9-a671-a1d798db4c74" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Dilation with scale factor $\\frac{1}{3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8054/ma-source-field/53c7ddf8ddc00b934ee89e0216bf262db4f3527c9c107dac538ec3d7bd02e0ee/83351679bef40cdde3e69e55c2c6f08222a317ed82557f1e3ec0abdce5a513f4" :answer/id #uuid "1a07ec2e-4723-50fa-a492-65d833fca2c4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Reflection across the $y$-axis" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8054/ma-source-field/53c7ddf8ddc00b934ee89e0216bf262db4f3527c9c107dac538ec3d7bd02e0ee/b3dd010b5de3347aa8363384dfcef5a2cbe8f7a1fa63e51d63e92f25d9459b76" :answer/id #uuid "e8825cd3-515a-5a66-ba2f-f64d182752ed" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Reflection in the line $x=3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8054/ma-source-field/53c7ddf8ddc00b934ee89e0216bf262db4f3527c9c107dac538ec3d7bd02e0ee/e821bdfd2f36e3147f802b5ce06cca9441eae2e2c01e830461fa25d5c9d2dc5a" :answer/id #uuid "c2e9ced4-a3e4-50e4-8475-6ffa71f360f3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Reflection in the line $y=3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8054/ma-source-field/53c7ddf8ddc00b934ee89e0216bf262db4f3527c9c107dac538ec3d7bd02e0ee" :answer-field/id #uuid "daffb22d-4d43-548d-b3e0-44a4cfce0727" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-8054/ma-source-field/53c7ddf8ddc00b934ee89e0216bf262db4f3527c9c107dac538ec3d7bd02e0ee/a868feefac40bb7b0111347167c383122fd4a9aadbd951f54e5afb18f41996b4" "q-8054/ma-source-field/53c7ddf8ddc00b934ee89e0216bf262db4f3527c9c107dac538ec3d7bd02e0ee/45b3f3a947a62cbb84343e51a596f8f94e1255e046e3dfde9740d1e89c324c95" "q-8054/ma-source-field/53c7ddf8ddc00b934ee89e0216bf262db4f3527c9c107dac538ec3d7bd02e0ee/83351679bef40cdde3e69e55c2c6f08222a317ed82557f1e3ec0abdce5a513f4" "q-8054/ma-source-field/53c7ddf8ddc00b934ee89e0216bf262db4f3527c9c107dac538ec3d7bd02e0ee/b3dd010b5de3347aa8363384dfcef5a2cbe8f7a1fa63e51d63e92f25d9459b76" "q-8054/ma-source-field/53c7ddf8ddc00b934ee89e0216bf262db4f3527c9c107dac538ec3d7bd02e0ee/e821bdfd2f36e3147f802b5ce06cca9441eae2e2c01e830461fa25d5c9d2dc5a"] :answer-field/correct "q-8054/ma-source-field/53c7ddf8ddc00b934ee89e0216bf262db4f3527c9c107dac538ec3d7bd02e0ee/a868feefac40bb7b0111347167c383122fd4a9aadbd951f54e5afb18f41996b4" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-8054" :question/id #uuid "3ddcb294-a508-54d0-bd15-63145db8f082" :question/math-academy-id "q-8054" :question/problem "What linear transformation $T$ is represented by the matrix $T=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a dilation of scale factor $k$ is represented by the matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nHere, we have $k=3.$ Therefore, the matrix represents a dilation with a scale factor of $3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/ea