426585301d27ed/53b1f84dcf10761a401cb01c88a4bb24fff5835471e7b5fb580b1c37e60e8035"] :answer-field/correct "q-183765/ma-source-field/d3bbe598efa9ab318f5b41bbab14ed79b6d66ef5ea54bf66c2426585301d27ed/9a407ed61fd36c140de8ee053b7c6ff1ce616fd9af5cbbd1ba28c020ed5ee381" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-183765" :question/id #uuid "f1d88cc5-5f34-51c6-bb45-73abd209e524" :question/math-academy-id "q-183765" :question/problem "Describe the set $S={...,3,6,9,12,15,...}$ using a constructive definition.\n\n*Hint: Take ${a}_{1}=3$ in the sequence that generates the elements of $S.$*\n\n$$\nS={ {{field-1}}\\,:\\,n {{field-2}} }\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the elements of our set\n\n$$\n…,\\,3,\\,6,\\,9,\\,12,\\,15,\\,…\n$$\n\nform a two-way infinite arithmetic sequence with common difference $d=3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =3 \\\\  & =6-3 \\\\  & =9-6 \\\\  & =12-9 \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting  ${a}_{1}=3,$ the $n$th term ${a}_{n}$ of our sequence for $n\\in Z$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)\\cdot d \\\\  & =3+(n-1)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =3+3n-3 \\\\  & =3n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can define our set using a constructive definition as follows:\n\n$$\nS={3n\\,:\\,n\\in Z}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-183765/ma-source-field/22e6221ba40cf933e3f5fb01c46af1dab8d914fb0fec2f7e2b6555bf56ac100e" "q-183765/ma-source-field/d3bbe598efa9ab318f5b41bbab14ed79b6d66ef5ea54bf66c2426585301d27ed"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c5b3eb6-187f-5f16-a32e-66b0842adfe9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-183765"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-183770/ma-source-field/9d63554e8e7c2d4dac7df4064a85df14412b5122cd1d26d0e5dba9f23a0756b1/037846d5861ae6e4523198fb5e398d3d2640f3a30c9f4c1ea3c7bd8a5df66372" :answer/id #uuid "4bd5cf80-3e0e-5fd7-9676-437495032f16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2n-1" :db/ensure [: