rm ${a}_{n}$ of our sequence for $n\\in Z$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)\\cdot d \\\\  & =-5+(n-1)\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-5+4n-4 \\\\  & =4n-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can define our set using a constructive definition as follows:\n\n$$\nS={4n-9\\,:\\,n\\in Z}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-183770/ma-source-field/9d63554e8e7c2d4dac7df4064a85df14412b5122cd1d26d0e5dba9f23a0756b1" "q-183770/ma-source-field/059cbd4743438a71b2498d0db149b5967765da25a6867718d8ad78fc0672fc36"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c5b3eb6-187f-5f16-a32e-66b0842adfe9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-183770"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-183771/ma-source-field/f7eda4f88152d39b8fac62d9ede53dad22117d327da44dbde799b38aeb1c953e/c96efb1797cf9881776946044b4b7b3704db7ca5d6e094c26c51a103dc6f643f" :answer/id #uuid "732edcb4-4e31-5d86-b075-68edffdf6963" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-2)^{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183771/ma-source-field/f7eda4f88152d39b8fac62d9ede53dad22117d327da44dbde799b38aeb1c953e/271a59677fb6ef5397de7bbc832169d0f8f571ac2e82b97053c9379e1c21e68a" :answer/id #uuid "04884edb-26ab-5691-9276-5a39738b7de0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1\\cdot {2}^{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183771/ma-source-field/f7eda4f88152d39b8fac62d9ede53dad22117d327da44dbde799b38aeb1c953e/b13fc4f593da59d7c9e30d20ffdcc832c6275279d834330d42708c3a88b8c1c9" :answer/id #uuid "8f61797a-9b84-55c2-bfde-709089f59a51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183771/ma-source-field/f7eda4f88152d39b8fac62d9ede53dad22117d327da44dbde799b38aeb1c953e/ec9f783b4818056c67fa5d6f74c04a1e69e9d9fb781222ab12e733926dfa64fb" :answer/id #uuid "d360ed39-2b76-51e2-859d-ae7636a79a4a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{2}^{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]