e/text :answer/value "the transitive property" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334685/ma-source-field/4963854d5738bb7dd0ab55444b5272c502bab51af75df875ffdb88e8b95f14cd" :answer-field/id #uuid "869f87d8-d462-5ef0-919e-8c5fd622fb0b" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/choices ["q-334685/ma-source-field/4963854d5738bb7dd0ab55444b5272c502bab51af75df875ffdb88e8b95f14cd/3fbc166f0ca82f98a387364d8e9c36034073c6b33cb86f09819bccc9f55bb35c" "q-334685/ma-source-field/4963854d5738bb7dd0ab55444b5272c502bab51af75df875ffdb88e8b95f14cd/438b4c4d03a21de630e66c77197769846fa4a0ad2f925cfdb3df140268e70810" "q-334685/ma-source-field/4963854d5738bb7dd0ab55444b5272c502bab51af75df875ffdb88e8b95f14cd/cc545c04e2dcad28fd649be5b590cd32108605dca0f2f8781f99422c4ab67505" "q-334685/ma-source-field/4963854d5738bb7dd0ab55444b5272c502bab51af75df875ffdb88e8b95f14cd/747bf59f129b39ed16d0609e880083b7ec7fa22b98988114d7cffd9bba5b175a" "q-334685/ma-source-field/4963854d5738bb7dd0ab55444b5272c502bab51af75df875ffdb88e8b95f14cd/8fd8091ad80f7d2511ea6ab5fad6d1dd366029d679ddf5d03fdce7b5b86d2f68"] :answer-field/correct "q-334685/ma-source-field/4963854d5738bb7dd0ab55444b5272c502bab51af75df875ffdb88e8b95f14cd/438b4c4d03a21de630e66c77197769846fa4a0ad2f925cfdb3df140268e70810" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "189a55f5-72ee-590d-b213-1f6bb96fbc77"] :question/problem "Consider the following statement. \n\nIf $f(x)=3{e}^{2x}+2x,$ then $f=O({e}^{2x})$ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nA proof of the statement is given below\n\n $\\text{L1}:\\,f=O(3{e}^{2x}+2x)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(\\frac{2x}{3{e}^{2x}})=0$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,2x=O(3{e}^{2x})$ \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,f=O(3{e}^{2x})$  \n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,f=O({e}^{2x})$ \n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L1}$ follows from {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from lines \n{{field-2}} and \n{{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from line {{field-4}}  and \n{{field-5}}." :question/worked-solution "Suppose $f(x),g(x),h(x)$ and $k(x)$ are functions and $c$ is a nonzero constant. Then, we have the following properties of Big-O notation. \n\n- The sum and product properties. If\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(k)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\n \nthen\n\n$$\nf+g=O(h+k)\\,\\text{and}\\,fg=O(hk)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The constant multiple property. If \n\n$$\nf=O(cg)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\n \nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(g)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The reflexive property. \n\n$$\nf=O(f)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\n- The transitive property. If \n\n$$\nf=O(g)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The absorption property. If\n\n$$\nf=O(g+h)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\n \nthen \n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider line $\\text{L1},$ which states that\n\n$$\nf=O({{3{e}^{2x}+2x}_{⏟}}_{f})\n$$\n\nand this is true by $\\text{the reflexive property}.$\n\n- Next, we consider line $\\text{L4}.$ From line $\\text{L1},$ we have\n\n$$\nf=O(3{e}^{2x}+2x)\n$$\n\nand from line $\\text{L3},$ we have\n\n$$\n2x=O(3{e}^{2x}).\n$$\n\nThus, by lines $\\text{L1 and L3}$ and the $\\text{absorption property},$ we have \n\n$$\nf=O(3{e}^{2x}+2x)=O(3{e}^{2x}).\n$$\n\n- Finally, we consider line $\\text{L5}.$ From line $\\text{L4},$ we have\n\n$$\nf=O(3{e}^{2x})\n$$\n\nand by the $\\text{constant multiple property}$ with $c=3,$ we have\n\n$$\nf=O({e}^{2x}).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-334685/ma-source-field/8b1cea60124f7907edeaaa488e8258e3b70ebf1aca2f1f655e978ff6050fa208" "q-334685/ma-source-field/76272c68fb509289c41a825b269170163ae0303f5b490f466ab948ec68089645" "q-334685/ma-source-field/42d0b6fef1f1aaa0a59f05f6ccd1027dae593b1a8f3c849e15739680a4a7b745" "q-3346