wer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334709/ma-source-field/f1352c8ac06359b7141cc14082fb068e6b4c7cfb08d7cb95f1f78029cd58cad5" :answer-field/id #uuid "027eda39-8180-548c-9212-c37a8b75ea4d" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/choices ["q-334709/ma-source-field/f1352c8ac06359b7141cc14082fb068e6b4c7cfb08d7cb95f1f78029cd58cad5/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-334709/ma-source-field/f1352c8ac06359b7141cc14082fb068e6b4c7cfb08d7cb95f1f78029cd58cad5/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-334709/ma-source-field/f1352c8ac06359b7141cc14082fb068e6b4c7cfb08d7cb95f1f78029cd58cad5/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-334709/ma-source-field/f1352c8ac06359b7141cc14082fb068e6b4c7cfb08d7cb95f1f78029cd58cad5/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-334709/ma-source-field/f1352c8ac06359b7141cc14082fb068e6b4c7cfb08d7cb95f1f78029cd58cad5/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :answer-field/correct "q-334709/ma-source-field/f1352c8ac06359b7141cc14082fb068e6b4c7cfb08d7cb95f1f78029cd58cad5/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-334709" :question/id #uuid "b4af4f8d-8886-57f9-92e8-20fda99f6128" :question/math-academy-id "q-334709" :question/problem "The local truncation error (LTE) of a numerical method with step size $Δx$ is\n\n$$\nτ(Δx)=4(Δx)^{3}-(Δx)^{4}.\n$$\n\nComplete the following sentences.$\\,$ With step size $Δx=0.3,$ the local truncation error is $≈$\n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ With step size $Δx=0.1,$ the local truncation error is $≈$\n{{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Decreasing from $Δx=0.3$ to $Δx=0.1,$ the LTE is reduced by a factor of $≈$\n{{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ According to this data, the order of the method is approximately\n{{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "A numerical method has order $p$ if $p$ is the largest positive integer such that the local truncation error (LTE) satisfies\n\n$$\nτ(Δx)=O\\,((Δx)^{p+1})\\,\\text{as}\\,Δx\\to 0.\n$$\n\nThe order describes how fast errors shrink as $Δx$ decreases.\n\nIn other words, a numerical method has order $p$ if, for sufficiently small step sizes, reducing the step size by a factor of $k$ reduces the LTE by a factor of approximately ${k}^{p+1}.$\n\nFirst, we compute the LTE for the given step sizes:\n\n- With step size $Δx=0.3,$ the LTE is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}τ(0.3) & =4(0.3)^{3}-(0.3)^{4} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 0.027-0.008\\,1 \\\\  & =0.108-0.008\\,1 \\\\  & =0.099\\,9 \\\\  & ≈0.100.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- With step size $Δx=0.1,$ the LTE is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}τ(0.1) & =4(0.1)^{3}-(0.1)^{4} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 0.001-0.000\\,1 \\\\  & =0.004-0.000\\,1 \\\\  & =0.003\\,9 \\\\  & ≈0.004.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we determine the order by comparing the errors. The step size decreases from $0.3$ to $0.1.$ So, it reduces by a factor of\n\n$$\nk=\\frac{0.3}{0.1}=3.\n$$\n\nAs a result, for a numerical method of order $p,$ the LTE should decrease by a factor of approximately\n\n$$\n{k}^{p+1}={3}^{p+1}.\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, the LTE actually decreases from $0.099\\,9$ to $0.003\\,9.$ So, it reduces by a factor of\n\n$$\n\\frac{0.099\\,9}{0.003\\,9}=25.615\\,38…≈25.615.\n$$\n\nComparing the two scale factors for the LTE, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{3}^{p+1} & ≈25.615\\,38… \\\\ p+1 & ≈{log}_{3}⁡(25.615\\,38…) \\\\ p+1 & ≈2.952… \\\\ p & ≈1.952….\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, rounding to the nearest integer, the estimated order of the method is\n$2.$\n\nIndeed, this coincides with the definition of the order from the expression for the LTE:\n\n$$\nτ(Δx)=4(Δx)^{3}-(Δx)^{4}\\,⇒\\,τ(Δx)=O\\,((Δx)^{3})=O\\,((Δx)^{2+1}),\\,Δx\\to 0.\n$$\n\nHence, the order of the method is $2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-334709/ma-source-field/af89b9cee1e8a74ebe5bab22565f63d0a9a8e4b48292848242ed03d4f9a7d096" "q-334709/ma-source-field/92ad7e89d294eb0dfa4715d5374bc70684e2fd05ac3507300e3d90e4a192cf70" "q-334709/ma-source-field/378521bb698e55099ec9027136ff945fb1c6e7511a5b425b214980a0c6b7bc76" "q-334709/ma-source-field/f1352c8ac06359b7141cc14082fb068e6b4c7cfb08d7cb95f1f78029cd58cad5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "42c41150-5104-58cc-927b-f55b94529cb2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-334709"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-334710/ma-source-field/5f8579eb6bc698969b5742be8d4c4aabd68c07de1e713258dea3f972241a8513/1c3749c3cd74b1bfc2266a575b44a558f14ce2e9c18402bcc68e3a99d24a4157" :answer/id #uuid "17cc96c1-7c53-5909-a9eb-4804b7e498d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.057" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334710/ma-source-field/5f8579eb6bc698969b5742be8d4c4aabd68c07de1e713258dea3f972241a8513/be2996522c88880b85c94a2df96123acadb7ac9f8da34e41793102bb8efe9a83" :answer/id #uuid "cad7653e-3452-5b8d-9ce7-c46d36f9a267" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.075" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334710/ma-source-field/5f8579eb6bc698969b5742be8d4c4aabd68c07de1e713258dea3f972241a8513/b34544a9837d181994c7a132937df1564b327d325fab23b2c613d8bcfe8cb599" :answer/id #uuid "f389774e-2155-5122-83ea-27a9212a7e57" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.375" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334710/ma-source-field/5f8579eb6bc698969b5742be8d4c4aabd68c07de1e713258dea3f972241a8513/961991a7f93b751281fcba76338cc9ff87be02987f655e77f53c85797d18537d" :answer/id #uuid "2eb02a74-9fae-5992-999d-2d580bdb32f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.420" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334710/ma-source-field/5f8579eb6bc698969b5742be8d4c4aabd68c07de1e713258dea3f972241a8513/c01be69fe812f7cb27bf7043bbb0bc85bda5ba8878dfb5ae47287b7fc571ee81" :answer/id #uuid "78583d61-1a17-5f4f-be43-b20d831cfe8a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :a