d "5d1825a3-5ffb-52b1-8b17-c6fa1547fd34" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "increases" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335040/ma-source-field/7853b8390a1a88650c3e796b3b588e4d720d0f60da4868b2747077857d94c9a9" :answer-field/id #uuid "80014b96-58a1-540f-b4b9-40b8251a49a0" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/choices ["q-335040/ma-source-field/7853b8390a1a88650c3e796b3b588e4d720d0f60da4868b2747077857d94c9a9/349b5e74e9c4e10760a76b9d32e42f4bfc15459d46e647ef0a728c0a0f85924d" "q-335040/ma-source-field/7853b8390a1a88650c3e796b3b588e4d720d0f60da4868b2747077857d94c9a9/3ed515d894ca9eab0c4ba27f94e6d07f7ea399773bb6725db5f3ea80887fb921"] :answer-field/correct "q-335040/ma-source-field/7853b8390a1a88650c3e796b3b588e4d720d0f60da4868b2747077857d94c9a9/349b5e74e9c4e10760a76b9d32e42f4bfc15459d46e647ef0a728c0a0f85924d" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "d4850b2b-4a19-5e29-aed4-55be99e7b3ed"] :question/problem "![](images/35/359b56411d4e215ef0ed423f6280a9e3641d5806d525b78e97569aaa02afe72f.png)\n\nConsider the phase portrait above showing a solution of a Lotka-Volterra predator-prey model\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}=8x-4xy \\\\ {y}^{′}=-6y+2xy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $x=x(t),y=y(t),$ and $a,b,c,$ and $d$ are positive constants.\n\nSelect the options below that best describe the dynamics of the system from point $A$ to point $B$ on the solution.\n\n$\\,$\nThe trajectory \n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$\nThe number of prey {{field-3}} and the number of predators {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "The Lotka-Volterra predator-prey model is given by\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}=ax-bxy \\\\ {y}^{′}=-cy+dxy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $a,b,c,d$ are positive real constants. Here, $x=x(t)$ represents the prey and $y=y(t)$ represents the predators.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the statements:\n\n- The trajectory $\\text{circles around}$ $\\text{the nonzero equilibrium}.$\n\n- From $A$ to $B,$ the number of prey $\\text{decreases}$ and the number of predators $\\text{decreases}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-335040/ma-source-field/1954c5a9e180875845c7923ed4d8e82ab452802753fd1e493997117a469351b9" "q-335040/ma-source-field/51e1245cdbc9aba2961c796fb316bb4ab7eeea8abada7aaadb90912b6889e6cb" "q-335040/ma-source-field/417b69673af4a2919ebcf6797291a1c663464cfcb9f0f9e926bb1f1a6aba8ba5" "q-335040/ma-source-field/7853b8390a1a88650c3e796b3b588e4d720d0f60da4868b2747077857d94c9a9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-335099/ma-source-field/47a12c9ca9860f00431ea7794eebb7aee42c39ce86717eb7b8e965d491d1bad8/9b34ae2fb0d4fe43e893c2343f4f1902b65505b6065de7d021454c118291ae7d" :answer/id #uuid "d480a481-e03a-5469-92c4-5278b1f7fdc7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ \\pi  & 0\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335099/ma-source-field/47a12c9ca9860f00431ea7794eebb7aee42c39ce86717eb7b8e965d491d1bad8/a5cdea5168ae9bb2eb7863f2eedecc59eb80fc3e5f31e5d967a1e9a00bcca67a" :answer/id #uuid "36e273ce-dbcd-5625-b775-6f6dcaa90c70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}-\\pi  & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335099/ma-source-field/47a12c9ca9860f00431ea7794eebb7aee42c39ce86717eb7b8e965d491d1bad8/3f7816fd71273d337e9a1521c8cff1490a12cb25e2417b1d94d9c47d33d2c388" :answer/id #uuid "0095bbe3-9652-5054-b2e6-b54c94a109af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335099/ma-source-field/47a12c9ca9860f00431ea7794eebb7aee42c39ce86717eb7b8e965d491d1bad8/efec29e504478a62a1059f69c8cbf47c66c999c4107cba56da639444690de4ec" :answer/id #uuid "e50c9797-8311-56db-9e8e-13eb031dd8db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}0 & \\pi  \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335099/ma-source-field/47a12c9ca9860f00431ea7794eebb7aee42c39ce86717eb7b8e965d491d1bad8" :answer-field/id #uuid "15699797-263d-5146-820d-3a7ce8d5cda0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/choices ["q-335099/ma-source-field/47a12c9ca9860f00431ea7794eebb7aee42c39ce86717eb7b8e965d491d1bad8/9b34ae2fb0d4fe43e893c2343f4f1902b65505b6065de7d021454c118291ae7d" "q-335099/ma-source-field/47a12c9ca9860f00431ea7794eebb7aee42c39ce86717eb7b8e965d491d1bad8/a5cdea5168ae9bb2eb7863f2eedecc59eb80fc3e5f31e5d967a1e9a00bcca67a" "q-335099/ma-source-field/47a12c9ca9860f00431ea7794eebb7aee42c39ce86717eb7b8e965d491d1bad8/3f7816fd71273d337e9a1521c8cff1490a12cb25e2417b1d94d9c47d33d2c388" "q-335099/ma-source-field/47a12c9ca9860f00431ea7794eebb7aee42c39ce86717eb7b8e965d491d1bad8/efec29e504478a62a1059f69c8cbf47c66c999c4107cba56da639444690de4ec"] :answer-field/correct "q-335099/ma-source-field/47a12c9ca9860f00431ea7794eebb7aee42c39ce86717eb7b8e965d491d1bad8/9b34ae2fb0d4fe43e893c2343f4f1902b65505b6065de7d021454c118291ae7d" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335099/ma-source-field/ea7d458f570b3b7419d42f6aea214d294025de28aad1c7641d5b0a9b78b84b6b/34072c330c1ddc31e1283826e1f63061acb37fc99b4c3bad85fac5f4064d536d" :answer/id #uuid "8b39ab91-1fd9-505d-8a6f-a0eae97c2dcc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "almost linear" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335099/ma-source-field/ea7d458f570b3b7419d42f6aea214d294025de28aad1c7641d5b0a9b78b84b6b/ffd3fd1ca243376069911a691e58f6223828faabc24fa921dc3d5f5adf98a658" :answer/id #uuid "66231965-9438-53a7-8707-d460c9b3ab3c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "not almost linear" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335099/ma-source-field/ea7d458f570b3b7419d42f6aea214d294025de28aad1c7641d5b0a9b78b84b6b" :answer-field/id #uuid "f3f0af58-6ec9-52a4-a9b1-c5ea22e61b52" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/choices ["q-335099/ma-source-field/ea7d458f570b3b7419d42f6aea214d294025de28aad1c7641d5b0a9b78b84b6b/34072c330c1ddc31e1283826e1f63061acb37fc99b4c3bad85fac5f4064d536d" "q-335099/ma-source-field/ea7d458f570b3b7419d42f6aea214d294025de28aad1c7641d5b0a9b78b84b6b/ffd3fd1ca243376069911a691e58f6223828faabc24fa921dc3d5f5adf98a658"] :answer-field/correct "q-335099/ma-source-field/ea7d458f570b3b7419d42f6aea214d294025de28aad1c7641d5b0a9b78b84b6b/ffd3fd1ca243376069911a691e58f6223828faabc24fa921dc3d5f5adf98a658" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335099" :question/id #uuid "f2c782c5-e338-5c8a-884e-7da2e7513b5c" :question/math-academy-id "q-335099" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=x(t)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi y(t)) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=y(t)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x(t))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven the system of differential equations, select the correct options below.The Jacobian determinant of the system at the equilibrium point ${x}^{∗}=[0,\\text{ }1]^{T}$ is given as\n\n$$\nJ(0,1)={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nAt this point, the system is \n{{field-2}}\nat ${x}^{∗}.$" :question/worked-solution "The system can be rewritten in matrix form as \n\n$$\n{x}^{′}=\\text{\\boldsymbol}f(x)\n$$\n\nwhere $x=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]$ and \n$\\text{\\boldsymbol}f(x)=[\\begin{aligned}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi y) \\\\ y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)\\end{aligned}].$\n\nWe need to compute the Jacobian determinant of $\\text{\\boldsymbol}f(x).$ \n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\nJ=|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y}\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi y))=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi y),\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi y))=-\\pi x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi y) \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x))=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x),\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x))=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we have\n\n$$\nJ=|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi y) & -\\pi x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi y) \\\\ \\pi y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the Jacobian at the equilibrium ${x}^{∗}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}J(0,1) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi (1)) & -\\pi (0)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi (1)) \\\\ \\pi (1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi (0)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi (0))\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ \\pi  & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot 0-0\\cdot \\pi  \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the Jacobian determinant is zero, our system is $\\text{not almost linear}$ at ${x}^{∗}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-335099/ma-source-field/47a12c9ca9860f00431ea7794eebb7aee42c39ce86717eb7b8e965d491d1bad8" "q-335099/ma-source-field/ea7d458f570b3b7419d42f6aea214d294025de28aad1c7641d5b0a9b78b84b6b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd9680fc-dfa9-5411-aeca-81659b7dec8a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335099"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335175/ma-source-field/8fae108f3e935b7e68df0c0b2a727d0adb5c67fc7500ab531155943de1f1352c/d11bfd3158fce0fc342975419f4ee21d63da18471b3cb7fb5c76fec1a8fa792f" :answer/id #uuid "875915a9-2dd7-5bfd-a876-9d427aa8a55b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335175/ma-source-field/8fae108f3e935b7e68df0c0b2a727d0adb5c67fc7500ab531155943de1f1352c/917d89dc43b3893a59f109615d78fa9fb8ef456a7c3e67407c6e429dc0b8206a" :answer/id #uuid "96de3917-2210-5111-9750-f9437e72cfa5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335175/ma-source-field/8fae108f3e935b7e68df0c0b2a727d0adb5c67fc7500ab531155943de1f1352c/ec7d8b659bd5b9217c6515e9573996a36a733ef30f4ac941ae605c65ceeb876a" :answer/id #uuid "ba2a0cc9-e777-59ad-9b3f-6332bbbb90e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t)+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335175/ma-source-field/8fae108f3e935b7e68df0c0b2a727d0adb5c67fc7500ab531155943de1f1352c/372db0ebaae3c35b8644b394c9ccc88cbf11adb28d473148aacbf2fc5f750c4b" :answer/id #uuid "445c6a63-f339-5ff2-afa4-e26785fbf1f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t)-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335175/ma-source-field/8fae108f3e935b7e68df0c0b2a727d0adb5c67fc7500ab531155943de1f1352c" :answer-field/id #uuid "7e1c7d9a-e955-5ffd-bbe8-c5635e09bdc8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/choices ["q-335175/ma-source-field/8fae108f3e935b7e68df0c0b2a727d0adb5c67fc7500ab531155943de1f1352c/d11bfd3158fce0fc342975419f4ee21d63da18471b3cb7fb5c76fec1a8fa792f" "q-335175/ma-source-field/8fae108f3e935b7e68df0c0b2a727d0adb5c67fc7500ab531155943de1f1352c/917d89dc43b3893a59f109615d78fa9fb8ef456a7c3e67407c6e429dc0b8206a" "q-335175/ma-source-field/8fae108f3e935b7e68df0c0b2a727d0adb5c67fc7500ab531155943de1f1352c/ec7d8b659bd5b9217c6515e9573996a36a733ef30f4ac941ae605c65ceeb876a" "q-335175/ma-source-field/8fae108f3e935b7e68df0c0b2a727d0adb5c67fc7500ab531155943de1f1352c/372db0ebaae3c35b8644b394c9ccc88cbf11adb28d473148aacbf2fc5f750c4b"] :answer-field/correct "q-335175/ma-source-field/8fae108f3e935b7e68df0c0b2a727d0adb5c67fc7500ab531155943de1f1352c/917d89dc43b3893a59f109615d78fa9fb8ef456a7c3e67407c6e429dc0b8206a" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335175" :question/id #uuid "d2b8ad61-9b47-5971-9495-e31b2ea4691b" :question/math-academy-id "q-335175" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=2y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=2x(t)+2,\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n| $[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t)$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]$ and $g(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})} & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{aligned}]}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-335175/ma-source-field/8fae108f3e935b7e68df0c0b2a727d0adb5c67fc7500ab531155943de1f1352c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4eca32dd-1563-55c6-b594-08588efd601b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335175"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
